e.\\n\\n\u201cEver yours, \u201cWILLIAM LEGRAND\u201d.\\n\\nThere was something in the tone of this note that caused me great uneasiness. Its entire style differed markedly from Legrand\u2019s. What could he be dreaming about? What new obsession had taken hold of his excitable mind? What \u201cbusiness of the highest importance\u201d could he possibly have to conduct? Jupiter\u2019s account of him suggested nothing good. I feared that the continued pressure of misfortune had finally disturbed my friend\u2019s reason. Without the slightest hesitation, therefore, I prepared to accompany the Black man.\\n\\nWhen we reached the wharf, I noticed a scythe and three spades, all apparently new, lying in the bottom of the boat in which we were to cross.\\n\\n\u201cWhat does all this mean, Jup?\u201d\"}"
