e most extraordinary behavior! I can explain it in only one way: you are not yourself. Otherwise, you could not speak either to me or about Harriet in this manner. Control yourself enough to say no more, and I will try to forget it.\u201d\\n\\nBut Mr. Elton had drunk only enough wine to raise his spirits, not enough to cloud his judgment. He knew perfectly well what he meant. After warmly protesting that her suspicion was deeply insulting, and briefly mentioning his respect for Miss Smith as her friend\u2014but admitting that he was surprised she had been mentioned at all\u2014he returned to the subject of his own passion and pressed her urgently for a favorable answer.\"}"
