          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"a7a35af863d5146424f8b8f1\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Tom managed to scratch up the cupboard with it and was about to start on the bureau when he was called away to dress for Sunday school.\\n\\nMary gave him a tin basin of water and a piece of soap. He carried them outside the door and set the basin on a small bench. Then he dipped the soap in the water, put it down, rolled up his sleeves, gently poured the water onto the ground, and went back into the kitchen. There he began carefully wiping his face with the towel behind the door. But Mary took the towel away and said:\\n\\n\u201cNow aren\u2019t you ashamed, Tom? You mustn\u2019t be so naughty. Water won\u2019t hurt you.\u201d\\n\\nTom was a little unsettled. The basin was filled again, and this time he stood over it for a while, gathering his courage. He took a deep breath and began. When he soon came back into the kitchen, both eyes shut and feeling around for the towel, soap and water were dripping honestly from his face. But after he dried himself, he still was not clean enough. The clean part ended at his chin and along his jaws, like a mask; below it, and around the back of his neck, was a wide stretch of untouched dark skin. Mary took charge, and when she finished, he was clean all over, with no difference in color. His wet hair was neatly brushed, its short curls arranged in a delicate, even shape. [In private, he painfully and laboriously smoothed the curls out and plastered his hair flat against his head, because he thought curls were feminine, and his own made him miserable.] Then Mary brought out a suit of clothes he had worn only on Sundays for two years. They were simply called his \u201cother clothes,\u201d which showed how small his wardrobe was. After he dressed, the girl \u201cput him to rights\u201d: she buttoned his tidy roundabout up to his chin, folded his huge shirt collar over his shoulders, brushed him off, and topped him with his speckled straw hat. He now looked much better\u2014and very uncomfortable. He felt just as uncomfortable as he looked, because wearing a complete outfit and being clean made him feel trapped. He hoped Mary would forget his shoes, but that hope failed. As usual, she covered them thoroughly with tallow and brought them out. He lost his temper and said he was always being forced to do everything he did not want to do.\"}"
