l scenery, view fine paintings, or sometimes simply seek whatever amusement happened to arise, I was always happy when I was near my father. I regretted whenever a third person joined us, yet if I turned toward my father with a troubled expression, his eyes would meet mine, shining with tenderness, and instantly restore joy to my heart. O, hours of intense delight! Brief as you were, memory has made you seem as long as an entire life, when I look back through the veil of grief that rose immediately afterward, as if to hide you from my sight.\"}"
