{"request_id":"d028eaaa6fd9ff9ea79cf371","rewritten_text":"As I reached my hand through the valve with a cup of water for the old cat, my shirt sleeves caught on the loop holding up the basket and, in an instant, pulled it loose from the bottom. If the whole thing had vanished into thin air, it could not have disappeared from my sight more suddenly. Truly, not even a tenth of a second passed between the basket coming free and its complete disappearance, along with everything inside it. My good wishes followed it toward the earth, but naturally I had no hope that the cat or kittens would survive to tell of their misfortune.

“At six o’clock, I saw a large part of the earth’s visible surface to the east covered in deep shadow. The darkness advanced very quickly, until, at five minutes before seven, the entire view was wrapped in night. Yet the setting sun continued to light the balloon long afterward. Though I had expected this, it still gave me immense pleasure. Clearly, in the morning I would see the sun rise at least several hours before the people of Rotterdam, despite their being much farther east. Thus, day after day, as my height increased, I would enjoy sunlight for longer and longer periods. I now decided to keep a journal of my journey, counting each day as twenty-four continuous hours, without considering the periods of darkness.

“At ten o’clock, feeling sleepy, I decided to lie down for the rest of the night. But then I faced a problem that, obvious as it may seem, had escaped me until that very moment. If I went to sleep as planned, how could the air in the chamber be renewed while I slept? I could not breathe it for more than an hour at most; and even if that time could be extended to an hour and a quarter, the consequences might be disastrous. This dilemma troubled me greatly. It may be hard to believe that, after all the dangers I had faced, I took the matter so seriously that I abandoned hope of completing my ultimate plan and finally decided that I must descend. But this hesitation lasted only a moment."}

