          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"61fac217d9f6d1069b013557\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cCertainly not,\u201d Duff answered.\\n\\n\u201cAnd, translating the word yokel for the ladies\u2019 benefit, I take your meaning to be that this attempt was not made by a countryman?\u201d said Mr. Losberne, smiling.\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s right, master,\u201d replied Blathers. \u201cThis is all concerning the robbery, is it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAll of it,\u201d said the doctor.\\n\\n\u201cNow, what\u2019s this about the boy the servants are talking of?\u201d Blathers asked.\\n\\n\u201cNothing whatsoever,\u201d replied the doctor. \u201cOne of the terrified servants took it into his head that he had something to do with this attempt to enter the house; but it\u2019s nonsense\u2014sheer absurdity.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cVery easily settled, if that\u2019s so,\u201d remarked Duff.\\n\\n\u201cWhat he says is perfectly correct,\u201d observed Blathers, nodding in confirmation and idly rattling the handcuffs as though they were castanets. \u201cWho is the boy? What story does he tell about himself? Where did he come from? He didn\u2019t fall out of the clouds, did he, master?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOf course not,\u201d replied the doctor, casting a nervous look at the two ladies. \u201cI know his entire history; but we can discuss that presently. You would like to see first, I suppose, the place where the thieves attempted to enter?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCertainly,\u201d rejoined Mr. Blathers. \u201cWe had best inspect the premises first, and question the servants afterwards. That is the customary way of conducting business.\u201d\\n\\nLights were procured; and Messrs. Blathers and Duff, accompanied by the native constable, Brittles, Giles, and everybody else, in short, entered the little room at the passage\u2019s end and looked out of the window; then went around by the lawn and looked in through it; after that, they had a candle brought out to examine the shutter; and then a lantern with which to follow the footprints; and finally a pitchfork for poking among the bushes. This completed, amid the breathless interest of every spectator, they returned inside; and Mr. Giles and Brittles were put through a melodramatic enactment of their parts in the previous night\u2019s adventures. They performed it about six times, contradicting one another in no more than one important detail the first time, and in no fewer than a dozen by the last. When this was accomplished, Blathers and Duff cleared the room and held a lengthy conference, which, in secrecy and solemnity, made a consultation of eminent doctors over the most difficult medical question seem mere child\u2019s play.\\n\\nMeanwhile, the doctor paced the adjoining room in a state of great uneasiness; while Mrs. Maylie and Rose watched him with anxious faces.\\n\\n\u201cUpon my word,\u201d he said, stopping after a great many very rapid turns, \u201cI scarcely know what to do.\u201d\"}"
