          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"76623a9ccf7908089b7694b6\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cStop the starboard! Ting-a-ling-ling! Stop the larboard! Come ahead on the starboard! Stop her! Let your outside turn over slowly! Ting-a-ling-ling! Chow-ow-ow! Get that head-line out! _Lively_ now! Come\u2014out with your spring-line\u2014what are you about there! Take a turn around that stump with its bight! Stand by that stage, now\u2014let her go! Engines done, sir! Ting-a-ling-ling! SH\u2019T! S\u2019H\u2019T! SH\u2019T!\u201d (testing the gauge-cocks).\\n\\nTom kept whitewashing, paying no heed to the steamboat. Ben stared for a moment, then called: \u201c_Hi-Yi! You\u2019re_ up a stump, ain\u2019t you!\u201d\\n\\nThere was no answer. Tom examined his final stroke with an artist\u2019s eye, then passed his brush over it gently once more and inspected the result as before. Ben came alongside him. Tom\u2019s mouth watered at the apple, but he continued working. Ben said:\\n\\n\u201cHello, old fellow, you\u2019ve got to work, hey?\u201d\\n\\nTom turned sharply and said:\\n\\n\u201cWhy, it\u2019s you, Ben! I wasn\u2019t noticing.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSay\u2014I\u2019m going swimming, I am. Don\u2019t you wish you could? But naturally you\u2019d rather _work_\u2014wouldn\u2019t you? Of course you would!\u201d\\n\\nTom studied the boy for a little while, then said:\\n\\n\u201cWhat do you call work?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, isn\u2019t _that_ work?\u201d\\n\\nTom went back to whitewashing and replied indifferently:\\n\\n\u201cWell, perhaps it is, and perhaps it isn\u2019t. All I know is, it suits Tom Sawyer.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, come now, you don\u2019t mean to pretend that you _like_ it?\u201d\\n\\nThe brush kept moving.\\n\\n\u201cLike it? Well, I don\u2019t see why I shouldn\u2019t. Does a boy get the chance to whitewash a fence every day?\u201d\\n\\nThat made the matter appear differently. Ben stopped nibbling his apple. Tom moved his brush delicately back and forth, stepped away to judge the effect, added a little here and there, and criticized the result again. Ben watched each motion, growing more interested and absorbed all the while. Presently he said:\\n\\n\u201cSay, Tom, let _me_ whitewash a little.\u201d\\n\\nTom thought it over and was about to agree, but changed his mind:\\n\\n\u201cNo\u2014no\u2014I reckon it wouldn\u2019t quite do, Ben. You see, Aunt Polly is terribly particular about this fence\u2014right here beside the street, you know\u2014but if it were the back fence I wouldn\u2019t care, and _she_ wouldn\u2019t either. Yes, she\u2019s terribly particular about this one; it has to be done very carefully. I reckon there isn\u2019t one boy in a thousand, perhaps two thousand, who can do it as it ought to be done.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo\u2014is that so? Oh, come now\u2014let me just try. Only a little\u2014I\u2019d let _you_, if you were me, Tom.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBen, I\u2019d like to, honest injun; but Aunt Polly\u2014well, Jim wanted to do it, but she wouldn\u2019t let him; Sid wanted to do it, and she wouldn\u2019t let Sid.\u201d\"}"
