ur boy?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, he\u2019s my boy,\u201d Sikes replied, staring hard at Oliver and absently putting his hand into the pocket where he kept the pistol.\\n\\n\u201cYour father walks a little too fast for you, doesn\u2019t he, my lad?\u201d the driver asked, noticing that Oliver was out of breath.\\n\\n\u201cNot at all,\u201d Sikes interrupted. \u201cHe\u2019s used to it. Here, take my hand, Ned. Get in!\u201d\\n\\nSpeaking to Oliver in this way, he helped him into the cart. The driver pointed to a pile of sacks and told him to lie there and rest.\\n\\nAs they passed one milestone after another, Oliver wondered more and more where his companion intended to take him. Kensington, Hammersmith, Chiswick, Kew Bridge, and Brentford all went by, yet they continued as steadily as though their journey had only just begun.\"}"
