          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"0199dd6d6a2088496cf8df3a\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cCertainly not,\u201d Duff replied.\\n\\n\u201cAnd, translating the word yokel for the ladies\u2019 benefit, I take your meaning to be that this attempt was not made by a countryman?\u201d Mr. Losberne asked with a smile.\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s it, sir,\u201d Blathers replied. \u201cThis is all about the robbery, is it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAll of it,\u201d said the doctor.\\n\\n\u201cNow, what\u2019s this about the boy the servants have been talking about?\u201d Blathers asked.\\n\\n\u201cNothing at all,\u201d the doctor replied. \u201cOne of the frightened servants decided he had something to do with this attempt to break into the house; but it\u2019s nonsense\u2014sheer absurdity.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cEasily settled, if that\u2019s so,\u201d Duff remarked.\\n\\n\u201cWhat he says is quite correct,\u201d Blathers observed, nodding in confirmation and idly playing with the handcuffs as though they were castanets. \u201cWho is the boy? What account does he give of himself? Where did he come from? He didn\u2019t fall out of the clouds, did he, sir?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOf course not,\u201d the doctor replied, casting a nervous glance at the two ladies. \u201cI know his entire history; but we can discuss that presently. You would like first to see where the thieves made their attempt, I suppose?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCertainly,\u201d Mr. Blathers answered. \u201cWe had better inspect the premises first and question the servants afterward. That is the usual way of doing things.\u201d\\n\\nLights were then brought; and Messrs. Blathers and Duff, accompanied by the local constable, Brittles, Giles, and everyone else, went into the little room at the end of the passage and looked out the window. They then went around by way of the lawn and looked in through it; after that, they had a candle passed out so they could inspect the shutter, and then a lantern with which to trace the footprints, and finally a pitchfork for poking through the bushes. This completed, amid the breathless interest of all who watched, they returned inside; and Mr. Giles and Brittles were made to act out their parts in the previous night\u2019s adventures. They performed it some six times over, contradicting each other in no more than one important detail the first time, and in no more than a dozen by the last. Once this was accomplished, Blathers and Duff cleared the room and held a lengthy private council, compared with which a consultation of eminent doctors over the most difficult medical problem would have been child\u2019s play in secrecy and solemnity.\\n\\nMeanwhile, the doctor paced the adjoining room in a state of great unease, while Mrs. Maylie and Rose watched with anxious faces.\\n\\n\u201cUpon my word,\u201d he said, stopping after a great many rapid turns, \u201cI hardly know what to do.\u201d\"}"
