nergy until it is needed; your lightning is waiting, ready like a charge in a gun, but it costs you nothing until you fire it. Yes, the single ground connection\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOf course! I don\u2019t know how I missed that. It\u2019s not only cheaper, but more effective than the other arrangement, because if wires break or become tangled, no harm is done.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, especially if we have a warning device in the cave and disconnect the broken wire. Well, go on. The Gatlings?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes\u2014that\u2019s arranged. In the center of the inner circle, on a spacious platform six feet high, I\u2019ve grouped a battery of thirteen Gatling guns and supplied plenty of ammunition.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s it. They command every approach, and when the Church\u2019s knights arrive, there will be music. The edge of the precipice above the cave\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019ve put a wire fence there, and a Gatling.\u201d\"}"
