rried steps when a deep church bell struck the hour. At its first stroke, both guides stopped and turned their heads toward the direction from which the sound came.\\n\\n\u201cEight o\u2019clock, Bill,\u201d said Nancy when the bell fell silent.\\n\\n\u201cWhat\u2019s the use of telling me? I can hear it, can\u2019t I?\u201d Sikes answered.\\n\\n\u201cI wonder whether _they_ can hear it,\u201d said Nancy.\\n\\n\u201cOf course they can,\u201d replied Sikes. \u201cIt was Bartlemy time when I was shopped; and there wasn\u2019t a penny trumpet at the fair whose squeaking I couldn\u2019t hear. After I was locked up for the night, the noise and uproar outside made that thundering old jail so quiet, I could almost have dashed my brains against the iron plates of the door.\u201d\"}"
