          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"83b3eb35b37271aac84cc752\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Winters at the latitude of Sullivan\u2019s Island are rarely very harsh, and in autumn it is unusual for anyone to need a fire. Around the middle of October, 18\u2014, however, there came a remarkably cold day. Just before sunset, I made my way through the evergreens to my friend\u2019s hut, which I had not visited for several weeks. At that time I lived in Charleston, nine miles from the island, and travel between the two places was far more difficult than it is today. When I reached the hut, I knocked as usual. Receiving no answer, I took the key from its hiding place, unlocked the door, and entered. A bright fire was burning on the hearth. It was unexpected, but very welcome. I removed my overcoat, settled into an armchair beside the crackling logs, and patiently waited for my hosts to return.\\n\\nThey arrived soon after dark and welcomed me warmly. Jupiter, grinning from ear to ear, hurried around preparing marsh-hens for supper. Legrand was in one of his fits\u2014what else can I call them?\u2014of excitement. He had discovered an unknown bivalve that formed a new genus. More than that, with Jupiter\u2019s help, he had captured a _scarab\u00e6us_ that he believed was entirely new, and he wanted my opinion about it the next day.\\n\\n\u201cAnd why not tonight?\u201d I asked, warming my hands over the fire and wishing the entire tribe of _scarab\u00e6i_ to the devil.\\n\\n\u201cAh, if only I had known you were here!\u201d Legrand said. \u201cBut it has been so long since I saw you. How could I have guessed that you would visit me tonight, of all nights? On my way home I met Lieutenant G\u2014\u2014 from the fort, and foolishly lent him the beetle. So you cannot see it until morning. Stay here tonight, and I will send Jup for it at sunrise. It is the most beautiful thing in creation!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat? Sunrise?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNonsense! No\u2014the beetle. It is a brilliant gold color, about the size of a large hickory nut, with two jet-black spots near one end of its back and another, slightly longer, at the other. The antennae are\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDey ain\u2019t no tin in him, Massa Will, I keep tellin\u2019 you,\u201d Jupiter interrupted. \u201cDe bug is a goole bug, solid, every bit of him, inside and all, \u2019cept his wing. I never feel half so hebby a bug in my life.\u201d\"}"
