          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"8969c9abfac68869b79ea72f\",\"rewritten_text\":\"When the wedding took place, about three weeks later, St. Peter\u2019s was packed with a crowd of fashionable people. The Dean of Chichester conducted the service most impressively, and everyone agreed that they had never seen a more handsome bride and groom. They were more than handsome, though\u2014they were happy. Lord Arthur never once regretted all he had suffered for Sybil, while she gave him the finest things a woman can give a man: devotion, tenderness, and love. Reality did not destroy their romance. They always felt young.\\n\\nSeveral years later, after they had had two beautiful children, Lady Windermere visited Alton Priory, a lovely old house the Duke had given his son as a wedding present. One afternoon, as she sat with Lady Arthur beneath a lime tree in the garden, watching the little boy and girl dart along the rose walk like flashes of sunlight, she suddenly took her hostess\u2019s hand and asked, \u2018Are you happy, Sybil?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Dear Lady Windermere, of course I am happy. Aren\u2019t you?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018I have no time to be happy, Sybil. I always like the last person introduced to me; but usually, as soon as I know people, I grow tired of them.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Don\u2019t your lions satisfy you, Lady Windermere?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Oh dear, no! Lions are only useful for one season. Once their manes are cut, they are the dullest creatures alive. Besides, they behave very badly when you are truly kind to them. Do you remember that dreadful Mr. Podgers? He was a terrible fraud. Of course, I did not mind that, and I even forgave him when he asked to borrow money, but I could not tolerate his making love to me. He has made me hate palmistry. I study telepathy now. It is much more entertaining.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018You mustn\u2019t say anything against palmistry here, Lady Windermere; it is the only subject Arthur dislikes people joking about. I assure you, he takes it very seriously.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018You don\u2019t mean that he believes in it, Sybil?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Ask him, Lady Windermere\u2014here he is.\u2019 Lord Arthur came up the garden carrying a large bunch of yellow roses, with his two children dancing around him.\\n\\n\u2018Lord Arthur?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Yes, Lady Windermere.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018You don\u2019t mean that you believe in palmistry?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Of course I do,\u2019 said the young man with a smile.\\n\\n\u2018But why?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Because I owe it all the happiness of my life,\u2019 he murmured, sinking into a wicker chair.\"}"
