too would finally rest. Death still seemed far away, though I constantly wished for it. I often sat for hours without moving or speaking, longing for some great upheaval that would bury both me and my destroyer beneath its ruins.\\n\\nThe time of the assizes drew near. I had already spent three months in prison, and though I remained weak and constantly at risk of falling ill again, I was forced to travel almost a hundred miles to the country town where the court would meet. Mr. Kirwin took responsibility for gathering the witnesses and preparing my defence.\"}"
