          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"cd55f53130c8f4e644880665\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cStop the starboard! Ting-a-ling-ling! Stop the larboard! Move ahead on the starboard! Stop her! Let your outside paddle turn slowly! Ting-a-ling-ling! Chow-ow-ow! Get that head-line out! Quickly now! Come on\u2014get out your spring-line\u2014what are you doing there! Wrap its bight around that stump! Stand by that stage, now\u2014let her go! Engines stopped, sir! Ting-a-ling-ling! SH\u2019T! S\u2019H\u2019T! SH\u2019T!\u201d (testing the gauge-cocks).\\n\\nTom kept whitewashing and paid no attention to the steamboat. Ben stared for a moment, then said, \u201cHi-Yi! You\u2019re stuck, aren\u2019t you!\u201d\\n\\nTom did not answer. He examined his latest stroke like an artist, then gently swept his brush over it again and studied the result as before. Ben came up beside him. Tom\u2019s mouth watered at the apple, but he kept working. Ben said:\\n\\n\u201cHello, old fellow. You have to work, huh?\u201d\\n\\nTom turned suddenly and said, \u201cWhy, it\u2019s you, Ben! I didn\u2019t notice you.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSay\u2014I\u2019m going swimming. Don\u2019t you wish you could? But of course you\u2019d rather work, wouldn\u2019t you? Of course you would!\u201d\\n\\nTom studied the boy for a moment and said, \u201cWhat do you call work?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, isn\u2019t that work?\u201d\\n\\nTom went back to whitewashing and answered casually, \u201cWell, maybe it is, and maybe it isn\u2019t. All I know is, it suits Tom Sawyer.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, come on. You don\u2019t mean to pretend that you like it?\u201d\\n\\nThe brush kept moving.\\n\\n\u201cLike it? Well, I don\u2019t see why I shouldn\u2019t. Does a boy get the chance to whitewash a fence every day?\u201d\\n\\nThat made it seem different. Ben stopped nibbling his apple. Tom moved his brush neatly back and forth, stepped back to inspect the effect, added a touch here and there, and examined it again. Ben watched every movement, becoming more interested and absorbed. At last he said:\\n\\n\u201cSay, Tom, let me whitewash a little.\u201d\\n\\nTom thought about it and was about to agree, but then changed his mind.\\n\\n\u201cNo\u2014no\u2014I don\u2019t think that would do, Ben. You see, Aunt Polly is very particular about this fence\u2014it\u2019s right here on the street, you know. If it were the back fence, I wouldn\u2019t mind, and neither would she. Yes, she\u2019s very particular about this fence. It has to be done carefully. I guess there isn\u2019t one boy in a thousand, maybe two thousand, who can do it the way it needs to be done.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo\u2014is that so? Oh, come on\u2014let me try. Just a little. I\u2019d let you if you were me, Tom.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBen, I\u2019d like to, honest Indian; but Aunt Polly\u2014well, Jim wanted to do it, but she wouldn\u2019t let him. Sid wanted to do it, and she wouldn\u2019t let Sid.\u201d\"}"
