rent diameter, as seen from the balloon, subtended an angle of about sixty-five seconds. Its sombre color, varying in intensity, was always darker than any other point on the visible hemisphere, and at times deepened into the most complete and impenetrable blackness. Beyond this, little could be learned. By twelve o\u2019clock the circular centre had greatly diminished in circumference, and by seven P.M. I had lost sight of it altogether; the balloon having passed over the western edge of the ice and rapidly drifted away toward the equator.\\n\\n\u201cApril 8th. Observed a perceptible reduction in the earth\u2019s apparent diameter, together with a considerable change in its general color and aspect.\"}"
