ace with his future partner, once again faced the cold night wind. He paused only a few minutes in the male paupers\u2019 ward, abusing them somewhat, in order to reassure himself that he could perform the duties of workhouse master with the necessary severity. Satisfied of his qualifications, Mr. Bumble left the building with a light heart and bright visions of future advancement, which occupied his thoughts until he reached the undertaker\u2019s shop.\\n\\nNow, Mr. and Mrs. Sowerberry had gone out to tea and supper, and Noah Claypole was never inclined to undertake more physical exertion than was needed for the convenient performance of eating and drinking. Consequently, the shop remained open, although it was past the usual closing hour. Mr. Bumble tapped several times on the counter with his cane; but, receiving no answer and seeing a light shining through the glass window of the small parlor at the back, he ventured to peer inside and see what was happening. When he saw what was happening, he was considerably surprised.\"}"
