n a great deal of good.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd besides, if you had to go to the sea, it would have been better not to go to South End. South End is an unhealthy place. Perry was surprised to hear that you had chosen South End.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI know many people have that idea, but it is certainly a mistake, sir. We all remained perfectly healthy there and never suffered the least inconvenience from the mud; and Mr. Wingfield says it is entirely mistaken to suppose the place unhealthy. I am sure he can be trusted, because he thoroughly understands the nature of the air, and his own brother and family have been there repeatedly.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou should have gone to Cromer, my dear, if you went anywhere. Perry stayed at Cromer for a week once, and considers it the best of all the seaside resorts.\u201d\"}"
