tmorland. I could almost imagine myself among the Swiss mountains. The small patches of snow still lingering on the northern slopes, the lakes, and the rushing rocky streams were all familiar and beloved sights. Here, too, we made several acquaintances who nearly managed to deceive me into happiness. Clerval\u2019s pleasure was proportionately greater than mine; among talented people, his mind expanded, and he discovered within himself greater abilities and resources than he could have imagined possessing while he kept company with his inferiors.\"}"
