          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"638c32bcb83520ae67ff79ec\",\"rewritten_text\":\"One day, while I was occupied with my books and Mr. Pocket, I received a note in the mail. The sight of its outside threw me into great agitation; although I had never seen the handwriting in which it was addressed, I knew whose hand it was. It had no formal opening\u2014Dear Mr. Pip, Dear Pip, Dear Sir, or Dear Anything\u2014but read as follows:\\n\\n\u201cI am to come to London the day after tomorrow by the midday coach. I believe it was arranged that you should meet me? In any case, Miss Havisham has that impression, and I am writing in obedience to it. She sends you her regards.\\n\\n\u201cYours, ESTELLA.\u201d\\n\\nIf there had been time, I would probably have ordered several new suits for the occasion; but there was not, and I had to be satisfied with the clothes I already owned. My appetite disappeared at once, and I knew neither peace nor rest until the day came. Yet its arrival brought me neither; I was worse than ever, and began haunting the coach office in Wood Street, Cheapside, before the coach had even left the Blue Boar in our town. Though I knew perfectly well that it had not, I still felt it unsafe to let the coach office out of my sight for more than five minutes at a time. In this irrational state, I had completed the first half-hour of a four- or five-hour watch when Wemmick ran into me.\\n\\n\u201cHello, Mr. Pip,\u201d he said. \u201cHow are you? I would hardly have expected this to be your usual place.\u201d\\n\\nI explained that I was waiting to meet someone arriving by coach, and asked after the Castle and the Aged.\\n\\n\u201cBoth thriving, thank you,\u201d said Wemmick, \u201cand especially the Aged. He is in wonderful spirits. He will be eighty-two on his next birthday. I am thinking of firing eighty-two times, if the neighborhood does not object and my cannon can withstand the strain. But this is not London conversation. Where do you think I am going?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTo the office?\u201d I said, since he was heading that way.\\n\\n\u201cAlmost,\u201d Wemmick replied. \u201cI am going to Newgate. We are dealing with a banker\u2019s-parcel case at present, and I have been down the road to take a look at the scene of the crime. Now I must have a word or two with our client.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDid your client commit the robbery?\u201d I asked.\\n\\n\u201cGood heavens, no,\u201d Wemmick answered very dryly. \u201cBut he is accused of it. You or I might be accused of it just as easily. Either of us could be accused, you know.\u201d\"}"
