          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"389d53cdde30c6db2d3f5384\",\"rewritten_text\":\"They know what a clever lad he is; he\u2019ll be a lifer. They\u2019ll make the Artful nothing less than a lifer.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat do you mean by lagging and a lifer?\u201d demanded Mr. Bolter. \u201cWhat\u2019s the point of talking that way to me? Why don\u2019t you speak so I can understand you?\u201d\\n\\nFagin was about to translate these mysterious expressions into ordinary language; and, once interpreted, Mr. Bolter would have learned that they meant the phrase \u201ctransportation for life,\u201d when the conversation was interrupted by the arrival of Master Bates, his hands in his trouser pockets and his face twisted into an expression of half-comic misery.\\n\\n\u201cIt\u2019s all over, Fagin,\u201d said Charley, after he and his new companion had been introduced to each other.\\n\\n\u201cWhat do you mean?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThey\u2019ve found the gentleman who owns the box; two or three more are coming to identify him; and the Artful\u2019s booked for a passage out,\u201d replied Master Bates. \u201cI\u2019ll need a complete mourning suit, Fagin, and a hatband, to visit him in before he sets out on his travels. To think of Jack Dawkins\u2014lively Jack\u2014the Dodger\u2014the Artful Dodger\u2014going abroad for an ordinary cheap snuffbox! I never thought he\u2019d have done it for less than a gold watch, chain, and seals. Oh, why didn\u2019t he rob some rich old gentleman of all his valuables and go out like a gentleman, instead of as a common thief, without any honour or glory!\u201d\\n\\nAfter expressing these feelings for his unfortunate friend, Master Bates sat down on the nearest chair, looking bitter and dejected.\\n\\n\u201cWhat do you mean, saying he has neither honour nor glory?\u201d exclaimed Fagin, shooting an angry glance at his pupil. \u201cWasn\u2019t he always the best among you all? Is there one of you who could match him or come close to him at any game? Eh?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot one,\u201d replied Master Bates, his voice made hoarse by regret; \u201cnot one.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen what are you talking about?\u201d Fagin answered angrily. \u201cWhat are you crying for?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBecause it won\u2019t be on the record, will it?\u201d said Charley, driven into complete defiance of his venerable friend by the force of his grief; \u201cbecause it won\u2019t appear in the indictment; because no one will ever know half of what he was. How will he appear in the Newgate Calendar? Perhaps he won\u2019t be there at all. Oh, my goodness, what a blow it is!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHa! Ha!\u201d cried Fagin, extending his right hand and turning to Mr. Bolter in a fit of laughter that shook him as though he were suffering from palsy. \u201cSee how proud they are of their profession, my dear.\u201d\"}"
