ace reddened as though he were fighting for breath. He sprang up and seized his cudgel, but an instant later sank back into his chair, shaking violently, his features wearing the look of death itself. He said nothing. I felt the deepest pity for him.\\n\\n\u201cMy friend,\u201d said Dupin gently, \u201cyou are needlessly frightening yourself\u2014you truly are. We have no intention of harming you. I give you a gentleman\u2019s, and a Frenchman\u2019s, word that we mean you no injury. I know perfectly well that you are innocent of the atrocities in the Rue Morgue. It would not be proper, however, to deny that you are in some degree connected with them.\u201d\"}"
