          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"223af4cc2285952626163a7d\",\"rewritten_text\":\"After supper the whole gang went out onto the bar to search for turtle eggs. They poked sticks into the sand, and whenever they found a soft spot, dropped to their knees and dug with their fingers. At times they pulled fifty or sixty eggs from a single hole. They were perfectly round, white objects, slightly smaller than an English walnut. That evening they enjoyed a grand fried-egg feast, and had another Friday morning.\\n\\nAfter breakfast they went whooping and prancing onto the bar, chasing one another in circles and throwing off their clothes as they ran, until they were naked. Then they carried the frolic far up the bar\u2019s shallow water, struggling against the strong current, which repeatedly swept their legs from beneath them and made the sport all the merrier. Every so often they bent together and flung water into one another\u2019s faces with their hands, slowly drawing nearer, their faces turned aside to escape the choking sprays. At last they seized and wrestled until the strongest ducked his neighbor, and then all of them plunged beneath the surface in a tangle of pale arms and legs, rising together, blowing, sputtering, laughing, and gasping for air.\\n\\nOnce thoroughly worn out, they would race ashore and sprawl upon the dry, scorching sand, covering themselves with it. Presently they would dash back into the water and repeat the whole performance. At length they realized that their bare skin made fairly good flesh-colored \u201ctights,\u201d so they marked out a ring in the sand and put on a circus\u2014with three clowns, since none of them would surrender that most honored position to another.\\n\\nAfter that they brought out their marbles and played \u201cknucks,\u201d \u201cringtaw,\u201d and \u201ckeeps\u201d until the game lost its charm. Joe and Huck then took another swim, but Tom refused, having discovered that when he kicked off his trousers he had also knocked the string of rattlesnake rattles from his ankle. He wondered how he had avoided cramp for so long without the protection of that mysterious charm. He would not go in again until he found it, and by then the other boys were weary and prepared to rest. Gradually they drifted apart, sank into the \u201cdumps,\u201d and gazed wistfully across the broad river toward the village, which lay dozing in the sunshine. Tom caught himself writing \u201cBECKY\u201d in the sand with his big toe. He rubbed it out and scolded himself for being so weak. Yet he wrote it again; he could not resist. He erased it once more, then removed the temptation by herding the other boys together and joining them.\"}"
