          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"e6f533ba37f6eb3fdbc40099\",\"rewritten_text\":\"I then went from one shop to another, buying whatever was needed to alter his appearance. That business finished, I turned, for my own purposes, toward Little Britain. Mr. Jaggers was seated at his desk, but when he saw me enter, he rose at once and stood in front of the fire.\\n\\n\u201cNow, Pip,\u201d he said, \u201cbe cautious.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI will, sir,\u201d I replied. For, as I came along, I had carefully considered what I meant to say.\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t implicate yourself,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, \u201cand don\u2019t implicate anybody else. You understand\u2014anybody. Tell me nothing: I don\u2019t wish to know anything; I am not inquisitive.\u201d\\n\\nOf course, I perceived that he knew the man had arrived.\\n\\n\u201cI only wish, Mr. Jaggers,\u201d said I, \u201cto satisfy myself that what I have been told is true. I have no expectation that it is false, but I may at least confirm it.\u201d\\n\\nMr. Jaggers nodded. \u201cBut did you say \u2018told\u2019 or \u2018informed\u2019?\u201d he asked, holding his head to one side, and looking not at me but at the floor, as though listening there. \u201cTold would appear to suggest verbal communication. You cannot have verbal communication with a man in New South Wales, you know.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI will say, informed, Mr. Jaggers.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGood.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have been informed by a person called Abel Magwitch that he is the benefactor who has been unknown to me for so long.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat is the man,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, \u201cin New South Wales.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd no one else?\u201d I asked.\\n\\n\u201cAnd no one else,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers.\\n\\n\u201cI am not so unreasonable, sir, as to hold you responsible for my errors and mistaken conclusions; but I had always believed it was Miss Havisham.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAs you say, Pip,\u201d returned Mr. Jaggers, turning his cool eyes on me and biting his forefinger, \u201cI am not responsible for that in the least.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd yet it seemed so much like it, sir,\u201d I pleaded, my heart cast down.\\n\\n\u201cNot the smallest particle of evidence, Pip,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, shaking his head and gathering up his skirts. \u201cTrust nothing to appearances; trust everything to evidence. There is no better rule.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have nothing more to say,\u201d I said with a sigh, after remaining silent for a short while. \u201cI have confirmed my information, and that is the end of it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd Magwitch\u2014in New South Wales\u2014having at last revealed himself,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, \u201cyou will understand, Pip, how strictly, throughout my communications with you, I have kept to the exact line of fact. There has never been the slightest departure from that exact line. You are fully aware of this?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cQuite, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI communicated to Magwitch\u2014in New South Wales\u2014when he first wrote to me\u2014from New South Wales\u2014the warning that he must never expect me to depart from the exact line of fact.\u201d\"}"
