          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"818984895c8f223bf3029202\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cOh, I misunderstood you. I thought you said \u2018anybody,\u2019 and therefore assumed that \u2018anybody\u2019 meant\u2014well, anybody; that is, everybody.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt doth\u2014anybody of noble birth; and better still if he be royal.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat, it seemeth to me, may well be so,\u201d said the abbot, who perceived a chance to smooth matters and prevent disaster, \u201cfor it were unlikely that so marvelous a gift as this should be granted for revealing the affairs of beings less exalted than those born near the heights of greatness. Our King Arthur\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWould you hear of him?\u201d interrupted the enchanter.\\n\\n\u201cMost gladly, yea, and with gratitude.\u201d\\n\\nEveryone was instantly filled with awe and interest again, the incorrigible fools. They watched the enchantments with rapt attention, then looked at me with a \u201cThere now, what have you to say to that?\u201d expression when the announcement was made:\\n\\n\u201cThe king is weary from the chase, and hath lain in his palace these two hours, sleeping without dreams.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGod\u2019s blessing upon him!\u201d said the abbot, crossing himself; \u201cmay that sleep refresh both body and soul.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd so it might, were he asleep,\u201d I said, \u201cbut the king is not sleeping; the king is riding.\u201d\\n\\nThere was trouble once more\u2014a clash of authority. No one knew which of us to trust; I still retained some reputation. The magician\u2019s contempt was aroused, and he said:\\n\\n\u201cLo, I have seen many wondrous soothsayers, prophets, and magicians in my lifetime, but never one before who could sit idle and perceive the heart of things without a single incantation to aid him.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou have dwelt in the woods, and lost much thereby. I use incantations myself, as this good brotherhood know\u2014but only when the occasion is important