          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"470dbb7d7445a9281f6892d6\",\"rewritten_text\":\"But do not suppose that I did not consider it an evil in itself.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBelieve me, they were all entirely comfortable.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI might not think better of them for that, perhaps. Such a crowd of women and children have no _right_ to be comfortable aboard ship.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Frederick, you are speaking very idly. What would become of us poor sailors\u2019 wives, who often need to be carried from one port to another after our husbands, if everyone shared your feelings?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAs you see, my feelings did not stop me from taking Mrs Harville and her whole family to Plymouth.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut I dislike hearing you speak so much like a fine gentleman, as though women were all fine ladies rather than rational beings. None of us expect smooth water throughout our lives.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAh! my dear,\u201d said the Admiral, \u201conce he has a wife, he will sing another tune. If he marries, and we are fortunate enough to live until another war, we shall see him do as you and I, and many others, have done. We shall find him deeply grateful to anyone who brings him his wife.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAy, that we shall.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNow I have finished,\u201d cried Captain Wentworth. \u201cWhenever married people begin attacking me with, \u2018Oh! you will think quite differently when you are married,\u2019 I can only answer, \u2018No, I shall not;\u2019 and then they repeat, \u2018Yes, you will,\u2019 and there is no more to say.\u201d\\n\\nHe rose and walked away.\\n\\n\u201cWhat a great traveller you must have been, ma\u2019am!\u201d said Mrs Musgrove to Mrs Croft.\\n\\n\u201cFairly so, ma\u2019am, during the fifteen years of my marriage; though many women have travelled farther. I have crossed the Atlantic four times, and gone once to the East Indies and back, only once; besides visiting various places nearer home: Cork, Lisbon, and Gibraltar. But I never passed the Straits, and was never in the West Indies. Bermuda and Bahama, you know, are not what we call the West Indies.\u201d\\n\\nMrs Musgrove had nothing to say against this; she could not accuse herself of ever having called them anything at all during her life.\\n\\n\u201cAnd I assure you, ma\u2019am,\u201d Mrs Croft continued, \u201cthat nothing surpasses the accommodations of a man-of-war; I speak, of course, of the higher rates. In a frigate, naturally, one is more confined; yet any reasonable woman may be perfectly happy in one; and I can safely say that the happiest portion of my life was spent aboard ship. While we were together, you know, there was nothing to fear.\"}"
