een hearing the arguing voices and breaking open the chamber door. Some said as little as three minutes; others as much as five. The door was difficult to open.\\n\\n\u201c_Alfonzo Garcio_, undertaker, states that he lives in the Rue Morgue. He is a native of Spain. He was one of the group who entered the house but did not go upstairs. He is nervous and feared the effects of agitation. He heard the voices arguing. The gruff voice belonged to a Frenchman. He could not make out what was said. The shrill voice was that of an Englishman\u2014of this he is certain.\u201d\"}"
