ss, I may be able to send it to-morrow.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Oh, that will be quite soon enough!\u2019 said Lord Arthur courteously, \u2018provided it arrives to-morrow night or on Thursday morning. As for the explosion, let us say Friday at exactly noon. The Dean is invariably at home then.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Friday, at noon,\u2019 repeated Herr Winckelkopf, making a note of it in a large ledger lying on a bureau beside the fireplace.\\n\\n\u2018And now,\u2019 said Lord Arthur, getting to his feet, \u2018please tell me how much I owe you.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018It is such a trifling matter, Lord Arthur, that I do not wish to charge you anything. The dynamite is seven and sixpence, the clock three pounds ten, and the carriage roughly five shillings. I am delighted to oblige any friend of Count Rouvaloff\u2019s.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018But your trouble, Herr Winckelkopf?\u2019\"}"
