          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"0adeb930eb348adb1a7722e6\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cWhat\u2019s the matter?\u201d demanded Oliver.\\n\\n\u201cHush!\u201d replied the Dodger. \u201cDo you see that old fellow at the bookstall?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThe old gentleman across the street?\u201d said Oliver. \u201cYes, I see him.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHe\u2019ll do,\u201d said the Dodger.\\n\\n\u201cA fine mark,\u201d said Master Charley Bates.\\n\\nOliver looked from one to the other in great surprise, but he had no chance to ask questions. The two boys quietly crossed the road and slipped in behind the old gentleman they had pointed out. Oliver followed a few steps behind them. Unsure whether to go forward or turn back, he stood watching in silent amazement.\\n\\nThe old gentleman looked very respectable, with a powdered head and gold spectacles. He wore a bottle-green coat with a black velvet collar and white trousers, and carried a smart bamboo cane under his arm. He had picked up a book from the stall and stood reading it as seriously as if he were sitting in his own study. He may even have imagined himself there, for he was so absorbed that he seemed to notice neither the stall, the street, the boys, nor anything except the book. He read straight through it, turning the page when he reached the bottom and beginning at the top of the next, continuing with the greatest interest and eagerness.\\n\\nWhat horror and alarm filled Oliver as he stood a few paces away, his eyes opened as wide as possible, and saw the Dodger thrust his hand into the old gentleman\u2019s pocket and pull out a handkerchief! He saw him pass it to Charley Bates, and then watched them both run around the corner at full speed!\\n\\nIn an instant, the whole mystery of the handkerchiefs, watches, jewels, and the Jew came rushing into the boy\u2019s mind.\\n\\nFor a moment he stood there, terror making his blood tingle through every vein until he felt as if he were burning. Then, confused and frightened, he ran off, moving his feet as fast as he could.\\n\\nIt all happened within a minute. Just as Oliver began to run, the old gentleman put his hand into his pocket and discovered that his handkerchief was gone. He turned sharply, saw the boy hurrying away at great speed, and naturally concluded that Oliver was the thief. Shouting \u201cStop thief!\u201d with all his strength, he ran after him, still holding the book in his hand.\"}"
