hed her forehead with eau-de-cologne. Mr. Otis immediately insisted that she eat something and ordered supper for everyone. It was a mournful meal, for scarcely anyone spoke; even the twins were subdued and awestruck, being deeply attached to their sister. When it was over, Mr. Otis, despite the little Duke\u2019s pleas, sent them all to bed. Nothing more could be done that night, he said, and in the morning he would telegraph Scotland Yard to send detectives down at once.\"}"
