ongratulations to the Minister\u2019s worthy wife.\\n\\nThe Otises were mistaken, however. The ghost was still in the house. Though he was now almost an invalid, he was not ready to give up, especially after hearing that the young Duke of Cheshire was among the guests. The Duke\u2019s great-uncle, Lord Francis Stilton, had once wagered a hundred guineas with Colonel Carbury that he would play dice with the Canterville ghost. The next morning, Lord Francis was found lying on the card-room floor in such a helpless, paralyzed condition that, although he lived to a very old age, he was never again able to say anything except \u2018Double Sixes.\u2019\"}"
