          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"cd1b7676e82e59622c1c72ff\",\"rewritten_text\":\"After a while, twelve o\u2019clock sounded from the tall Westminster tower, and with every stroke of the deep bell the night appeared to quiver. Then the railway lights were extinguished, leaving one lonely lamp shining like a great ruby upon a gigantic mast, while the city\u2019s roar grew more distant.\\n\\nAt two he rose and wandered towards Blackfriars. How unreal it all appeared, how much like some fantastic dream! The houses across the river seemed formed from darkness. One might have thought that silver and shadow had remade the world. The vast dome of St. Paul\u2019s showed through the murky air like a bubble.\\n\\nAs he neared Cleopatra\u2019s Needle, he noticed a man bending over the parapet. When he drew closer, the man raised his head, and the gaslight fell directly across his face.\\n\\nIt was Mr. Podgers, the cheiromantist! The fat, flabby countenance, the gold-rimmed spectacles, the weak, sickly smile, and the sensual mouth could belong to no one else.\\n\\nLord Arthur halted. A splendid thought struck him, and he crept quietly up behind. In an instant he had grasped Mr. Podgers by the legs and hurled him into the Thames. There was a rough oath, a heavy splash, and then silence. Lord Arthur peered anxiously over the parapet, but saw nothing of the cheiromantist except a tall hat spinning in an eddy of moonlit water. Presently that too disappeared, and no sign of Mr. Podgers remained. Once he fancied he saw the bulky, misshapen figure swimming towards the bridge staircase, and a dreadful sense of failure seized him; but it proved only a reflection, and when the moon emerged from behind a cloud, the feeling vanished. At last he believed that destiny\u2019s decree had been fulfilled. He drew a profound sigh of relief, and Sybil\u2019s name rose to his lips.\\n\\n\u2018Have you dropped anything, sir?\u2019 a voice suddenly asked behind him.\\n\\nHe turned and found a policeman holding a bull\u2019s-eye lantern.\\n\\n\u2018Nothing of consequence, sergeant,\u2019 he replied with a smile. Hailing a passing hansom, he climbed in and ordered the driver to take him to Belgrave Square.\\n\\nFor the next several days he swung between hope and fear. At times he almost expected Mr. Podgers to enter the room, while at others he felt that Fate could not treat him so unjustly. Twice he went to the cheiromantist\u2019s address in West Moon Street, but could not bring himself to ring. He yearned for certainty and dreaded it.\\n\\nAt last it arrived. He was seated in the club smoking-room, drinking tea and listening somewhat wearily to Surbiton\u2019s description of the latest comic song at the Gaiety, when the waiter entered carrying the evening papers.\"}"
