          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"f092357cdec885b603974c3d\",\"rewritten_text\":\"If, however, you want one for home use, I can provide you with an excellent device and guarantee that you will be satisfied with the result. May I ask whom it is intended for? If it is for the police, or for anyone connected with Scotland Yard, I am afraid I can do nothing for you. English detectives are truly our best friends, and I have always found that, by relying on their stupidity, we can do exactly as we please. I could not spare one of them.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018I assure you,\u2019 said Lord Arthur, \u2018that it has nothing to do with the police. In fact, the clock is intended for the Dean of Chichester.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Good heavens! I had no idea you felt so strongly about religion, Lord Arthur. Few young men do these days.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018I am afraid you overestimate me, Herr Winckelkopf,\u2019 said Lord Arthur, blushing. \u2018The truth is, I know nothing at all about theology.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Then it is purely a private matter?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Entirely private.\u2019\\n\\nHerr Winckelkopf shrugged and left the room, returning a few minutes later with a round cake of dynamite about the size of a penny and a pretty little French clock, topped by an ormolu figure of Liberty trampling the hydra of Despotism.\\n\\nLord Arthur\u2019s face brightened when he saw it. \u2018That is exactly what I want,\u2019 he exclaimed. \u2018Now tell me how it goes off.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Ah! That is my secret,\u2019 replied Herr Winckelkopf, regarding his invention with justifiable pride. \u2018Tell me when you want it to explode, and I will set the mechanism for that exact moment.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Well, today is Tuesday, and if you could send it at once\u2014\u2019\\n\\n\u2018That is impossible; I have a great deal of important work to do for some friends of mine in Moscow. Still, I might send it tomorrow.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Oh, that will be quite soon enough!\u2019 said Lord Arthur politely. \u2018If it is delivered tomorrow night or Thursday morning, that will do. As for the explosion, say Friday at exactly noon. The Dean is always at home at that hour.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Friday, at noon,\u2019 repeated Herr Winckelkopf, making a note of it in a large ledger lying on a bureau near the fireplace.\\n\\n\u2018And now,\u2019 said Lord Arthur, rising, \u2018please tell me how much I owe you.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018It is such a small matter, Lord Arthur, that I do not wish to charge you. The dynamite costs seven shillings and sixpence, the clock three pounds ten, and the carriage about five shillings. I am only too happy to oblige any friend of Count Rouvaloff\u2019s.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018But your trouble, Herr Winckelkopf?\u2019\"}"
