          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"f072cbb2fa376fc5ff4d8691\",\"rewritten_text\":\"There was something so striking in the growing intensity of Mr. Wopsle\u2019s eye. He seemed to be turning over so many thoughts and becoming so confused that I could not understand him. I kept thinking about it long after he had risen into the clouds inside a large watch-case, and still I could not understand it. I was thinking about it when I left the theatre an hour later and found him waiting for me near the door.\\n\\n\u201cHow are you?\u201d I asked, shaking his hand as we walked down the street together. \u201cI saw that you saw me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSaw you, Mr. Pip!\u201d he replied. \u201cYes, of course I saw you. But who else was there?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWho else?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt is the strangest thing,\u201d said Mr. Wopsle, falling again into his confused expression. \u201cAnd yet I could swear it was him.\u201d\\n\\nAlarmed, I begged Mr. Wopsle to explain what he meant.\\n\\n\u201cWhether I would have noticed him at first if you had not been there,\u201d said Mr. Wopsle, continuing in the same confused manner, \u201cI cannot say for certain; but I think I would have.\u201d\\n\\nWithout meaning to, I looked around me, as I had grown used to doing on my way home. His mysterious words sent a chill through me.\\n\\n\u201cOh! He cannot be seen now,\u201d said Mr. Wopsle. \u201cHe left before I did. I saw him go.\u201d\\n\\nBecause I had reason to be suspicious, I even suspected the poor actor. I feared he was trying to trap me into admitting something. So I watched him as we walked on together, but said nothing.\\n\\n\u201cI had the foolish idea that he must be with you, Mr. Pip, until I saw that you were completely unaware of him, sitting behind you there like a ghost.\u201d\\n\\nThat earlier chill came over me again, but I was determined not to speak yet. His words could easily mean that someone had sent him to make me connect these hints with Provis. Of course, I was completely certain that Provis had not been there.\\n\\n\u201cI suppose you wonder at me, Mr. Pip; indeed, I can see that you do. But it is so strange! You will hardly believe what I am about to tell you. I could scarcely believe it myself if you told it to me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cReally?\u201d I said.\\n\\n\u201cYes, really. Mr. Pip, do you remember a certain Christmas Day long ago, when you were a small child, and I dined at Gargery\u2019s? Some soldiers came to the door to have a pair of handcuffs repaired.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI remember it very well.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd you remember that two convicts were being chased, that we joined the search, that Gargery carried you on his back, and that I led the way while you kept up with me as best you could?\u201d\"}"
