          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"1e73521e5f123db0e09f94d9\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cWhat\u2019s the matter?\u201d demanded Oliver.\\n\\n\u201cHush!\u201d answered the Dodger. \u201cDo you see that old cove at the book-stall?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThe old gentleman across the way?\u201d said Oliver. \u201cYes, I see him.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHe\u2019ll do,\u201d said the Dodger.\\n\\n\u201cA prime plant,\u201d remarked Master Charley Bates.\\n\\nOliver glanced from one to the other in profound surprise, but was given no chance to ask questions; for the two boys crept across the road and slipped in close behind the old gentleman to whom they had pointed. Oliver followed a few paces behind them; and, uncertain whether to go forward or turn back, stood watching in silent astonishment.\\n\\nThe old gentleman looked a highly respectable person, with a powdered head and gold spectacles. He wore a bottle-green coat with a black velvet collar, white trousers, and carried a smart bamboo cane beneath his arm. He had taken a book from the stall and stood there reading it as intently as though he were seated in his own study, in his elbow-chair. It is quite possible that he imagined himself there; for his abstraction made it clear that he noticed neither the book-stall, nor the street, nor the boys\u2014in short, nothing except the book itself. He read straight through it, turning the leaf upon reaching the bottom of each page, beginning at the top line of the next, and proceeding steadily with the greatest interest and eagerness.\\n\\nWhat were Oliver\u2019s horror and alarm, as he stood a few paces away with his eyelids opened as wide as they could go, when he saw the Dodger thrust his hand into the old gentleman\u2019s pocket and pull out a handkerchief! He watched him pass it to Charley Bates; and then saw them both run around the corner at full speed!\\n\\nIn an instant, the entire mystery of the handkerchiefs, watches, jewels, and the Jew came rushing into the boy\u2019s mind.\\n\\nFor a moment he stood there, the blood tingling through every vein with such terror that he felt as though he were in a blazing fire; then, bewildered and frightened, he turned and ran, making off as quickly as his feet could carry him, without knowing what he was doing.\\n\\nThe whole thing had happened within a minute. At the very moment Oliver started to run, the old gentleman put his hand into his pocket, discovered that his handkerchief was gone, and wheeled sharply around. Seeing the boy hurrying away at such speed, he naturally took him for the thief; and, crying \u201cStop thief!\u201d at the top of his voice, set off after him, book in hand.\"}"
