ve you know the rest of the adventure as well as I do.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI suppose,\u201d I said, \u201cthat you missed the spot on your first attempt to dig because Jupiter foolishly let the bug fall through the skull\u2019s right eye instead of its left.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cExactly. This mistake shifted the \u2018shot\u2019\u2014that is, the position of the peg nearest the tree\u2014by about two and a half inches. If the treasure had been directly beneath the \u2018shot,\u2019 the error would have mattered little. But \u2018the shot\u2019 and the nearest point of the tree were only two points used to establish a direction. Naturally, though the error was small at first, it grew as we followed the line, and after fifty feet it had led us completely away from the treasure.\u201d\"}"
