          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"d58636c1eef394b2e57d17d4\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cWhat\u2019s the trouble?\u201d\\n\\nI said:\\n\\n\u201cPap, and Mam, and Sis, and\u2014\u201d\\n\\nThen I broke down. He said:\\n\\n\u201cOh, darn it, don\u2019t take on so; we all have our troubles, and this will turn out all right. What\u2019s the matter with them?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThey\u2019re\u2014they\u2019re\u2014are you the watchman of the boat?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes,\u201d he said, looking fairly pleased with himself. \u201cI\u2019m the captain and the owner and the mate and the pilot and watchman and head deckhand; and sometimes I\u2019m the freight and passengers. I\u2019m not as rich as old Jim Hornback, and I can\u2019t be as blameably generous and good to Tom, Dick, and Harry as he is, throwing money around the way he does; but I\u2019ve told him many a time that I wouldn\u2019t trade places with him; for, I say, a sailor\u2019s life is the life for me, and I\u2019m damned if I\u2019d live two miles outside town, where nothing ever happens, not for all his money and as much more besides. I say\u2014\u201d\\n\\nI broke in and said:\\n\\n\u201cThey\u2019re in terrible trouble, and\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWho is?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, Pap and Mam and Sis and Miss Hooker; and if you\u2019d take your ferryboat and go up there\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cUp where? Where are they?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOn the wreck.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat wreck?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, there\u2019s only one.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat, you don\u2019t mean the Walter Scott?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGood heavens! What are they doing there, for goodness\u2019 sake?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, they didn\u2019t go there on purpose.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI bet they didn\u2019t! Why, great goodness, they have no chance if they don\u2019t get off mighty quick! How in the world did they ever get into such a mess?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cEasily enough. Miss Hooker was visiting up there in town\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, Booth\u2019s Landing\u2014go on.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cShe was visiting there at Booth\u2019s Landing, and just at dusk she started across with her Black woman in the horse ferry to spend the night at her friend\u2019s house, Miss What\u2019s-her-name\u2014I\u2019ve forgotten her name\u2014and they lost their steering oar, swung around, and drifted downstream, stern first, about two miles, and struck the wreck broadside. The ferryman, the Black woman, and the horses were all lost, but Miss Hooker grabbed hold and got aboard the wreck. Well, about an hour after dark we came downstream in our trading scow, and it was so dark we didn\u2019t see the wreck until we were right on it; and then we struck it broadside too. But all of us were saved except Bill Whipple\u2014and oh, he was the best creature! I almost wish it had been me, I do.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy goodness! It\u2019s the most astonishing thing I ever heard.\u201d\"}"
