h was determined, and Sir William\u2019s efforts to persuade her did not change her mind.\\n\\n\u201cYou dance so well, Miss Eliza, that it is cruel to deny me the pleasure of watching you; and although this gentleman generally dislikes the amusement, I am sure he can have no objection to pleasing us for half an hour.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMr. Darcy is all politeness,\u201d said Elizabeth, smiling.\\n\\n\u201cHe certainly is. But given the reason, my dear Miss Eliza, we cannot be surprised by his willingness; for who would object to such a partner?\u201d\\n\\nElizabeth gave him a playful look and turned away. Her refusal had not offended the gentleman, and he was thinking of her with some satisfaction when Miss Bingley addressed him\u2014\"}"
