{"request_id":"27c7d0089024081e09e0c614","rewritten_text":"Indeed, I felt no concern for her. She was what people call a remarkable woman and could handle worldly matters without my help. To be honest, I believe she always saw me as an idle boy, a useless extra, fit only for building castles in the air, and was quite pleased to be rid of me. It was a dark night when I said goodbye to her. Taking the three creditors who had caused me so much trouble as my assistants, I carried the balloon, with its car and equipment, by a roundabout route to the station where the other supplies had been stored. We found everything there untouched, and I immediately began my work.

“It was the first of April. As I said, the night was dark, with not a star in sight, and a light rain fell from time to time, making us very uncomfortable. My main worry, however, was the balloon. Despite its protective varnish, it was beginning to grow heavy with damp, and the powder might also be damaged. So I kept my three creditors working hard, having them pound ice around the central cask and stir the acid in the others. Still, they kept questioning me about what I meant to do with all this equipment and complained bitterly about the terrible work I was making them perform. They said they could not see what good could come from getting soaked merely to take part in such dreadful magic. I grew anxious and worked with all my strength, for I truly believe the fools thought I had made a pact with the devil, and that what I was doing was, in short, nothing proper. I was therefore very afraid they would abandon me. However, I managed to calm them by promising to pay all I owed as soon as I finished the present task. Naturally, they understood these words in their own way. No doubt they imagined that I would soon possess a great deal of ready money; and as long as I paid everything I owed, plus a little extra for their services, I suspect they cared very little what happened to either my soul or my body.

“After about four and a half hours, I found that the balloon was fully inflated. I attached the car and placed all my equipment inside it, remembering the condensing apparatus, a plentiful supply of water, and a large amount of food, including pemmican, which contains much nourishment in a small space."}

