          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"75a1cd902d9647c5c56b413e\",\"rewritten_text\":\"It is a strange thing, but everyone who disappears is said to be seen in San Francisco. It must be a delightful city, with all the attractions of the next world.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat do you think happened to Basil?\u201d Dorian asked, holding his Burgundy up to the light and wondering how he could discuss the matter so calmly.\\n\\n\u201cI haven\u2019t the slightest idea. If Basil chooses to hide, that is none of my concern. If he is dead, I don\u2019t want to think about him. Death is the only thing that truly frightens me. I hate it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy?\u201d the younger man asked tiredly.\\n\\n\u201cBecause,\u201d Lord Henry said, passing the gilt lattice of an open vinaigrette beneath his nose, \u201cnowadays one can survive everything except that. Death and vulgarity are the only two facts of the nineteenth century that cannot be explained away. Let us have coffee in the music room, Dorian. You must play Chopin for me. The man my wife ran away with played Chopin beautifully. Poor Victoria! I was very fond of her. The house feels rather lonely without her. Of course, married life is only a habit, and a bad one. But we regret losing even our worst habits. Perhaps we regret them most. They are such an important part of who we are.\u201d\\n\\nDorian said nothing. He rose from the table, went into the next room, sat at the piano, and let his fingers wander over the white and black keys. When the coffee arrived, he stopped and looked across at Lord Henry. \u201cHarry, did you ever think that Basil might have been murdered?\u201d\\n\\nLord Henry yawned. \u201cBasil was very popular, and he always wore a Waterbury watch. Why would anyone murder him? He was not clever enough to have enemies. Of course, he had a remarkable gift for painting. But a man can paint like Velasquez and still be completely dull. Basil was really rather dull. He interested me only once, when he told me years ago that he adored you wildly and that you were the main inspiration for his art.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI was very fond of Basil,\u201d Dorian said, sadness in his voice. \u201cBut don\u2019t people say he was murdered?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, some newspapers do. It doesn\u2019t seem likely to me. I know there are terrible places in Paris, but Basil was not the kind of man who would have gone to them. He had no curiosity. That was his greatest flaw.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat would you say, Harry, if I told you that I had murdered Basil?\u201d the younger man asked.\"}"
