          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"138b250dc381b579b3566d7b\",\"rewritten_text\":\"The insect\u2019s weight was truly remarkable, and, considering everything, I could hardly blame Jupiter for his opinion of it; but for the life of me, I could not understand Legrand\u2019s agreement with that opinion.\\n\\n\u201cI sent for you,\u201d he said grandly, after I had finished examining the beetle, \u201cI sent for you so that I might have your counsel and assistance in advancing the designs of Fate and the bug\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Legrand,\u201d I cried, interrupting him, \u201cyou are certainly unwell and should take some precautions. You must go to bed, and I will stay with you for a few days, until you recover. You are feverish and\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cFeel my pulse,\u201d he said.\\n\\nI did so and, to tell the truth, found no sign of fever at all.\\n\\n\u201cBut you may be ill without having a fever. Let me prescribe for you this once. First, go to bed. Then\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou are mistaken,\u201d he interrupted. \u201cI am as well as I can expect to be under the excitement I am experiencing. If you truly wish me well, you will relieve that excitement.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd how is that to be done?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cVery easily. Jupiter and I are going on an expedition into the hills on the mainland, and for this expedition we will need the help of someone we can trust. You are the only person we can rely on. Whether we succeed or fail, the excitement you now see in me will be calmed.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI am eager to oblige you in any way,\u201d I replied; \u201cbut do you mean that this infernal beetle has anything to do with your expedition into the hills?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt does.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen, Legrand, I can take no part in such an absurd undertaking.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI am sorry\u2014very sorry\u2014for we will have to attempt it alone.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAttempt it alone! The man must be mad!\u2014but wait! How long do you intend to be gone?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cProbably all night. We will leave at once and return, in any case, by sunrise.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd will you promise me, on your honor, that when this whim of yours is over, and the beetle business\u2014good God!\u2014has been settled to your satisfaction, you will return home and follow my advice without question, as you would that of your physician?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, I promise. Now let us go, for we have no time to waste.\u201d\\n\\nWith a heavy heart, I accompanied my friend. We set out at about four o\u2019clock\u2014Legrand, Jupiter, the dog, and myself. Jupiter carried the scythe and spades, insisting on bearing them all himself\u2014apparently more because he feared trusting either tool within his master\u2019s reach than from any excess of diligence or willingness.\"}"
