sk; six tinned-metal tubes, three inches in diameter, properly shaped, and ten feet long; a quantity of a certain metallic or semi-metallic substance, which I will not name; and twelve demijohns of a very common acid. The gas produced from these last materials is one that no one but myself has ever generated\u2014or at least ever used for a similar purpose. I would have no objection to revealing the secret, except that it properly belongs to a citizen of Nantes, France, who shared it with me on the condition that I keep it confidential.\"}"
