          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"f914d1a9074bfb63f45dfa38\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cOne more word, Rose. Dearest Rose\u2014just one more!\u201d cried Harry, throwing himself before her. \u201cIf I had been less fortunate\u2014if the world had expected me to live some obscure, peaceful life\u2014if I had been poor, sick, or helpless\u2014would you have turned away from me then? Or has the prospect of my rising to wealth and honour created this hesitation?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDo not force me to answer,\u201d Rose replied. \u201cThe question does not arise, and never will. It is unfair, almost cruel, to press me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIf your answer is what I hardly dare hope,\u201d Harry said, \u201cit will bring a ray of happiness to my lonely life and light the road ahead. It is no small thing, with a few brief words, to do so much for someone who loves you above all else. Oh, Rose, in the name of my passionate and lasting love; in the name of everything I have suffered for you, and everything you condemn me to endure; answer this one question!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen, if your circumstances had been different,\u201d Rose answered; \u201cif you had been only somewhat, rather than so greatly, above me; if I could have been a help and comfort to you in some humble, peaceful retreat, instead of a burden and disadvantage among ambitious and distinguished people; I would have been spared this trial. I have every reason to be happy\u2014very happy\u2014now. But then, Harry, I admit I would have been happier.\u201d\\n\\nAs Rose made this confession, memories of old hopes, cherished when she was young, crowded into her mind. But they brought tears, as old hopes often do when they return faded and ruined; and afterward she felt relieved.\\n\\n\u201cI cannot prevent this weakness, and it makes me more determined,\u201d she said, holding out her hand. \u201cI must leave you now\u2014truly.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI ask one promise,\u201d said Harry. \u201cOnce, and only once more\u2014within a year, perhaps much sooner\u2014may I speak to you about this for the last time?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot to pressure me into changing my firm decision,\u201d Rose replied with a sad smile. \u201cThat would be useless.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo,\u201d said Harry. \u201cOnly to hear you repeat it, if you will\u2014repeat it finally. I will place at your feet whatever position or fortune I may have gained; and if you still keep your present decision, I will not try, by word or deed, to change it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen let it be so,\u201d Rose answered. \u201cIt is only one more pain, and by then I may be better able to bear it.\u201d\\n\\nShe held out her hand again.\"}"
