          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"426cd54832207d6cdaf17526\",\"rewritten_text\":\"It seemed to be a collection of back lanes, ditches, and small gardens, with the look of a rather dull, quiet retreat. Wemmick\u2019s house was a little wooden cottage surrounded by garden plots. Its top had been cut out and painted to look like a battery fitted with guns.\\n\\n\u201cMy own work,\u201d said Wemmick. \u201cLooks nice, doesn\u2019t it?\u201d\\n\\nI praised it highly. I believe it was the smallest house I had ever seen, with the strangest Gothic windows\u2014most of them false\u2014and a Gothic door almost too small to enter.\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s a real flagstaff,\u201d said Wemmick, \u201cand on Sundays I raise a real flag. Now look here. After I cross this bridge, I pull it up\u2014like this\u2014and cut off communication.\u201d\\n\\nThe bridge was a plank crossing a ditch about four feet wide and two feet deep. It was very pleasant to see the pride with which he raised it and secured it, smiling with real enjoyment rather than doing it mechanically.\\n\\n\u201cAt nine o\u2019clock every night, Greenwich time,\u201d said Wemmick, \u201cthe gun fires. There it is, you see! And when you hear it go off, I think you\u2019ll agree it\u2019s a Stinger.\u201d\\n\\nThe gun stood in a separate fortress made of latticework. An ingenious little tarpaulin cover, shaped like an umbrella, protected it from the weather.\\n\\n\u201cThen, at the back,\u201d said Wemmick, \u201cout of sight, so it doesn\u2019t spoil the idea of the fortifications\u2014for I believe that if you have an idea, you should carry it out and maintain it\u2014I don\u2019t know whether you agree\u2014\u201d\\n\\nI said that I certainly did.\\n\\n\u201c\u2014At the back, there\u2019s a pig, along with chickens and rabbits. Then I put together my own little frame, you see, and grow cucumbers. You\u2019ll judge at supper what kind of salad I can produce. So, sir,\u201d said Wemmick, smiling again but also speaking seriously as he shook his head, \u201cif you imagine the little place under siege, it could last a devil of a long time for provisions.\u201d\\n\\nHe then led me to a bower about twelve yards away. It was reached by such cleverly twisting paths that it took quite a while to get there. In this retreat, our glasses had already been set out. Our punch was cooling in an ornamental lake beside which the bower stood. The lake was circular, with an island in the middle that might have supplied the salad for supper. Wemmick had built a fountain in it; when a small mill was set turning and a cork was removed from a pipe, the fountain played so strongly that it made the back of your hand quite wet.\"}"
