hour. At its first stroke, both his guides stopped and turned their heads toward the direction of the sound.\\n\\n\u201cEight o\u2019clock, Bill,\u201d Nancy said when the bell fell silent.\\n\\n\u201cWhat\u2019s the point of telling me? I can hear it, can\u2019t I?\u201d Sikes replied.\\n\\n\u201cI wonder whether they can hear it,\u201d said Nancy.\\n\\n\u201cOf course they can,\u201d Sikes answered. \u201cIt was Bartlemy time when I was locked up, and there wasn\u2019t a penny trumpet at the fair whose squealing I couldn\u2019t hear. After I was shut in for the night, the noise and uproar outside made that thundering old jail so silent that I could almost have beaten my brains out against the iron plates of the door.\u201d\"}"
