r his terrible work. He began wondering whether he and Basil Hallward had ever met, and, if they had, what impression they had formed of each other.\\n\\n\u201cLeave me now,\u201d said a stern voice behind him.\\n\\nHe turned and hurried out, only aware that the dead man had been pushed back into the chair and that Campbell was staring into a gleaming yellow face. As he went downstairs, he heard the key turning in the lock.\\n\\nIt was well after seven when Campbell returned to the library. He was pale, but perfectly composed. \u201cI have done what you asked me to do,\u201d he muttered.\"}"
