s jackboots, where the butler found it the next morning. Once safely inside his own room, he threw himself onto a small pallet bed and hid his face beneath the blankets. After some time, however, the brave old Canterville spirit returned to him, and he decided to go and speak to the other ghost as soon as daylight came. So, just as dawn began to silver the hills, he went back toward the place where he had first seen the grim phantom. He felt that two ghosts were better than one and that, with his new friend\u2019s help, he might safely face the twins.\"}"
