n overcame him. Were these children of sin and misery destined to their ends, just as he was destined to his? Were they, like him, only puppets in some monstrous spectacle?\\n\\nYet it was not the mystery of suffering but its comedy that impressed him: its utter uselessness, its grotesque lack of meaning. How disjointed everything appeared! How little harmony there was anywhere! He marvelled at the discord between the shallow optimism of the age and the actual facts of existence. He was still very young.\\n\\nAfter some time he found himself before Marylebone Church. The silent road resembled a long ribbon of polished silver, marked here and there by the dark arabesques of moving shadows.\"}"
