irable servant; but, generally speaking, he preferred him to his own brothers and sisters and honoured him more than his own father and mother. He confidently called on the jury to do the same. The evidence of these two witnesses, together with the documents they had discovered, would show that the prisoner had received lists of His Majesty\u2019s forces and their positions and preparations, by sea and land. It would leave no doubt that he had regularly passed such information to a hostile power.\"}"
