d her skirts out of harm\u2019s way. The boy fled at once, scrambled up the tall board fence, and vanished over it.\\n\\nHis Aunt Polly stood astonished for a moment, then began to laugh softly.\\n\\n\u201cDamn that boy, can\u2019t I ever learn? Hasn\u2019t he played tricks like that on me often enough for me to watch out by now? But old fools are the greatest fools there are. You can\u2019t teach an old dog new tricks, as they say. But goodness, he never plays the same trick two days in a row, and how is anyone supposed to know what\u2019s coming? He seems to know exactly how long he can torment me before I lose my temper, and he knows that if he can distract me for a minute or make me laugh, it all fades away and I can\u2019t strike him once.\u201d\"}"
