          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"04136a991a45108cdcee9f01\",\"rewritten_text\":\"But do not imagine that I did not consider it an evil in itself.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBelieve me, they were all perfectly comfortable.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI might not like them any better for that, perhaps. So many women and children have no _right_ to be comfortable aboard ship.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Frederick, you are talking complete nonsense. What would become of us poor sailors\u2019 wives, who often need to be carried to one port or another to join our husbands, if everyone shared your feelings?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy feelings, as you see, did not stop me from taking Mrs Harville and her entire family to Plymouth.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut I hate to hear you speak like such a gentleman, as though women were all delicate ladies instead of rational creatures. None of us expects smooth water throughout our lives.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAh, my dear,\u201d said the Admiral, \u201conce he has a wife, he will sing a different tune. If he marries, and we are fortunate enough to live through another war, we shall see him do as you and I, and many others, have done. We shall see him deeply grateful to anyone who brings him his wife.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, we shall.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNow I am finished,\u201d cried Captain Wentworth. \u201cWhenever married people begin attacking me with, \u2018Oh, you will think very differently when you are married,\u2019 I can only answer, \u2018No, I shall not.\u2019 Then they say again, \u2018Yes, you will,\u2019 and that ends the matter.\u201d\\n\\nHe rose and moved away.\\n\\n\u201cYou must have been a great traveller, ma\u2019am!\u201d said Mrs Musgrove to Mrs Croft.\\n\\n\u201cFairly so, ma\u2019am, during the fifteen years of my marriage, though many women have travelled farther. I have crossed the Atlantic four times, and gone once to the East Indies and back; besides visiting various places nearer home: Cork, Lisbon, and Gibraltar. But I never went beyond the Straits, and was never in the West Indies. We do not count Bermuda or the Bahamas as the West Indies, you know.\u201d\\n\\nMrs Musgrove had nothing to say in disagreement; she could not accuse herself of ever having called them anything at all during her life.\\n\\n\u201cAnd I assure you, ma\u2019am,\u201d Mrs Croft continued, \u201cthat nothing can surpass the accommodations aboard a man-of-war; I speak, of course, of the higher rates. In a frigate, naturally, you are more confined, though any reasonable woman may be perfectly happy in one; and I can safely say that the happiest part of my life was spent aboard ship. While we were together, you know, there was nothing to fear.\u201d\"}"
