          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"bcd5b46acd82186bcf6d2b1b\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cStop the starboard! Ting-a-ling-ling! Stop the larboard! Come ahead on the starboard! Stop her! Let your outside paddle turn slowly! Ting-a-ling-ling! Chow-ow-ow! Get that head-line out! Quickly now! Come\u2014get out your spring-line\u2014what are you doing there! Take a turn around that stump with the bight of it! Stand by that stage, now\u2014let her go! Engines stopped, sir! Ting-a-ling-ling! SH\u2019T! S\u2019H\u2019T! SH\u2019T!\u201d (testing the gauge cocks).\\n\\nTom kept whitewashing, paying no attention to the steamboat. Ben stared for a moment, then said: \u201cHi-Yi! You\u2019re stuck, aren\u2019t you!\u201d\\n\\nThere was no answer. Tom examined his last stroke with an artist\u2019s eye, then gave his brush another gentle sweep and studied the result as before. Ben moved alongside him. Tom\u2019s mouth watered for the apple, but he stayed with his work. Ben said:\\n\\n\u201cHello, old fellow, you have to work, do you?\u201d\\n\\nTom turned suddenly and said:\\n\\n\u201cWhy, it\u2019s you, Ben! I wasn\u2019t paying attention.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSay\u2014I\u2019m going swimming. Don\u2019t you wish you could? But of course you\u2019d rather work, wouldn\u2019t you? Of course you would!\u201d\\n\\nTom considered the boy for a moment, then said:\\n\\n\u201cWhat do you call work?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, isn\u2019t that work?\u201d\\n\\nTom went back to whitewashing and answered casually:\\n\\n\u201cWell, maybe it is, and maybe it isn\u2019t. All I know is, it suits Tom Sawyer.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, come on, you don\u2019t mean to pretend that you like it?\u201d\\n\\nThe brush kept moving.\\n\\n\u201cLike it? Well, I don\u2019t see why I shouldn\u2019t. Does a boy get the chance to whitewash a fence every day?\u201d\\n\\nThat made the matter look different. Ben stopped nibbling his apple. Tom moved his brush delicately back and forth, stepped back to judge the effect, added a touch here and there, and criticized the result again. Ben watched every movement, becoming more and more interested and absorbed. At last he said:\\n\\n\u201cSay, Tom, let me whitewash a little.\u201d\\n\\nTom thought it over and was about to agree, but changed his mind:\\n\\n\u201cNo\u2014no\u2014I don\u2019t think it would do, Ben. You see, Aunt Polly is extremely particular about this fence\u2014it\u2019s right here on the street, you know\u2014but if it were the back fence, I wouldn\u2019t mind, and she wouldn\u2019t either. Yes, she\u2019s extremely particular about this fence; it has to be done very carefully. I suppose there isn\u2019t one boy in a thousand, maybe two thousand, who can do it the way it has to be done.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo\u2014is that so? Oh, come on\u2014let me just try. Only a little\u2014I\u2019d let you if you were me, Tom.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBen, I\u2019d like to, honestly; but Aunt Polly\u2014well, Jim wanted to do it, but she wouldn\u2019t let him; Sid wanted to do it, and she wouldn\u2019t let Sid.\u201d\"}"
