          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"509a1fcc6c1ad67f4826c5fa\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Their arrival had kindled a sort of fire in the heart of Saint Antoine, spreading quickly as they passed, stirring and flickering into flames of faces at most doors and windows. Yet no one had followed them, and no man spoke when they entered the wine-shop, though every eye there turned toward them.\\n\\n\u201cGood day, gentlemen!\u201d said Monsieur Defarge.\\n\\nIt may have been a signal that loosened the general tongue. It drew an answering chorus of \u201cGood day!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt is bad weather, gentlemen,\u201d said Defarge, shaking his head.\\n\\nAt this, every man looked at his neighbour, then all lowered their eyes and sat in silence. Except one man, who rose and went out.\\n\\n\u201cMy wife,\u201d said Defarge aloud, addressing Madame Defarge, \u201cI have travelled several leagues with this good road-mender, called Jacques. I met him\u2014by accident\u2014a day and a half\u2019s journey from Paris. He is a good child, this road-mender called Jacques. Give him something to drink, my wife!\u201d\\n\\nA second man rose and went out. Madame Defarge placed wine before the road-mender called Jacques. He removed his blue cap to the company and drank. In the breast of his blouse he carried some coarse dark bread; from time to time he ate it, sitting near Madame Defarge\u2019s counter, munching and drinking. A third man rose and went out.\\n\\nDefarge refreshed himself with a draught of wine\u2014but took less than he gave the stranger, since wine was no rarity to him\u2014and stood waiting until the countryman had finished his breakfast. He looked at no one present, and now no one looked at him; not even Madame Defarge, who had taken up her knitting and was working.\\n\\n\u201cHave you finished your meal, friend?\u201d he asked, when the time came.\\n\\n\u201cYes, thank you.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCome, then! You shall see the room I told you that you could occupy. It will suit you