          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"4603c6eaf350a46b596ce5c5\",\"rewritten_text\":\"There was something so remarkable in the growing intensity of Mr. Wopsle\u2019s gaze, and he seemed to be turning so many thoughts over in his mind and becoming so confused, that I could not understand it. I sat thinking about it long after he had risen into the clouds inside a large watch-case, and still I could not understand it. I was still thinking of it when I left the theatre an hour later and found him waiting for me near the door.\\n\\n\u201cHow are you?\u201d I said, shaking hands with him as we turned down the street together. \u201cI saw that you saw me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSaw you, Mr. Pip!\u201d he replied. \u201cYes, of course I saw you. But who else was there?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWho else?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt is the strangest thing,\u201d said Mr. Wopsle, slipping back into his bewildered expression; \u201cand yet I could swear to him.\u201d\\n\\nAlarmed, I begged Mr. Wopsle to explain what he meant.\\n\\n\u201cWhether I would have noticed him at first if you had not been there,\u201d said Mr. Wopsle, continuing in the same bewildered manner, \u201cI cannot say for certain; yet I think I would have.\u201d\\n\\nWithout meaning to, I looked around me, as I had grown accustomed to do on my way home; for these mysterious words sent a chill through me.\\n\\n\u201cOh! He cannot be in sight,\u201d said Mr. Wopsle. \u201cHe left before I did. I saw him go.\u201d\\n\\nBecause I had reason to be suspicious, I even suspected the poor actor. I feared he was trying to trap me into making some admission. So I watched him as we walked on together, but said nothing.\\n\\n\u201cI had the absurd idea that he must be with you, Mr. Pip, until I saw that you were completely unaware of him, sitting behind you there like a ghost.\u201d\\n\\nThe chill I had felt before came over me again, but I was determined not to speak yet, since his words were entirely consistent with his being instructed to make me connect these hints with Provis. Naturally, I was completely certain and secure in knowing that Provis had not been there.\\n\\n\u201cI expect you wonder at me, Mr. Pip; indeed, I can see that you do. But it is so strange! You will scarcely believe what I am about to tell you. I could hardly believe it myself if you told it to me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cReally?\u201d I said.\\n\\n\u201cNo, truly. Mr. Pip, you remember, long ago, a certain Christmas Day, when you were a small child, and I dined at Gargery\u2019s, and some soldiers came to the door to have a pair of handcuffs repaired?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI remember it very well.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd you remember that two convicts were being pursued, and that we joined the chase, and that Gargery carried you on his back, while I led the way, and you kept up with me as well as you could?\u201d\"}"
