          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"6cac0415a658db44a3a286f9\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cIf I can\u2019t live on that, I shan\u2019t ask anyone to give me a lift. Is that satisfactory?\u201d\\n\\nThere was a tremendous roar of applause. Above it, the king\u2019s voice rang out:\\n\\n\u201cAway with his bonds, and set him free! Let everyone, high and low, rich and poor, honor him, for he has become the king\u2019s right hand. He is clothed with power and authority, and his seat is on the highest step of the throne! Now drive away this creeping night and bring back the light and cheer, so that all the world may bless you.\u201d\\n\\nBut I said:\\n\\n\u201cThat a common man should be shamed before the world is nothing. But it would dishonor the _king_ if anyone who saw his minister naked did not also see him freed from that shame. If I might ask that my clothes be brought back\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThey are not suitable,\u201d the king interrupted. \u201cFetch clothing of another kind; dress him like a prince!\u201d\\n\\nMy plan had worked. I wanted to keep matters as they were until the eclipse became total. Otherwise, they would keep trying to make me end the darkness, and of course I could not do that. Sending for the clothes bought some time, but not enough. So I needed another excuse. I said it would be natural for the king to change his mind and regret, at least partly, what he had done in his excitement. Therefore, I would let the darkness deepen for a while; if, after a reasonable time, the king still held to his decision, the darkness would be dismissed. Neither the king nor anyone else was satisfied with this arrangement, but I had to stand firm.\\n\\nIt grew darker and darker, blacker and blacker, while I struggled with those awkward sixth-century clothes. At last it became completely dark, and the crowd groaned in horror as cold, unnatural night breezes moved through the place and the stars appeared and twinkled overhead. At last the eclipse was total, and I was very glad, though everyone else was miserable\u2014which was only natural. I said:\\n\\n\u201cThe king, by remaining silent, still accepts the terms.\u201d Then I raised my hands and stood that way for a moment. After that I said, with the deepest solemnity: \u201cLet the enchantment dissolve and pass away harmlessly!\u201d\\n\\nFor a moment there was no response in the deep darkness and graveyard silence. But when the sun\u2019s silver rim appeared again a moment or two later, the crowd burst into a huge shout and came rushing down like a flood, smothering me with blessings and gratitude. And Clarence was certainly not the last of them.\"}"
