          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"4be747a60a674a273512d773\",\"rewritten_text\":\"WHEN the wedding was held, about three weeks later, St. Peter\u2019s was packed with a perfect crowd of fashionable people. The Dean of Chichester conducted the service with the greatest impressiveness, and everyone agreed that they had never seen a more handsome bride and bridegroom. They were not merely handsome, however\u2014they were happy. Lord Arthur never once regretted all he had endured for Sybil, while she, for her part, gave him the finest gifts a woman can offer a man\u2014worship, tenderness, and love. Reality had not destroyed their romance. They always felt young.\\n\\nSeveral years later, after two lovely children had been born to them, Lady Windermere visited Alton Priory, a beautiful old house that the Duke had given his son as a wedding present. One afternoon, while sitting with Lady Arthur beneath a lime-tree in the garden and watching the little boy and girl dart along the rose-walk like wandering sunbeams, she suddenly took her hostess\u2019s hand and asked, \u2018Are you happy, Sybil?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Dear Lady Windermere, of course I am happy. Aren\u2019t you?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018I have no time for happiness, Sybil. I always take a fancy to the last person introduced to me; but generally, once I know people, I grow tired of them.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Don\u2019t your lions keep you satisfied, Lady Windermere?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Oh, no! Lions are useful for only one season. Once their manes have been cut, they are the dullest creatures alive. Besides, if you are genuinely kind to them, they behave very badly. Do you remember that dreadful Mr. Podgers? He was a terrible impostor. Naturally, I did not care about that, and I even forgave him when he asked to borrow money, but I could not endure his making love to me. He has made me detest cheiromancy. I practise telepathy now. It is far more entertaining.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018You must not say anything against cheiromancy here, Lady Windermere; it is the one subject Arthur does not like people to joke about. I assure you, he takes it quite seriously.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018You cannot mean that he believes in it, Sybil?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Ask him, Lady Windermere\u2014there he is\u2019; and Lord Arthur came up the garden carrying a large bunch of yellow roses, with his two children dancing around him.\\n\\n\u2018Lord Arthur?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Yes, Lady Windermere.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018You cannot mean that you believe in cheiromancy?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Of course I do,\u2019 said the young man with a smile.\\n\\n\u2018But why?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Because I owe it all the happiness of my life,\u2019 he murmured, sinking into a wicker chair.\"}"
