r their complete union. Woodville\u2019s fame continued to grow, while Elinor became more beautiful and wise under the guidance of her gifted lover.\\n\\nIn two months Elinor would be twenty-one, and everything was ready for their marriage. How can I describe the disaster that followed such joy? Yet the earth would not be the sorrowful, blighted place it is if a pair of such angelic beings had been allowed to live entirely for each other. Search the whole world, and you will not find the perfect happiness their marriage would have brought them. The order of things among us miserable inhabitants of earth would have had to change before such complete joy could be permitted.\"}"
