ned home and entered the house, where I presented myself to the family. My haggard, wild appearance caused great alarm, but I answered no questions and scarcely spoke. I felt as though I had been placed under a curse\u2014as though I had no right to ask for their sympathy, and could never again enjoy their company.\"}"
