          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"ecd8bf3338673b52c7f92cfd\",\"rewritten_text\":\"There was something so extraordinary in the growing brightness of Mr. Wopsle\u2019s eye, and he appeared to be turning over so many matters in his mind while becoming increasingly bewildered, that I could not understand it. I sat pondering it long after he had risen into the clouds inside a large watch-case, and still could not understand it. I was thinking of it still when I left the theatre an hour later and found him waiting for me by the door.\\n\\n\u201cHow do you do?\u201d I asked, shaking his hand as we walked down the street together. \u201cI saw that you saw me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSaw you, Mr. Pip!\u201d he replied. \u201cYes, naturally I saw you. But who else was there?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWho else?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt is the strangest thing,\u201d said Mr. Wopsle, slipping once more into his absent expression; \u201cand yet I could swear to him.\u201d\\n\\nGrowing alarmed, I begged Mr. Wopsle to explain what he meant.\\n\\n\u201cWhether I should have observed him at first if you had not been there,\u201d said Mr. Wopsle, continuing in the same distracted manner, \u201cI cannot say for certain; but I believe I should.\u201d\\n\\nWithout meaning to, I looked around, as I was used to do on my way home; for these mysterious words sent a chill through me.\\n\\n\u201cOh! He cannot be visible now,\u201d said Mr. Wopsle. \u201cHe left before I did. I saw him go.\u201d\\n\\nGiven the reason I had for suspicion, I even suspected the poor actor himself. I feared he meant to trap me into some confession. So I watched him as we walked on together, but remained silent.\\n\\n\u201cI had the absurd notion that he must be with you, Mr. Pip, until I saw that you were entirely unaware of him, sitting behind you there like a ghost.\u201d\\n\\nThe earlier chill passed over me again, but I determined not to speak yet, since his words were quite compatible with the possibility that he had been prompted to make me connect these allusions with Provis. Naturally, I was completely certain and secure in knowing that Provis had not been there.\\n\\n\u201cI expect you wonder at me, Mr. Pip; indeed, I can see that you do. But it is so very strange! You will scarcely believe what I am about to tell you. I could hardly believe it myself, had you told it to me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIndeed?\u201d I said.\\n\\n\u201cNo, indeed. Mr. Pip, you remember, long ago, a particular Christmas Day, when you were still a child, and I dined at Gargery\u2019s, and some soldiers came to the door to have a pair of handcuffs repaired?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI remember it very well.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd you remember there was a pursuit of two convicts, and that we joined it, and that Gargery carried you on his back, while I led the way, and you kept up with me as best you could?\u201d\"}"
