e was dressed, he entered the library and sat down to the light French breakfast arranged for him on a small round table beside the open window. It was a perfect day. The warm air seemed scented with spices. A bee flew in and buzzed around the blue-dragon bowl before him, filled with sulphur-yellow roses. He felt entirely happy.\\n\\nThen his gaze suddenly fell upon the screen he had set before the portrait, and he started.\\n\\n\u201cIs it too cold for Monsieur?\u201d asked his valet, placing an omelette on the table. \u201cShall I close the window?\u201d\\n\\nDorian shook his head. \u201cI am not cold,\u201d he murmured.\"}"
