 any change in her manner that might provoke a remonstrance from him. Escaping all inquiry or public notice was of great importance to her; but she meant to be as decidedly cool towards him as their relationship allowed, and to withdraw, as quietly as possible, the few unnecessary steps of intimacy along which she had gradually been drawn. Accordingly, she was more reserved and cooler than she had been the previous evening.\\n\\nHe wished to revive her curiosity about how and where he might formerly have heard her praised; he greatly desired the satisfaction of being pressed for further information. But the spell was broken: he discovered that the warmth and excitement of a public room were needed to kindle his modest cousin\u2019s vanity; at least, he found that it could not now be accomplished by any of the attempts he might venture amid the more commanding claims of the others.\"}"
