          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"02c59a0d5580e2b595cf4aa2\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cBut do not imagine that I did not consider it an evil in itself.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBelieve me, they were all perfectly comfortable.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI might not like them better for that. Such a number of women and children have no right to be comfortable on board.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Frederick, you are talking nonsense. What would become of us poor sailors\u2019 wives, who often need to be carried to one port or another after our husbands, if everyone felt as you do?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy feelings, you see, did not stop me from taking Mrs Harville and all her family to Plymouth.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut I hate to hear you speak like such a fine gentleman, as if women were all delicate ladies instead of sensible creatures. None of us expect calm seas all our lives.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAh, my dear,\u201d said the Admiral, \u201cwhen he has a wife, he will sing a different tune. If he is married, and we are lucky enough to live through another war, we shall see him do as you and I, and many others, have done. We shall see him very grateful to anyone who brings him his wife.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, we shall.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNow I have finished,\u201d cried Captain Wentworth. \u201cWhenever married people begin attacking me with, \u2018Oh, you will think very differently when you are married,\u2019 I can only say, \u2018No, I shall not.\u2019 Then they say again, \u2018Yes, you will,\u2019 and that ends the matter.\u201d\\n\\nHe rose and moved away.\\n\\n\u201cWhat a great traveller you must have been, ma\u2019am!\u201d said Mrs Musgrove to Mrs Croft.\\n\\n\u201cQuite a traveller, ma\u2019am, during the fifteen years of my marriage, though many women have travelled more. I have crossed the Atlantic four times, gone once to the East Indies and back, and visited various places nearer home: Cork, Lisbon, and Gibraltar. But I never went beyond the Straits, and I was never in the West Indies. Bermuda and the Bahamas are not called the West Indies, you know.\u201d\\n\\nMrs Musgrove had nothing to say against this; she could not accuse herself of ever having called them anything at all in her life.\\n\\n\u201cAnd I assure you, ma\u2019am,\u201d Mrs Croft continued, \u201cthat nothing can match the comfort of a man-of-war. I mean, of course, the larger ships. In a frigate, you are more confined; still, any reasonable woman may be perfectly happy in one. I can safely say that the happiest part of my life was spent on board a ship. While we were together, you know, there was nothing to fear.\u201d\"}"
