          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"46698065af88293d52687bf0\",\"rewritten_text\":\"The insect was remarkably heavy, and, considering everything, I could hardly blame Jupiter for his opinion of it. But I could not understand, no matter how hard I tried, why Legrand agreed with him.\\n\\n\u201cI sent for you,\u201d he said grandly, after I had finished examining the beetle, \u201cso that I might have your advice and help in carrying out the plans of Fate and the bug\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Legrand,\u201d I cried, interrupting him, \u201cyou are clearly unwell and should take some precautions. You must go to bed, and I will stay with you for a few days, until you recover. You are feverish and\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cFeel my pulse,\u201d he said.\\n\\nI did so and, to tell the truth, found no sign of fever at all.\\n\\n\u201cBut you may be ill without having a fever. Let me prescribe for you this once. First, go to bed. Then\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou are mistaken,\u201d he interrupted. \u201cI am as well as I can be, considering the excitement I am suffering. If you truly wish to help me, you will relieve that excitement.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd how can that be done?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cVery easily. Jupiter and I are going on an expedition into the hills on the mainland, and we will need the help of someone we can trust. You are the only person we can rely on. Whether we succeed or fail, the excitement you see in me will be calmed.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI am willing to help you in any way,\u201d I replied, \u201cbut do you mean that this cursed beetle has something to do with your expedition into the hills?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt does.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen, Legrand, I cannot take part in such an absurd plan.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI am sorry\u2014very sorry\u2014for we will have to attempt it alone.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAttempt it alone! The man must be mad! But wait\u2014how long do you expect to be gone?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cProbably all night. We will leave at once and return, in any case, by sunrise.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd will you promise me, on your honor, that when this strange idea is over, and the beetle matter\u2014good God!\u2014has been settled to your satisfaction, you will come home and follow my advice exactly, as you would that of your doctor?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, I promise. Now let us go, for we have no time to waste.\u201d\\n\\nWith a heavy heart, I went with my friend. We set out at about four o\u2019clock\u2014Legrand, Jupiter, the dog, and me. Jupiter carried the scythe and spades, insisting on carrying all of them. It seemed to me that he did so more because he was afraid to leave either tool within his master\u2019s reach than because of any special willingness or helpfulness.\"}"
