n could rouse him. I had planned to spend the night at the hut, as I had often done before, but seeing my host in this state, I thought it best to leave. He did not ask me to stay, but as I departed, he shook my hand with even greater warmth than usual.\\n\\nAbout a month later\u2014and during that time I had seen nothing of Legrand\u2014I was visited in Charleston by his servant, Jupiter. I had never seen the good old Black man look so dejected, and I feared that some serious misfortune had overtaken my friend.\"}"
