erce seas around the Cape, I might finally moor my worn skiff in a creek shaded by the fragrant groves of the spice-scented islands in the distant Indian Ocean.\\n\\nThese are wild dreams. Yet ever since they came to me a week ago, as I stood on the heights of St. Peter\u2019s, they have governed my imagination. I have chosen my boat and gathered my meager supplies. I have selected a few books; the chief among them are Homer and Shakespeare. But the libraries of the world are open to me, and in any port I can replenish my collection. I do not expect my circumstances to improve; but the monotonous present has become unbearable.\"}"
        }
