          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"6bcf7492df0a3b0035b71db3\",\"rewritten_text\":\"I went from shop to shop, buying what was needed to change his appearance. When that was done, I made my way to Little Britain. Mr. Jaggers was at his desk, but when he saw me enter, he rose at once and stood in front of the fire.\\n\\n\u201cNow, Pip,\u201d he said, \u201cbe careful.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI will, sir,\u201d I replied. On the way there, I had thought carefully about what I meant to say.\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t involve yourself,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, \u201cand don\u2019t involve anyone else. You understand\u2014anyone. Don\u2019t tell me anything: I don\u2019t want to know anything; I\u2019m not curious.\u201d\\n\\nOf course, I understood that he knew the man had arrived.\\n\\n\u201cI only want, Mr. Jaggers,\u201d I said, \u201cto make sure that what I have been told is true. I have no hope that it is false, but at least I can confirm it.\u201d\\n\\nMr. Jaggers nodded. \u201cBut did you say \u2018told\u2019 or \u2018informed\u2019?\u201d he asked, tilting his head. He did not look at me, but listened toward the floor. \u201cTold suggests that it was said directly. You can\u2019t have spoken directly with a man in New South Wales, you know.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI will say, informed, Mr. Jaggers.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGood.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have been informed by a person named Abel Magwitch that he is the benefactor who has been unknown to me for so long.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat is the man,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, \u201cin New South Wales.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd no one else?\u201d I asked.\\n\\n\u201cAnd no one else,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers.\\n\\n\u201cI am not so unreasonable, sir, as to hold you responsible for my mistakes and false conclusions; but I always believed it was Miss Havisham.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAs you say, Pip,\u201d replied Mr. Jaggers, turning his cool eyes on me and biting his forefinger, \u201cI am not responsible for that.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd yet it seemed so much like it, sir,\u201d I pleaded, my heart sinking.\\n\\n\u201cNot the slightest evidence, Pip,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, shaking his head and gathering up his coat. \u201cTrust nothing because of how it looks; trust everything because of the evidence. There is no better rule.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have nothing more to say,\u201d I said with a sigh, after standing silent for a while. \u201cI have confirmed what I was told, and that is the end of it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd Magwitch\u2014in New South Wales\u2014having finally revealed himself,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, \u201cyou will understand, Pip, how strictly, in all my dealings with you, I have kept to the facts. I have never departed in the least from the facts. You know that perfectly well?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cPerfectly, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhen Magwitch first wrote to me\u2014from New South Wales\u2014I told him\u2014from New South Wales\u2014that he must never expect me to depart from the strict facts.\u201d\"}"
