{"request_id":"8b6d6ea0a1bc5bae4ed8c071","rewritten_text":"After this, a few more loops were unfastened from the rim, another section of cloth was brought forward, and the freed loops were attached to their proper buttons. In this way, the entire upper part of the bag could be placed between the netting and the hoop. The hoop would now fall inside the car, while the whole weight of the car and everything in it would be supported only by the buttons. At first this might seem unsafe, but it was not. The buttons were very strong, and they were so close together that each one carried only a small part of the total weight. Indeed, even if the car and its contents had been three times heavier, I would not have felt uneasy. I then raised the hoop again inside the gum-elastic covering and supported it at nearly its former height with three light poles prepared for the purpose. This kept the bag stretched at the top and held the lower part of the netting in its proper position. The only task left was to close the opening of the enclosure. This was easily done by gathering the folds of material and twisting them very tightly inward with a kind of fixed tourniquet.

“In the sides of the covering, now fitted around the car, were three circular panes of thick, clear glass. Through them I could see without difficulty in every horizontal direction. A fourth window of the same kind had been placed in the cloth forming the bottom, directly above a small opening in the floor of the car. This allowed me to look straight downward. I had found it impossible to install a similar device overhead because of the unusual way the opening there had to be closed and the wrinkles this caused in the cloth. I therefore could not expect to see anything directly above me. This mattered little, since even if I had been able to place a window there, the balloon itself would have blocked my view.

“About a foot below one of the side windows was a circular opening eight inches across. It had a brass rim whose inner edge was threaded like a screw. The large tube of the condenser was screwed into this rim, while the body of the machine remained inside the gum-elastic chamber.”"}

