          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"c75544e8da71c0bca8fdc5f5\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cWell, everybody does it that way, Huck.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTom, it don\u2019t make any difference. I ain\u2019t everybody, and I can\u2019t _stand_ it. It\u2019s terrible being tied down like that. And grub comes too easy\u2014I don\u2019t take no interest in vittles that way. I got to ask before I go fishing; I got to ask before I go swimming\u2014dern\u2019d if I ain\u2019t got to ask to do everything. Why, I had to talk so proper it wasn\u2019t any comfort\u2014I had to go up in the attic and rip out for a spell every day, just to get a taste in my mouth, or I\u2019d have died, Tom. The widder wouldn\u2019t let me smoke; she wouldn\u2019t let me yell, gape, stretch, or scratch in front of folks\u2014\u201d [Then, with a sudden fit of particular irritation and hurt]\u2014\u201cAnd dad fetch it, she prayed all the time! I never saw such a woman! I _had_ to shove, Tom\u2014I simply had to. And besides, school\u2019s going to start, and I\u2019d have had to go\u2014well, I wouldn\u2019t stand _that_, Tom. Looky-here, Tom, being rich ain\u2019t all it\u2019s cracked up to be. It\u2019s nothing but worry and worry, sweat and sweat, and wishing you was dead every minute. Now these clothes suit me, and this bar\u2019l suits me, and I ain\u2019t ever going to give \u2019em up again. Tom, I\u2019d never have got into all this trouble if it hadn\u2019t been for that money; so you just take my share along with yours, and give me a ten-center now and then\u2014not often, because I don\u2019t give a dern for anything unless it\u2019s tolerable hard to get\u2014and you go beg the widder off for me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, Huck, you know I can\u2019t do that. \u2019Tain\u2019t fair; and besides, if you\u2019ll stick with it a little longer, you\u2019ll come to like it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cLike it! Yes\u2014the way I\u2019d like a hot stove if I sat on it long enough. No, Tom, I won\u2019t be rich,