          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"f749d158ae65ad4410ed6d90\",\"rewritten_text\":\"But in that bitter _tirade_ against Chantilly, which appeared in yesterday\u2019s \u2018_Mus\u00e9e_,\u2019 the satirist, making some disgraceful allusions to the cobbler\u2019s change of name when he took up the buskin, quoted a Latin line we had often discussed. I mean the line\\n\\nPerdidit antiquum litera prima sonum.\\n\\n\u201cI had told you that this referred to Orion, formerly written Urion; and, because of certain sharp points connected with this explanation, I knew you could not have forgotten it. It was therefore clear that you would inevitably connect the two ideas of Orion and Chantilly. That you had made the connection, I saw from the expression of the smile that crossed your lips. You were thinking of the poor cobbler\u2019s sacrifice. Until then, you had been stooping as you walked; but now I saw you straighten to your full height. I was certain that you were reflecting on Chantilly\u2019s small stature. At that moment I interrupted your thoughts by observing that, since he was in fact a very little man\u2014that Chantilly\u2014he would be better suited to the _Th\u00e9\u00e2tre des Vari\u00e9t\u00e9s_.\u201d\\n\\nSoon afterward, we were reading an evening edition of the \u201cGazette des Tribunaux,\u201d when the following paragraphs caught our attention.\\n\\n\u201c_Extraordinary Murders_.\u2014This morning, at about three o\u2019clock, the residents of the Quartier St. Roch were awakened by a series of terrible screams, apparently coming from the fourth floor of a house in the Rue Morgue, known to be occupied solely by Madame L\u2019Espanaye and her daughter, Mademoiselle Camille L\u2019Espanaye. After some delay, caused by an unsuccessful attempt to gain entry in the usual way, the gate was broken open with a crowbar, and eight or ten neighbors entered with two _gendarmes_. By then the cries had stopped; but as the group rushed up the first flight of stairs, two or more harsh voices, angrily arguing, were heard and seemed to come from the upper part of the house. When the second landing was reached, these sounds had also ceased, and everything was completely silent. The group spread out and hurried from room to room. On reaching a large rear chamber on the fourth floor, whose door was found locked with the key inside and was forced open, they saw a scene that filled everyone present with horror and astonishment alike.\\n\\n\u201cThe room was in the greatest disorder\u2014the furniture broken and scattered everywhere. There was only one bedstead; the bed had been taken from it and thrown into the middle of the floor. On a chair lay a razor smeared with blood.\"}"
