          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"533aba441cbbc794bdf2ff13\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Smallpox!\\n\\nI rushed to the king and said into his ear:\\n\\n\u201cOut the door at once, sire! The woman is dying of the disease that ravaged Camelot two years ago.\u201d\\n\\nHe did not move.\\n\\n\u201cIndeed, I shall remain\u2014and help as well.\u201d\\n\\nI whispered again:\\n\\n\u201cKing, you must not. You must leave.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou mean well, and you speak wisely enough. But it would be shameful for a king to show fear, and shameful for a knight in armor to withhold his hand where there are those in need of help. Be at peace; I will not go. You are the one who must leave. The Church\u2019s ban is not upon me, but it forbids you to be here, and it will deal harshly with you if word reaches it of your trespass.\u201d\\n\\nIt was a desperate position for him, and might cost him his life, but there was no use arguing. If he believed his knightly honor was at stake, that ended the matter; he would stay, and nothing could stop him. I knew that, and so I dropped the subject. The woman spoke:\\n\\n\u201cGood sir, out of your kindness, will you climb the ladder there and bring me news of what you find? Do not be afraid to tell me, for there are times when even a mother\u2019s heart is beyond breaking\u2014because it is already broken.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cStay,\u201d said the king, \u201cand give the woman something to eat. I will go.\u201d And he set down the knapsack.\\n\\nI turned to begin, but the king had already started. He stopped and looked down at a man lying in the dim light, who had not noticed us until then or spoken.\\n\\n\u201cIs he your husband?\u201d the king asked.\\n\\n\u201cYes.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIs he asleep?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThank God for that one mercy, yes\u2014for three hours now. Where can I fully repay my gratitude? My heart is bursting with it for the sleep he sleeps now.\u201d\\n\\nI said:\\n\\n\u201cWe will be careful. We will not wake him.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAh, no, you will not, for he is dead.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDead?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes. What a triumph it is to know it! No one can harm him, and no one can insult him again. He is in heaven now and happy; or, if not there, he remains in hell and is content, for in that place he will find neither abbot nor bishop. We were boy and girl together; we were man and wife for twenty-five years, and never separated until today. Think how long that is to love and suffer together. This morning he was out of his mind, and in his fancy we were boy and girl again, wandering through the happy fields. So, in that innocent, joyful conversation, he wandered farther and farther, still chatting lightly, and entered those other fields we know nothing of, where he was shut away from mortal sight.\"}"
