          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"43d3980f30a7f4b429b46c7b\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201c\u2018We have been to your residence,\u2019 said the first, \u2018and, unfortunately, did not find you there. We were told that you were probably walking in this direction, so we followed in the hope of catching up with you. Will you please enter the carriage?\u2019\\n\\n\u201cThe manner of both men was imperious, and as these words were spoken, they moved to place me between themselves and the carriage door. They were armed. I was not.\\n\\n\u201c\u2018Gentlemen,\u2019 I said, \u2018forgive me; but I generally ask who is doing me the honour of requesting my assistance, and what kind of case I am being summoned to attend.\u2019\\n\\n\u201cThe second speaker replied. \u2018Doctor, your clients are people of standing. As for the nature of the case, our confidence in your skill assures us that you will determine it more accurately than we could describe it. Enough. Will you please enter the carriage?\u2019\\n\\n\u201cI could do nothing but comply, and entered in silence. They followed me inside\u2014the last man leaping in after raising the steps. The carriage turned around and continued at its previous speed.\\n\\n\u201cI repeat this conversation exactly as it occurred. I have no doubt that it is the same word for word. I describe everything precisely as it happened, forcing my mind not to stray from the task. Where I make the broken marks that follow, I stop for the time being and place my paper in its hiding place.\\n\\n*****\\n\\n\u201cThe carriage left the streets behind, passed through the North Barrier, and emerged onto the country road. About two-thirds of a league beyond the Barrier\u2014it was not until later, when I traveled the route, that I estimated the distance\u2014it turned off the main avenue and soon stopped at an isolated house. All three of us got out and walked along a damp, soft path through a garden where an unattended fountain had overflowed, toward the house door. The door did not open at once when the bell was rung, and one of my two escorts struck the man who answered it across the face with his heavy riding glove.\\n\\n\u201cThere was nothing in this act that especially caught my attention, since I had seen ordinary people struck more often than dogs. But the other man, also angered, struck him in the same way with his arm. The brothers\u2019 expressions and manner were then so exactly alike that I realized for the first time that they were twins.\\n\\n\u201cFrom the moment we got out at the outer gate\u2014which we found locked, and which one brother opened to let us in before locking it again\u2014I had heard cries coming from an upper room.\"}"
