          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"3169746532903f71f411e65b\",\"rewritten_text\":\"And if he asked me why I wanted it, and why I believed I had any right to it, I would tell him\u2014though he cared little for such humble dreams\u2014that I had loved Estella deeply and for a long time, and that although I had lost her and must live a life of bereavement, anything connected with her was still nearer and dearer to me than anything else in the world. Seeing that Mr. Jaggers remained completely still and silent, apparently unmoved by my appeal, I turned to Wemmick and said, \u201cWemmick, I know you are a man with a gentle heart. I have seen your pleasant home, your old father, and all the innocent, cheerful, playful ways in which you renew yourself after your business life. I beg you to say a word for me to Mr. Jaggers, and to point out to him that, considering everything, he ought to be more open with me!\u201d\\n\\nI have never seen two men look at each other more strangely than Mr. Jaggers and Wemmick did after this appeal. At first, I feared that Wemmick would be dismissed from his employment at once; but that fear faded when I saw Mr. Jaggers soften into something like a smile, and Wemmick grow more confident.\\n\\n\u201cWhat is all this?\u201d said Mr. Jaggers. \u201cYou, with an old father, and you, with pleasant and playful ways?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell!\u201d Wemmick replied. \u201cIf I don\u2019t bring them here, what does it matter?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cPip,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, placing his hand on my arm and smiling openly, \u201cthis man must be the most cunning impostor in all London.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot at all,\u201d Wemmick replied, growing bolder still. \u201cI think you\u2019re another.\u201d\\n\\nAgain they exchanged the same strange looks, each apparently still uncertain whether the other was making fun of him.\\n\\n\u201cYou, with a pleasant home?\u201d said Mr. Jaggers.\\n\\n\u201cSince it doesn\u2019t interfere with business,\u201d Wemmick replied, \u201clet it be so. Now, looking at you, sir, I shouldn\u2019t be surprised if you were planning and arranging to have a pleasant home of your own one of these days, when you\u2019ve grown tired of all this work.\u201d\\n\\nMr. Jaggers nodded thoughtfully two or three times and actually sighed. \u201cPip,\u201d he said, \u201cwe won\u2019t speak of \u2018poor dreams\u2019; you know more about such matters than I do, having much fresher experience of them. But now, about this other matter. I\u2019ll put a case to you. Mind! I admit nothing.\u201d\\n\\nHe waited for me to say that I fully understood he had expressly stated that he admitted nothing.\\n\\n\u201cNow, Pip,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, \u201csuppose this case. Suppose a woman, in circumstances such as you have described, kept her child concealed and was forced to tell the fact to her legal adviser, because he had represented to her that, considering the scope of his defense, he needed to know the truth about that child.\"}"
