 ran, scrambled over the tall board fence, and vanished on the other side.\\n\\nHis Aunt Polly stood stunned for a moment, then began to laugh softly.\\n\\n\u201cDamn that boy, can\u2019t I ever learn? Hasn\u2019t he played tricks like that on me often enough for me to watch out by now? But old fools are the biggest fools there are. You can\u2019t teach an old dog new tricks, as they say. But goodness, he never plays the same trick two days in a row, so how is anyone supposed to know what he\u2019ll do? He seems to know exactly how long he can torment me before I lose my temper, and he knows that if he can distract me for a minute or make me laugh, my anger disappears and I can\u2019t hit him even once.\u201d\"}"
