          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"5046e7a8d62815e3cc3d7647\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cWhat\u2019s the trouble?\u201d\\n\\nI said:\\n\\n\u201cPap, and Mam, and Sis, and\u2014\u201d\\n\\nThen I broke down. He said:\\n\\n\u201cOh, dang it, don\u2019t take on so; we all have our troubles, and this one will turn out all right. What\u2019s the matter with them?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThey\u2019re\u2014they\u2019re\u2014are you the watchman of the boat?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes,\u201d he said, looking quite pleased with himself. \u201cI\u2019m the captain, owner, mate, pilot, watchman, and head deckhand; and sometimes I\u2019m the freight and passengers too. I\u2019m not as rich as old Jim Hornback, and I can\u2019t be as generous and good to Tom, Dick, and Harry as he is, throwing money around the way he does; but I\u2019ve told him many a time that I wouldn\u2019t trade places with him. A sailor\u2019s life is the life for me, I say, and I\u2019m darned if I\u2019d live two miles out of town, where nothing ever happens, not for all his money and as much more besides. I say\u2014\u201d\\n\\nI interrupted him and said:\\n\\n\u201cThey\u2019re in terrible trouble, and\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWho is?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, Pap and Mam and Sis and Miss Hooker; and if you\u2019d take your ferryboat and go up there\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cUp where? Where are they?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOn the wreck.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat wreck?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, there\u2019s only one.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat, you don\u2019t mean the Walter Scott?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGood land! What are they doing there, for goodness\u2019 sake?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, they didn\u2019t go there on purpose.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI bet they didn\u2019t! Why, great goodness, they have no chance if they don\u2019t get off mighty quick! How in the world did they ever get into such a mess?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cEasy enough. Miss Hooker was visiting up at the town\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, Booth\u2019s Landing\u2014go on.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cShe was visiting there at Booth\u2019s Landing, and just as evening began, she started across in the horse ferry with her Black woman to spend the night at her friend\u2019s house, Miss What-you-may-call-her\u2014I\u2019ve forgotten her name. They lost their steering oar, swung around, and floated downstream, stern first, for about two miles. Then they struck the wreck, and the ferryman, the Black woman, and the horses were all lost, but Miss Hooker grabbed hold and got aboard the wreck. About an hour after dark, we came downstream in our trading scow. It was so dark that we didn\u2019t see the wreck until we were right on it, and then we struck it too. But all of us were saved except Bill Whipple\u2014and oh, he was the best creature! I almost wish it had been me, I really do.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy goodness! It\u2019s the strangest thing I ever heard.\u201d\"}"
