ee them again\u2014for until she married last October, she had never been away from them for even a week, which must make it very strange to be in different kingdoms, I was going to say, but in any case different countries\u2014and so she wrote a very urgent letter to her mother\u2014or her father, I declare I do not know which, but we shall see presently in Jane\u2019s letter\u2014writing in Mr. Dixon\u2019s name as well as her own, urging them to come over immediately. They would meet them in Dublin and take them back to their country estate, Baly-craig, a beautiful place, I imagine.\"}"
