usily clearing the table for the pie and pudding.\\n\\nI could not take my eyes off him. Still clinging to the table leg with hands and feet, I watched the wretched man playfully touch his glass, pick it up, smile, tilt back his head, and drink the brandy. Immediately afterward, the company was overcome with indescribable alarm when he sprang to his feet, spun around several times in a terrifying, spasmodic whooping-cough dance, and rushed out the door. Through the window he could then be seen plunging violently and spitting, making the most hideous faces, and apparently out of his mind.\\n\\nI held on tightly while Mrs. Joe and Joe ran to him.\"}"
