 of them, Elizabeth more graciously than before. She even spoke to him once and looked at him more than once. Elizabeth was, in fact, considering an important plan. Its outcome soon explained it. After wasting a few minutes on the proper empty remarks, she began to give the invitation meant to include all the Musgroves\u2019 remaining obligations. \u201cTomorrow evening, to meet a few friends: no formal party.\u201d She said it with great grace, and the cards she had brought with her, marked \u201cMiss Elliot at home,\u201d were placed on the table with a courteous, inclusive smile for everyone, and one smile and one card more distinctly intended for Captain Wentworth. The truth was that Elizabeth had been in Bath long enough to understand the value of a man with such an air and appearance as his.\"}"
