e differing estimates of the interval between hearing the voices quarrelling and forcing open the chamber door. Some said it was no more than three minutes; others said as much as five. The door was difficult to open.\\n\\n\u201c_Alfonzo Garcio_, undertaker, states that he lives in the Rue Morgue. He is a native of Spain. He was among the party that entered the house, but did not go upstairs. Being nervous, he feared the effects of excitement. He heard the voices arguing. The gruff voice was that of a Frenchman. He could not make out what was said. The shrill voice was that of an Englishman\u2014of this he is certain.\u201d\"}"
