          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"14653526da35811b90050242\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cJupiter,\u201d he said when we reached its base, \u201ccome here! Was the skull nailed to the branch with its face turned outward, or toward the branch?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDe face was out, massa, so de crows could get at de eyes good, widout any trouble.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, then, was it through this eye or that one that you dropped the beetle?\u201d Legrand touched each of Jupiter\u2019s eyes.\\n\\n\u201c\u2019Twas dis eye, massa\u2014the lef eye\u2014jis as you tell me,\u201d and he pointed to his right eye.\\n\\n\u201cThat will do\u2014we must try it again.\u201d\\n\\nMy friend\u2019s madness now seemed, or perhaps only appeared, to show some method. He moved the peg marking where the beetle had fallen to a spot about three inches west of its former position. Then he measured from the nearest point of the trunk to the peg, as before, and extended the line straight for fifty feet. This marked a spot several yards away from where we had been digging.\\n\\nWe drew a circle around the new spot, somewhat larger than the first, and began digging again. I was terribly tired, but, without quite understanding what had changed in my thoughts, I no longer strongly disliked the work. I had become strangely interested\u2014even excited. Perhaps, despite Legrand\u2019s wild behavior, there was something thoughtful and deliberate about him that affected me. I dug eagerly and sometimes caught myself looking almost expectantly for the imagined treasure whose vision had driven my unfortunate companion mad. When these strange thoughts had taken their strongest hold on me, and after we had worked for perhaps an hour and a half, the dog\u2019s violent howling interrupted us again. At first his restlessness had clearly been caused by playfulness or whim, but now his cries became harsh and serious. When Jupiter tried once more to muzzle him, the dog resisted fiercely, leaped into the hole, and frantically clawed at the soil. Within seconds he had uncovered a mass of human bones\u2014two complete skeletons\u2014mixed with several metal buttons and what seemed to be the dust of decayed woolen cloth. One or two strokes of a spade turned up the blade of a large Spanish knife, and as we dug farther, three or four loose gold and silver coins appeared.\"}"
