ried to muzzle him, the animal resisted furiously, leaped into the hole, and began tearing at the earth with his claws. Within seconds he had exposed a heap of human bones, making up two complete skeletons, mixed with several metal buttons and what seemed to be the dust of decayed woolen cloth. A stroke or two of the spade turned up the blade of a large Spanish knife, and as we dug deeper, three or four loose gold and silver coins appeared.\"}"
