e driver pulled up sharply at the head of a dark lane. Above the low roofs and uneven chimney-stacks rose the black masts of ships. Coils of white mist clung to the yards like spectral sails.\\n\\n\u201cSomewhere around here, sir, isn\u2019t it?\u201d he asked hoarsely through the trap.\\n\\nDorian started and looked about him. \u201cThis will do,\u201d he replied; then, getting out quickly and paying the driver the extra fare he had promised, he walked swiftly toward the quay. Here and there, a lantern shone at the stern of some enormous merchant vessel. Its light trembled and broke apart in the puddles. A red glow came from a steamer bound outward and taking on coal. The slimy pavement resembled a wet mackintosh.\"}"
