o be as clearly cool towards him as their family relationship allowed, and to quietly withdraw from the unnecessary intimacy into which she had gradually been drawn. Accordingly, she was more guarded and cooler than she had been the previous evening.\\n\\nHe wanted to revive her curiosity about how and where he had once heard her praised, and very much wished to enjoy being questioned further. But the spell was broken. He realized that the excitement and liveliness of a public room were needed to stir his modest cousin\u2019s vanity; at least, he saw that he could not achieve it now through any of the attempts he could make while the others\u2019 stronger claims occupied her attention.\"}"
