          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"42ca43f139890e9fdd2c8a23\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cWell, everybody lives that way, Huck.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTom, it makes no difference. I ain\u2019t everybody, and I can\u2019t stand it. It\u2019s awful being tied down like that. And food comes too easily\u2014I don\u2019t care about eating when it\u2019s that way. I have to ask before I can go fishing; I have to ask before I can go swimming\u2014darned if I don\u2019t have to ask before doing everything. And I had to talk so politely that it wasn\u2019t any fun. Every day I had to go up into the attic and let loose for a while, just to get the proper taste back in my mouth, or I\u2019d have died, Tom. The widow wouldn\u2019t let me smoke; she wouldn\u2019t let me yell, gape, stretch, or scratch in front of people\u2014\u201d [Then, with a sudden burst of special anger and hurt]\u2014\u201cAnd blast it, she prayed all the time! I never saw such a woman! I had to shove off, Tom\u2014I simply had to. Besides, school is about to start, and I would have had to go. Well, I wouldn\u2019t stand that, Tom. Look here, Tom, being rich isn\u2019t what people say it is. It\u2019s nothing but worry and worry, sweat and sweat, and wishing you were dead all the time. These clothes suit me now, and this barrel suits me, and I\u2019m never going to leave them again. Tom, I never would have gotten into all this trouble if it hadn\u2019t been for that money. So you take my share along with yours, give me a dime once in a while\u2014not often, because I don\u2019t care about anything unless it\u2019s pretty hard to get\u2014and go ask the widow to let me go.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, Huck, you know I can\u2019t do that. It wouldn\u2019t be fair. Besides, if you try living this way a little longer, you\u2019ll come to like it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cLike it! Yes\u2014the way I\u2019d like sitting on a hot stove if I sat there long enough. No, Tom, I won\u2019t be rich, and I won\u2019t live in those cursed, stuffy houses. I like the woods, the river, and hogsheads, and I\u2019m going to stick with them. Blast it all! Just when we had guns, a cave, and everything ready for robbing, this foolish business has to come up and ruin it all!\u201d\\n\\nTom saw his chance\u2014\\n\\n\u201cLook here, Huck, being rich isn\u2019t going to stop me from becoming a robber.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo! Oh, good luck; are you really serious, Tom?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cJust as serious as I\u2019m sitting here. But Huck, we can\u2019t let you join the gang if you aren\u2019t respectable, you know.\u201d\\n\\nHuck\u2019s happiness disappeared.\\n\\n\u201cCan\u2019t let me join, Tom?\u201d\"}"
