          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"306432aad8dd203b6d9c7c55\",\"rewritten_text\":\"The exquisite gentlemen of the highest breeding wore small dangling ornaments that tinkled as they moved languidly; these golden fetters sounded like tiny precious bells. Together with the rustling of silk, brocade, and fine linen, their noise stirred a flutter in the air that wafted Saint Antoine and his ravenous hunger far away.\\n\\nDress was the one unfailing talisman and charm for keeping everything in its proper place. Everyone was dressed for a Fancy Ball that was never meant to end. From the Palace of the Tuileries, through Monseigneur and the entire Court, through the Chambers, the Tribunals of Justice, and all society (save the scarecrows), the Fancy Ball descended to the Common Executioner, who, in obedience to the charm, was obliged to officiate \u201cfrizzled, powdered, in a gold-laced coat, pumps, and white silk stockings.\u201d At the gallows and the wheel\u2014the axe being uncommon\u2014Monsieur Paris, as it was the episcopal fashion among his fellow Professors of the provinces, Monsieur Orleans, and the rest, to call him, presided in this elegant attire. And who among the company at Monseigneur\u2019s reception in that year of our Lord seventeen hundred and eighty could doubt that a system founded upon a frizzled, powdered, gold-laced, pumped, white-silk-stockinged hangman would last until the stars went out?\\n\\nWhen Monseigneur had relieved his four bearers of their burdens and drunk his chocolate, he ordered the doors of the Holiest of Holiests opened and came forth. Then there was submission, cringing and fawning, servility, and abject humiliation! As for bowing in body and spirit, nothing remained in that regard for Heaven\u2014which may have been one reason, among others, that Monseigneur\u2019s worshippers never troubled it.\\n\\nGiving one fortunate slave a word of promise and another a smile, whispering to one and waving his hand to the next, Monseigneur passed affably through his rooms toward the distant region of the Circumference of Truth. There, he turned and came back, and in due time had himself shut within his sanctuary by the chocolate sprites, after which he was seen no more.\\n\\nThe spectacle ended, the flutter in the air grew into quite a small storm, and the precious little bells rang down the stairs. Soon only one person remained of the whole crowd. With his hat beneath his arm and his snuff-box in his hand, he slowly made his way among the mirrors toward the exit.\\n\\n\u201cI devote you,\u201d said this person, pausing at the last door and turning toward the sanctuary, \u201cto the Devil!\u201d\\n\\nThen he shook the snuff from his fingers as though shaking dust from his feet, and quietly walked downstairs.\"}"
