e world will obey you.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAll this would be very sensible if it were spoken to someone else,\u201d Raymond replied bitterly. \u201cTake your own advice, and you, the first peer in the land, may become its sovereign. You, the good, wise, and just man, may rule every heart. But I have realized\u2014too soon for my happiness, too late for England\u2019s good\u2014that I accepted a task beyond my ability. I cannot control myself. My passions rule me; even my smallest impulse is my tyrant. Do you think I gave up the Protectorate\u2014and I have given it up\u2014in a moment of anger? By the living God, I swear I will never take up that bauble again, never again burden myself with the care and misery whose visible sign it is.\"}"
