{"request_id":"558179cbf4c6b12dd0e7abc2","rewritten_text":"As I passed my hand through the valve with a cup of water for the old cat, my shirt sleeves caught in the loop supporting the basket and, in an instant, pulled it loose from the bottom. If the whole thing had truly vanished into thin air, it could not have disappeared from my sight more suddenly. There could not have been even a tenth of a second between the basket’s release and its complete disappearance, along with everything it held. My good wishes followed it to the ground, but naturally I had no hope that either the cat or her kittens would survive to tell of their misfortune.

“At six o’clock, I saw a large portion of the earth’s visible surface to the east covered in deep shadow. This shadow advanced with great speed until, at five minutes before seven, the entire area before me was wrapped in the darkness of night. Yet it was long after this that the setting sun’s rays stopped illuminating the balloon; and although I had fully expected this, the sight still gave me immense pleasure. Clearly, in the morning I would see the rising sun at least several hours before the people of Rotterdam, despite their position much farther east. Thus, day after day, as my altitude increased, I would enjoy sunlight for a longer and longer time. I now resolved to keep a journal of my journey, counting each day as twenty-four continuous hours, without considering the periods of darkness.

“At ten o’clock, feeling sleepy, I decided to lie down for the remainder of the night. But then a difficulty arose which, obvious as it may seem, had escaped my notice until that very moment. If I slept as I intended, how could the air in the chamber be renewed while I slept? Breathing it for more than an hour at most would be impossible; and even if that period could be extended to an hour and a quarter, the consequences might be disastrous. This dilemma troubled me greatly. It may scarcely be believed that, after all the dangers I had endured, I regarded the matter so seriously that I abandoned all hope of completing my ultimate design and finally resigned myself to the necessity of descending. But this hesitation lasted only a moment."}

