          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"27b5a7744f7edd37fa90084c\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Smallpox!\\n\\nI hurried to the king and spoke into his ear:\\n\\n\u201cOut the door at once, sire! The woman is dying of the disease that ravaged Camelot two years ago.\u201d\\n\\nHe did not move.\\n\\n\u201cIndeed, I shall remain\u2014and help as well.\u201d\\n\\nI whispered once more:\\n\\n\u201cKing, you must not. You must leave.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYour purpose is good, and your words are not unwise. Yet it would shame a king to show fear, and shame a belted knight to hold back his hand where there are those in need of aid. Peace, I will not go. You are the one who must leave. The Church\u2019s ban is not laid upon me, but it forbids you to remain here, and she will treat you harshly should word reach her of your trespass.\u201d\\n\\nIt was a perilous position for him, and could cost him his life, but arguing was useless. If he believed his knightly honor was involved, that settled the matter; he would stay, and nothing could stop him. I knew this, and therefore let the subject drop. The woman spoke:\\n\\n\u201cGood sir, out of your kindness, will you climb that ladder and bring me word of what you discover? Do not fear to tell me, for there are times when even a mother\u2019s heart is beyond breaking\u2014having already broken.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cStay,\u201d said the king, \u201cand give the woman food. I will go.\u201d And he set down the knapsack.\\n\\nI turned to begin, but the king had already gone ahead. He stopped and looked down at a man lying in the dim light, who had not noticed us until then or spoken.\\n\\n\u201cIs that your husband?\u201d the king asked.\\n\\n\u201cYes.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIs he sleeping?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGod be thanked for that one mercy, yes\u2014for three hours now. Where may I repay my gratitude in full? My heart is overflowing with thanks for the sleep he sleeps now.\u201d\\n\\nI said:\\n\\n\u201cWe shall be careful. We will not wake him.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAh, no, that you will not, for he is dead.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDead?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes. What a triumph it is to know it! No one can hurt him, and no one can insult him again. He is in heaven now and happy; or, if not there, he remains in hell and is content, for there he will find neither abbot nor bishop. We were boy and girl together; we were husband and wife for these five-and-twenty years, never parted until today. Think how long that is to love and suffer side by side. This morning he was out of his mind, imagining that we were boy and girl again, wandering through the joyful fields; and so, in that innocent, happy talk, he wandered farther and farther, still lightly chatting, and entered those other fields of which we know nothing, shut away from mortal sight.\"}"
