arcy, with grave courtesy, requested the honour of her hand, but without success. Elizabeth was resolute, and Sir William\u2019s efforts to persuade her did nothing to change her mind.\\n\\n\u201cYou dance so excellently, Miss Eliza, that it is cruel to deny me the pleasure of seeing you; and although this gentleman generally dislikes the amusement, I am sure he can have no objection to obliging us for half an hour.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMr. Darcy is all politeness,\u201d said Elizabeth, smiling.\\n\\n\u201cHe certainly is; but given the inducement, my dear Miss Eliza, we cannot be surprised by his compliance. Who could object to such a partner?\u201d\\n\\nElizabeth gave him a mischievous look and turned away. Her refusal had not diminished her in the gentleman\u2019s estimation, and he was thinking of her with some satisfaction when Miss Bingley addressed him\u2014\"}"
