ad let us become engaged last year, none of this trouble would have happened. You won\u2019t send me back, will you? I can\u2019t go! I won\u2019t go!\u2019\\n\\nThe Minister could not help smiling at the handsome young troublemaker, and he was deeply touched by the boy\u2019s devotion to Virginia. Leaning down from his horse, he patted him kindly on the shoulders and said, \u2018Well, Cecil, if you refuse to go back, I suppose you must come with me. But I\u2019ll have to get you a hat at Ascot.\u2019\"}"
