          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"8764fb82d94d6f80282b9884\",\"rewritten_text\":\"At the stairs where we had taken him aboard, and ever afterward, I kept a wary lookout for any sign that we were suspected. I had seen none. We certainly had not been, and at that moment just as certainly were not, accompanied or followed by any boat. Had one been waiting on us, I would have run ashore and forced her either to proceed or to make her purpose plain. But we continued on without any sign of interference.\\n\\nHe wore his boat-cloak and seemed, as I have said, a natural part of the scene. It was striking\u2014though perhaps the miserable life he had led explained it\u2014that he was the least troubled of us all. He was not unconcerned, for he told me he hoped to live to see his gentleman become one of the finest gentlemen in a foreign land; nor, as I understood him, was he willing simply to submit or resign himself. But he had no intention of going halfway to meet danger. When danger came to him, he faced it; until then, he would not trouble himself about it.\\n\\n\u201cIf you knowed, dear boy,\u201d he said to me, \u201cwhat it is to sit here alonger my dear boy and smoke, arter being day after day betwixt four walls, you\u2019d envy me. But you don\u2019t know what it is.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI believe I know the pleasures of freedom,\u201d I replied.\\n\\n\u201cAh,\u201d said he, shaking his head solemnly. \u201cBut you don\u2019t know it equal to me. You must have been under lock and key, dear boy, to know it equal to me\u2014but I ain\u2019t a-going to be low.\u201d\\n\\nIt seemed inconsistent to me that, for any ruling idea, he should have risked his freedom, and even his life. But I considered that perhaps freedom without danger was so unlike the whole habit of his existence that it could not mean to him what it would mean to another man. I was not far wrong, for after smoking a little he said:\u2014\\n\\n\u201cYou see, dear boy, when I was over yonder, t\u2019other side the world, I was always looking toward this side; and it come flat to be there, though I was growing rich. Everybody knowed Magwitch, and Magwitch could come and go, and nobody\u2019s head would be troubled about him. They ain\u2019t so easy concerning me here, dear boy\u2014wouldn\u2019t be, leastways, if they knowed where I was.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIf everything goes well,\u201d I said, \u201cyou will be entirely free and safe again within a few hours.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell,\u201d he answered, drawing a deep breath, \u201cI hope so.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd believe so?\u201d\"}"
