          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"e8962ea13be7121610666eff\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Those venerable, feeble men were always seen by the public bowing, and people commonly believed that, after bowing a customer out, they continued bowing in the empty office until they bowed another customer in.\\n\\nThe barrister was perceptive enough to understand that the banker would not have expressed such an opinion on anything less substantial than moral certainty. Though unprepared for the large pill he had to swallow, he managed to get it down. \u201cAnd now,\u201d said Mr. Stryver, shaking his forensic forefinger at the Temple in general once it was down, \u201cmy way out of this is to prove you all wrong.\u201d\\n\\nIt was a piece of Old Bailey tactician\u2019s skill, and it brought him considerable relief. \u201cYou shall not prove me wrong, young lady,\u201d said Mr. Stryver; \u201cI\u2019ll do that for you.\u201d\\n\\nAccordingly, when Mr. Lorry called that night, as late as ten o\u2019clock, Mr. Stryver, surrounded by books and papers spread out for the purpose, appeared to have nothing less on his mind than the morning\u2019s subject. He even seemed surprised to see Mr. Lorry and was altogether absent and preoccupied.\\n\\n\u201cWell!\u201d said the good-natured emissary, after half an hour of fruitless attempts to bring him back to the matter. \u201cI have been to Soho.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTo Soho?\u201d Mr. Stryver repeated coldly. \u201cOh, of course! What am I thinking of!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd I have no doubt,\u201d said Mr. Lorry, \u201cthat I was right in the conversation we had. My opinion is confirmed, and I repeat my advice.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI assure you,\u201d replied Mr. Stryver in the friendliest manner, \u201cthat I am sorry for it on your account, and sorry for it on the poor father\u2019s account. I know this must always be a painful subject for the family; let us say no more about it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t understand you,\u201d said Mr. Lorry.\\n\\n\u201cI dare say you don\u2019t,\u201d Stryver replied, nodding in a soothing, conclusive way; \u201cnever mind, never mind.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut it does matter,\u201d Mr. Lorry insisted.\\n\\n\u201cNo, it doesn\u2019t; I assure you it doesn\u2019t. Having imagined sense where there is none, and a worthy ambition where there is no worthy ambition, I am glad to have escaped my mistake, and no harm has been done. Young women have made similar follies many times before, and have repented them in poverty and obscurity many times before. From an unselfish point of view, I am sorry the matter has been abandoned, because it would have been bad for me in worldly terms; from a selfish point of view, I am glad it has been abandoned, because it would have been bad for me in worldly terms\u2014it is scarcely necessary to say that I could have gained nothing from it.\"}"
