          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"98ac4c7e7f30f63f9d26c1ea\",\"rewritten_text\":\"After dinner, the whole gang went out onto the sandbar to hunt for turtle eggs. They poked sticks into the sand, and whenever they found a soft spot, they dropped to their knees and dug with their hands. Sometimes they pulled fifty or sixty eggs from a single hole. The eggs were perfectly round and white, a little smaller than an English walnut. That night they had a splendid fried-egg feast, and another on Friday morning.\\n\\nAfter breakfast, they went whooping and prancing onto the bar, chasing one another in circles and shedding their clothes as they ran until they were naked. Then they carried on their frolic far up the bar\u2019s shallow water, struggling against the strong current, which repeatedly knocked their legs out from under them and made the fun even greater. From time to time they gathered together and splashed water into one another\u2019s faces with their palms, gradually drawing closer, their faces turned away to escape the choking spray. At last they seized and wrestled with one another until the strongest ducked his neighbor, and then all of them went under in a tangle of pale legs and arms. They surfaced blowing, sputtering, laughing, and gasping for breath all at once.\\n\\nWhen they were thoroughly worn out, they ran ashore and sprawled on the dry, hot sand, lying there and covering themselves with it. Before long they would rush back into the water and repeat the whole performance. Finally, they realized that their bare skin served quite well as flesh-colored \u201ctights.\u201d They drew a circle in the sand and put on a circus\u2014with three clowns, since none of them would surrender that most honored position to another.\\n\\nNext they brought out their marbles and played \u201cknucks,\u201d \u201cringtaw,\u201d and \u201ckeeps\u201d until the game lost its appeal. Then Joe and Huck went swimming again, but Tom refused, because when he kicked off his trousers, he had also kicked the string of rattlesnake rattles from his ankle. He wondered how he had avoided cramps for so long without the protection of that mysterious charm. He would not go back into the water until he found it, and by then the other boys were tired and ready to rest. Gradually they drifted apart, sank into the \u201cdumps,\u201d and gazed wistfully across the broad river toward the village, which lay dozing in the sunlight. Tom caught himself writing \u201cBECKY\u201d in the sand with his big toe. He scratched it out and was angry at himself for being so weak. But he wrote it again anyway; he could not help himself. He erased it once more, then escaped the temptation by herding the other boys together and joining them.\"}"
