          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"862ba42cc33b3b63f88e5856\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Smallpox!\\n\\nI rushed to the king and whispered in his ear:\\n\\n\u201cLeave at once, sire! The woman is dying of the disease that ravaged Camelot two years ago.\u201d\\n\\nHe did not move.\\n\\n\u201cIndeed, I shall stay\u2014and help as well.\u201d\\n\\nI whispered again:\\n\\n\u201cKing, you must not. You must go.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou mean well, and your words are not foolish. But it would be shameful for a king to show fear, and shameful for a knight in armor to hold back his hand when people need help. Be quiet; I will not go. You are the one who must leave. The Church\u2019s ban is not upon me, but it forbids you to be here, and it will punish you severely if it hears of your trespass.\u201d\\n\\nIt was a desperate situation for him and might cost him his life, but there was no use arguing. If he believed his knightly honor was at stake, that ended the matter; he would stay, and nothing could stop him. I knew that, so I dropped the subject. The woman spoke:\\n\\n\u201cGood sir, would you kindly climb that ladder and tell me what you find? Do not be afraid to report it, for there are times when even a mother\u2019s heart is beyond breaking\u2014because it is already broken.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cStay,\u201d said the king, \u201cand give the woman something to eat. I will go.\u201d He set down the knapsack.\\n\\nI turned to leave, but the king had already begun. He stopped and looked down at a man lying in the dim light, who had not noticed us or spoken.\\n\\n\u201cIs he your husband?\u201d the king asked.\\n\\n\u201cYes.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIs he asleep?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThank God for that one kindness, yes\u2014for three hours. Where can I fully repay my gratitude? My heart is overflowing with it because he sleeps now.\u201d\\n\\nI said:\\n\\n\u201cWe will be careful. We will not wake him.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh no, you will not, for he is dead.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDead?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes. What a victory it is to know that! No one can hurt him or insult him again. He is in heaven now and happy; or, if he is not there, he remains in hell and is content, for there he will find neither abbot nor bishop. We were boy and girl together, and man and wife for twenty-five years, never separated until today. Think how long that is to love and suffer together. This morning he was out of his mind, imagining that we were boy and girl again, wandering through happy fields. So, in that innocent, joyful conversation, he wandered farther and farther, still talking lightly, and entered those other fields we know nothing about, shut away from mortal sight.\"}"
