e door. The door was not opened at once when the bell was rung, and one of my two conductors struck the man who opened it across the face with his heavy riding glove.\\n\\n\u201cThere was nothing in this act to draw my special notice, since I had seen common people struck more often than dogs. But the other man, angered as well, struck him in the same fashion with his arm; the brothers\u2019 expressions and bearing were then so precisely alike that I first understood they were twins.\\n\\n\u201cFrom the moment we alighted at the outer gate\u2014which we found locked, and which one brother opened to let us in before locking it again\u2014I had heard cries coming from an upper chamber.\"}"
