          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"349a96f0c7c1b3c634f5569a\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cI agree. It\u2019s the best plan. Will you hold hands and swear that we\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, no, that won\u2019t do for this. That\u2019s good enough for little, common rubbish\u2014especially with gals, \u2019cause _they_ go back on you anyhow, and blab when they get mad\u2014but there ought to be writing about a big thing like this. And blood.\u201d\\n\\nTom\u2019s entire being applauded the notion. It was profound, gloomy, and terrible; the hour, the circumstances, and the surroundings suited it perfectly. He picked up a clean pine shingle lying in the moonlight, drew a small piece of \u201cred keel\u201d from his pocket, turned his work toward the moon, and painfully scratched out these words, stressing every slow down-stroke by gripping his tongue between his teeth and easing the pressure on the up-strokes.\\n\\n\u201cHuck Finn and Tom Sawyer swears they will keep mum about This and They wish They may Drop down dead in Their Tracks if They ever Tell and Rot.\u201d\\n\\nHuckleberry was full of wonder at Tom\u2019s skill with writing and the grandeur of his language. He immediately pulled a pin from his lapel and was about to prick himself, but Tom stopped him:\\n\\n\u201cWait! Don\u2019t do that. A pin\u2019s brass. It may have verdigrease on it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat\u2019s verdigrease?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt\u2019s poison. That\u2019s what it is. You just swallow some once\u2014you\u2019ll find out.\u201d\\n\\nSo Tom unwound the thread from one of his needles, and each boy pricked the ball of his thumb and squeezed out a drop of blood. After many squeezes, Tom finally managed to sign his initials, using the ball of his little finger as a pen. Then he taught Huckleberry to form an H and an F, and the oath was finished. They buried the shingle near the wall with gloomy ceremonies and incantations, and the fetters binding their tongues were thought to be locked, with the key thrown away.\\n\\nA figure now crept silently through a gap at the far end of the ruined building, but they failed to notice it.\\n\\n\u201cTom,\u201d whispered Huckleberry, \u201cdoes this stop us from _ever_ telling\u2014_always_?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOf course it does. No matter _what_ happens, we\u2019ve got to keep mum. We\u2019d drop dead\u2014don\u2019t _you_ know that?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, I reckon that\u2019s true.\u201d\\n\\nThey went on whispering for a while. Presently, a dog began a long, mournful howl just outside\u2014less than ten feet away. The boys suddenly seized each other, terrified.\\n\\n\u201cWhich one of us does he mean?\u201d Huckleberry gasped.\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t know\u2014look through the crack. Quick!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, _you_, Tom!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI can\u2019t\u2014I can\u2019t _do_ it, Huck!\u201d\"}"
