          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"907d1d53216fe13eede345a3\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cOne word more, Rose. Dearest Rose\u2014just one more!\u201d cried Harry, throwing himself before her. \u201cIf I had been less\u2014less fortunate, as the world would call it\u2014if some obscure and peaceful life had been my destiny\u2014if I had been poor, sick, helpless\u2014would you have turned from me then? Or has my likely rise to wealth and honour given birth to this scruple?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDo not force me to answer,\u201d Rose replied. \u201cThe question does not arise, and never will. It is unfair, almost unkind, to press me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIf your answer is what I scarcely dare hope,\u201d Harry returned, \u201cit will cast a gleam of happiness upon my lonely path and light the way before me. It is no small thing to do so much, with a few brief words, for one who loves you above everything else. Oh, Rose: in the name of my passionate and lasting devotion; in the name of all I have suffered for you, and all you condemn me to endure; answer me this one question!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen, if your lot had been different,\u201d Rose answered; \u201cif you had been even a little, though not so far, above me; if I could have been a help and comfort to you in some humble life of peace and retirement, rather than a blemish and burden among ambitious and distinguished people; I would have been spared this trial. I have every reason to be happy\u2014very happy\u2014now; but then, Harry, I admit I would have been happier.\u201d\\n\\nAs Rose made this confession, crowded memories of old hopes, cherished long ago when she was a girl, filled her mind; but they brought tears with them, as old hopes do when they return withered, and the tears brought her relief.\\n\\n\u201cI cannot help this weakness, and it strengthens my resolve,\u201d she said, extending her hand. \u201cI must leave you now, truly.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI ask one promise,\u201d said Harry. \u201cOnce, and only once more\u2014say within a year, though it may be much sooner\u2014I may speak to you again on this subject, for the last time.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot to urge me to change my rightful decision,\u201d Rose replied, with a melancholy smile; \u201cit will be useless.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo,\u201d said Harry; \u201cto hear you repeat it, if you will\u2014repeat it finally! I will lay at your feet whatever position or fortune I may possess; and if you still hold to your present resolution, I will not try, by word or deed, to change it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen let it be so,\u201d Rose replied; \u201cit is only one more pang, and by then I may be better able to bear it.\u201d\\n\\nShe extended her hand again.\"}"
