nd that it would have been impossible to push through them without the scythe. At his master\u2019s command, Jupiter began cutting a passage for us toward the foot of an immensely tall tulip-tree. It stood on the level ground with eight or ten oaks, yet surpassed them all\u2014and every other tree I had ever seen\u2014in the beauty of its leaves and shape, the broad reach of its branches, and the majestic character of its whole appearance.\"}"
