          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"702aed4a85d5cfd40c306539\",\"rewritten_text\":\"The surrounding oaks were home to a tribe of nightingales\u2014and there I am now; Idris, in the cherished prime of youth, is beside me. Remember, I am only twenty-two, and scarcely seventeen summers have passed over the beloved of my heart. The river, swollen by autumn rains, flooded the lowlands, and Adrian, in his favorite boat, was engaged in the dangerous sport of tearing the highest branch from a submerged oak. Are you weary of life, Adrian, that you play with danger in this way?\u2014\\n\\nHe secured his prize and steered his boat through the flood. We watched him anxiously, but the current carried him away from us; he had to land much farther downstream and make a considerable detour before he could rejoin us. \u201cHe is safe!\u201d said Idris, as he sprang ashore and waved the branch above his head in triumph. \u201cWe will wait for him here.\u201d\\n\\nWe were alone together. The sun had set; the nightingales began to sing; and the evening star shone clearly in the still-bright flood of light lingering in the west. My angelic girl\u2019s blue eyes rested on this sweet emblem of herself. \u201cHow the light trembles,\u201d she said, \u201cas though that star\u2019s life were in it. Its wavering radiance seems to say that its condition, like ours on earth, is uncertain and changeable; it fears, I think, and it loves.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDo not gaze at the star, dear, generous friend,\u201d I cried. \u201cDo not read love in its trembling rays; do not look toward distant worlds; do not speak of the mere imagination of a feeling. I have been silent for so long\u2014so long, and with such painful longing, have I wished to speak to you and surrender my soul, my life, my whole being to you. Do not look at the star, dear love\u2014or do, and let that eternal spark plead for me; let it be my witness and advocate, silent as it shines. Love is to me what light is to the star; so long as that light is not extinguished by annihilation, so long will I love you.\u201d\\n\\nThe rapture of that moment must remain forever hidden from the world\u2019s hardened eyes. I can still feel her graceful form pressed against my overflowing heart; still, at the memory of that first kiss, sight, pulse, and breath grow faint and fail. Slowly and silently, we went to meet Adrian, whom we heard approaching.\\n\\nI begged Adrian to return to me after escorting his sister home. That same evening, as we walked along the moonlit forest paths, I poured out my entire heart\u2014its joy and its hope\u2014to my friend. For a moment he looked troubled. \u201cI might have foreseen this,\u201d he said. \u201cWhat conflict will now follow!\u201d\"}"
