t there at once to have me bound apprentice to Joe in the presence of the magistrates. I say we went there, but Pumblechook pushed me along as if I had just picked someone\u2019s pocket or set fire to a haystack; indeed, everyone in court seemed to think I had been caught red-handed. As Pumblechook shoved me through the crowd ahead of him, I heard some people say, \u201cWhat has he done?\u201d and others, \u201cHe\u2019s only a youngster, too, but he looks bad, doesn\u2019t he?\u201d One person with a mild, kindly face even gave me a tract decorated with a woodcut of a wicked young man covered in a complete sausage-shop of chains, and titled TO BE READ IN MY CELL.\\n\\nThe Hall seemed a strange place to me, with pews higher than those in a church\u2014and people leaning over them to watch\u2014and imposing Justices, one with a powdered head, reclining in chairs with folded arms, taking snuff, falling asleep, writing, or reading newspapers. On the walls hung several glossy black portraits, which my untrained eye saw as a mixture of hardbake and sticking-plaster.\"}"
