          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"bc981841d297ace8982ef22a\",\"rewritten_text\":\"A little after noon, the boys borrowed a small skiff from a citizen who was away and set off at once. When they were several miles below \u201cCave Hollow,\u201d Tom said:\\n\\n\u201cNow you can see that this bluff looks the same all the way down from Cave Hollow\u2014no houses, no woodpiles, bushes all alike. But do you see that white spot up there where there\u2019s been a landslide? Well, that\u2019s one of my marks. We\u2019ll go ashore now.\u201d\\n\\nThey landed.\\n\\n\u201cNow, Huck, from where we\u2019re standing, you could touch the hole I escaped from with a fishing pole. See if you can find it.\u201d\\n\\nHuck searched all around but found nothing. Tom proudly walked into a thick clump of sumac bushes and said:\\n\\n\u201cThere you are! Look at it, Huck; it\u2019s the snugest hole in this country. Just keep quiet about it. I\u2019ve always wanted to be a robber, but I knew I\u2019d need a place like this, and finding one was the trouble. Now we\u2019ve got it, and we\u2019ll keep it secret\u2014except we\u2019ll let Joe Harper and Ben Rogers in, because of course there has to be a Gang, or there wouldn\u2019t be any style to it. Tom Sawyer\u2019s Gang\u2014it sounds splendid, doesn\u2019t it, Huck?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, it certainly does, Tom. And who will we rob?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, almost anybody. Ambush people\u2014that\u2019s mostly how it\u2019s done.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd kill them?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, not always. Keep them in the cave until they raise a ransom.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat\u2019s a ransom?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMoney. You make them get all they can from their friends; and after you\u2019ve kept them a year, if it still hasn\u2019t been raised, then you kill them. That\u2019s the usual way. Only you don\u2019t kill the women. You lock them up, but you don\u2019t kill them. They\u2019re always beautiful and rich, and terribly frightened. You take their watches and things, but you always remove your hat and speak politely. Nobody is as polite as robbers\u2014you\u2019ll see that in any book. Then the women fall in love with you, and after they\u2019ve been in the cave a week or two, they stop crying, and after that you couldn\u2019t make them leave. If you drove them out, they\u2019d turn around and come back. That\u2019s how it is in all the books.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, that\u2019s really great, Tom. I believe it\u2019s better than being a pirate.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, it\u2019s better in some ways, because it\u2019s close to home and circuses and everything.\u201d\\n\\nBy then everything was ready, and the boys entered the hole, Tom leading. They worked their way to the far end of the tunnel, then secured their joined kite strings and moved on.\"}"
