t time; but all she possessed certainly emerged then, and she loved him passionately. There is no doubt that she idolized him completely. He exploited her affection so methodically that he obtained large sums of money from her, and persuaded her to buy her brother\u2019s share in the brewery\u2014which their father had weakly left him\u2014at an enormous price, claiming that once he became her husband, he would have to own and manage the whole concern. Your guardian was not yet involved in Miss Havisham\u2019s affairs, and she was too proud and too deeply in love to accept advice from anyone.\u201d\"}"
