          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"eeb65af109bb267e69fcccff\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cMen marry because they are weary; women, because they are curious: both end by being disappointed.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t think I\u2019m likely to marry, Harry. I\u2019m too much in love. That\u2019s one of your aphorisms. I\u2019m putting it into practice, as I do everything you say.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWho are you in love with?\u201d Lord Henry asked after a pause.\\n\\n\u201cAn actress,\u201d said Dorian Gray, blushing.\\n\\nLord Henry shrugged. \u201cThat is a rather commonplace _d\u00e9but_.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou wouldn\u2019t say that if you saw her, Harry.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWho is she?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHer name is Sibyl Vane.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNever heard of her.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo one has. They will someday, though. She is a genius.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear boy, no woman is a genius. Women are a decorative sex. They never have anything to say, but they say it charmingly. Women represent matter\u2019s triumph over mind, just as men represent mind\u2019s triumph over morals.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHarry, how can you say that?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Dorian, it is perfectly true. I am studying women at present, so I ought to know. The subject is not as abstruse as I once thought. Ultimately, I find, there are only two kinds of women, the plain and the coloured. Plain women are extremely useful. If you wish to acquire a reputation for respectability, you need only take them down to supper. The others are very charming. They make one mistake, however. They paint themselves in an attempt to look young. Our grandmothers painted in an attempt to speak brilliantly. _Rouge_ and _esprit_ once went together. That is finished now. So long as a woman can appear ten years younger than her own daughter, she is entirely content. As for conversation, only five women in London are worth talking to, and two of them cannot be admitted to decent society. But tell me about your genius. How long