          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"43b9738c9e475f8a9662c56c\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cOne word more, Rose. Dearest Rose\u2014one more!\u201d cried Harry, throwing himself before her. \u201cIf I had been less\u2014less fortunate, as the world would call it\u2014if some obscure and peaceful life had been allotted me\u2014if I had been poor, sick, helpless\u2014would you have rejected me then? Or has my likely rise to wealth and honour given birth to this scruple?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDo not force me to answer,\u201d replied Rose. \u201cThe question does not arise, and never will. It is unfair, almost unkind, to press it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIf your answer is what I scarcely dare hope,\u201d returned Harry, \u201cit will cast a gleam of happiness across my lonely path, and illuminate the road before me. It is no small thing to do so much, by speaking a few brief words, for one who loves you above everything. Oh, Rose: in the name of my passionate and lasting devotion; in the name of all I have suffered for you, and all you condemn me to endure; answer me this one question!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen, if your lot had been differently appointed,\u201d rejoined Rose; \u201cif you had been even somewhat, though not so greatly, above me; if I could have been a help and comfort to you in some humble life of peace and retirement, rather than a stain and hindrance amid ambitious and distinguished society; I should have been spared this ordeal. I have every reason to be happy\u2014very happy\u2014now; but then, Harry, I confess I should have been happier.\u201d\\n\\nCrowded memories of old hopes, cherished long ago when she was a girl, filled Rose\u2019s mind as she made this confession; but they brought tears with them, as old hopes do when they return withered, and the tears brought her relief.\\n\\n\u201cI cannot overcome this weakness, and it strengthens my resolve,\u201d said Rose, holding out her hand. \u201cI must leave you now, truly.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI ask one promise,\u201d said Harry. \u201cOnce, and only once more\u2014within a year, perhaps, though it may be much sooner\u2014I may speak to you again on this matter, for the final time.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot to urge me to change my rightful decision,\u201d replied Rose, with a melancholy smile; \u201cthat would be useless.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo,\u201d said Harry; \u201conly to hear you repeat it, if you will\u2014repeat it finally! I will place at your feet whatever rank or fortune I may possess; and if you still maintain your present resolution, I will not seek, by word or deed, to alter it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen let it be so,\u201d rejoined Rose; \u201cit is only one pain more, and by then I may be better able to endure it.\u201d\\n\\nShe held out her hand once again.\"}"
