          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"6eaf438e1c346d0d0ba63347\",\"rewritten_text\":\"I then went from shop to shop, buying whatever was needed to alter his appearance. When that was done, I made my way, for my own purposes, to Little Britain. Mr. Jaggers was at his desk, but when he saw me enter, he rose at once and stood before the fire.\\n\\n\u201cNow, Pip,\u201d he said, \u201cbe careful.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI will, sir,\u201d I replied. On the way there, I had thought carefully about what I meant to say.\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t commit yourself,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, \u201cand don\u2019t commit anyone else. You understand\u2014anyone. Don\u2019t tell me anything: I don\u2019t want to know anything; I\u2019m not curious.\u201d\\n\\nOf course, I understood that he knew the man had arrived.\\n\\n\u201cI only want, Mr. Jaggers,\u201d I said, \u201cto satisfy myself that what I have been told is true. I have no hope that it is untrue, but at least I can verify it.\u201d\\n\\nMr. Jaggers nodded. \u201cBut did you say \u2018told\u2019 or \u2018informed\u2019?\u201d he asked, tilting his head to one side. He did not look at me, but listened intently toward the floor. \u201cTold would suggest verbal communication. You can\u2019t have verbal communication with a man in New South Wales, you know.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019ll say, informed, Mr. Jaggers.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGood.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have been informed by a person named Abel Magwitch that he is the benefactor who has been unknown to me for so long.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat is the man,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, \u201cin New South Wales.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd no one else?\u201d I asked.\\n\\n\u201cAnd no one else,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers.\\n\\n\u201cI am not so unreasonable, sir, as to hold you responsible for my mistakes and false conclusions; but I always believed it was Miss Havisham.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAs you say, Pip,\u201d Mr. Jaggers replied, turning his cool eyes on me and biting his forefinger, \u201cI am not responsible