en a huge, flaming mass of material, whose nature I could not identify, roared and thundered past the balloon. When my fear and astonishment had somewhat faded, I had little trouble believing it was a massive volcanic fragment thrown from the world I was rapidly approaching. In all likelihood, it belonged to the strange class of objects sometimes found on earth and called meteoric stones for lack of a better name.\\n\\n\u201cApril 16th. Today, looking upward as best I could through each side window in turn, I saw, to my great delight, a very small part of the moon\u2019s disk extending beyond the balloon\u2019s enormous circumference on every side.\"}"
