our\u2014that is all. It often seems to me that art hides the artist far more completely than it reveals him. And so, when I received this offer from Paris, I decided to make your portrait the chief work in my exhibition. It never entered my mind that you would refuse. I see now that you were right. The picture must not be shown. You must not be angry with me, Dorian, for telling you this.\"}"
