rying to arrange my thoughts in the proper order for my attempt. My heart beat rapidly as I gathered the strength to speak to him. I was determined not to be rejected, yet I trembled to imagine what effect my words might have on him. At last, after much hesitation, I began:\\n\\n\u201cYour kindness toward me, my dearest father, and the affection\u2014the excessive affection\u2014you showed me when you first returned will, I hope, excuse me in your eyes for daring to speak to you, though with the tender affection of a daughter, yet also with the freedom of a friend and an equal.\u201d\"}"
