ch day they became more ardent and tender. It was a passion that had grown with him; it had become woven into every faculty and feeling, and could end only with his life. No one knew of their love except their two hearts. Yet although he feared his companions\u2019 judgment in all things, and even in this\u2014because he truly loved someone beneath him in fortune\u2014nothing could for a moment shake his resolve to unite himself with her as soon as he could gather enough courage to face the difficulties he was determined to overcome.\\n\\nDiana was entirely worthy of his deepest affection.\"}"
