{"request_id":"c7e0bd015e8eba69635ef91c","rewritten_text":"“By eight o’clock I had risen seventeen miles above the earth’s surface. It seemed clear that my rate of ascent was increasing, and that it would have continued to rise slightly even if I had not released the ballast. The pains in my head and ears returned violently from time to time, and I still occasionally bled from the nose; but overall, I suffered far less than might have been expected. Breathing, however, became more difficult every moment, and each breath brought an unpleasant spasm in my chest. I now unpacked the condensing apparatus and prepared it for immediate use.

“The view of the earth at this stage of my ascent was truly beautiful. To the west, north, and south, as far as I could see, stretched an apparently calm, endless ocean. Its blue grew deeper by the moment, and it was already beginning to look slightly curved. Far to the east, though perfectly visible, lay the islands of Great Britain, the entire Atlantic coasts of France and Spain, and a small part of northern Africa. Not a single building could be seen; the proudest cities of mankind had completely vanished from the earth’s surface. From the rock of Gibraltar, now reduced to a dim speck, the dark Mediterranean, dotted with shining islands like stars in the sky, stretched eastward as far as I could see. At last, its whole mass of water seemed to plunge over the edge of the horizon, and I found myself listening eagerly for the echoes of that mighty waterfall. Above me, the sky was pitch-black, and the stars shone brilliantly.

“The pigeons now seemed to be suffering greatly, so I decided to set them free. I first untied one, a beautiful gray-mottled bird, and placed him on the edge of the wickerwork. He seemed extremely uneasy, looking around anxiously, fluttering his wings, and cooing loudly, but he could not be persuaded to leave the car. At last I picked him up and threw him about six yards from the balloon. Instead of descending as I expected, he struggled desperately to return, crying in a high, piercing voice. He finally reached his former place on the rim, but had scarcely done so when his head fell onto his breast, and he dropped dead inside the car.”"}

