          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"af46cb5710d38848517c9533\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Suddenly Mr. Podgers released Lord Arthur\u2019s right hand and grasped his left, stooping so far over it that the gold rims of his spectacles appeared almost to brush the palm. For an instant his face turned into a white mask of terror, but he quickly regained his _sang-froid_, and, looking up at Lady Windermere, said with an artificial smile, \u2018It is the hand of a charming young man.\\n\\n\u2018Of course it is!\u2019 replied Lady Windermere, \u2018but will he make a charming husband? That is what I wish to discover.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018All charming young men do,\u2019 said Mr. Podgers.\\n\\n\u2018I don\u2019t believe a husband ought to be too fascinating,\u2019 murmured Lady Jedburgh thoughtfully; \u2018it is so dangerous.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018My dear child, they are never too fascinating,\u2019 cried Lady Windermere. \u2018But I want particulars. Particulars are the only things that matter. What is to happen to Lord Arthur?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Well, during the next few months Lord Arthur will take a voyage\u2014\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Oh yes, his honeymoon, naturally!\u2019\\n\\n\u2018And lose a relative.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Not his sister, I hope?\u2019 said Lady Jedburgh, her voice full of distress.\\n\\n\u2018Certainly not his sister,\u2019 answered Mr. Podgers, waving his hand deprecatingly; \u2018merely a distant relative.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Well, I am terribly disappointed,\u2019 said Lady Windermere. \u2018I shall have absolutely nothing to tell Sybil tomorrow. Nobody cares about distant relatives nowadays. They went out of fashion years ago. Still, I suppose she had better keep a black silk dress ready; it always serves for church, you know. And now let us go to supper. They are certain to have eaten everything, but perhaps we shall find some hot soup. Fran\u00e7ois once made excellent soup, but he is so disturbed by politics at present that I never feel entirely sure of him. I do wish General Boulanger would be quiet. Duchess, surely you are tired?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Not in the least, dear Gladys,\u2019 answered the Duchess, waddling toward the door. \u2018I have enjoyed myself immensely, and the cheiropodist\u2014I mean the cheiromantist\u2014is most interesting. Flora, where can my tortoise-shell fan be? Oh, thank you so much, Sir Thomas. And my lace shawl, Flora? Oh, thank you, Sir Thomas, very kind, I\u2019m sure\u2019; and the worthy creature at last succeeded in reaching the lower floor without dropping her scent-bottle more than twice.\\n\\nThroughout it all Lord Arthur Savile had stood beside the fireplace, oppressed by the same dread and the same sickening sense of approaching evil. He smiled sadly at his sister as she passed him on Lord Plymdale\u2019s arm, looking beautiful in pink brocade and pearls, and scarcely heard Lady Windermere call for him to follow. He thought of Sybil Merton, and the thought that anything might separate them brought tears to his eyes.\"}"
