          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"be955deb3ef44062359277be\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cCertainly not,\u201d replied Duff.\\n\\n\u201cAnd, translating the word \u2018yokel\u2019 for the ladies, I take it you mean that this attempt was not made by a countryman?\u201d said Mr. Losberne, smiling.\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s right, sir,\u201d replied Blathers. \u201cThis is all about the robbery, is it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAll of it,\u201d replied the doctor.\\n\\n\u201cNow, what is this about the boy the servants have been talking about?\u201d asked Blathers.\\n\\n\u201cNothing at all,\u201d replied the doctor. \u201cOne frightened servant decided that the boy had something to do with this attempt to break into the house; but it\u2019s nonsense\u2014complete absurdity.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cEasy enough to settle, if that\u2019s true,\u201d remarked Duff.\\n\\n\u201cWhat he says is quite right,\u201d observed Blathers, nodding firmly and idly playing with the handcuffs as though they were castanets. \u201cWho is the boy? What story does he tell about himself? Where did he come from? He didn\u2019t fall out of the clouds, did he, sir?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOf course not,\u201d replied the doctor, glancing nervously at the two ladies. \u201cI know his entire history, but we can discuss that later. You would like to see the place where the thieves tried to get in first, I suppose?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCertainly,\u201d replied Mr. Blathers. \u201cWe had better inspect the house first and question the servants afterward. That is the usual way of doing things.\u201d\\n\\nLights were brought, and Messrs. Blathers and Duff, accompanied by the local constable, Brittles, Giles, and everyone else, went into the little room at the end of the passage and looked out of the window. Then they went around across the lawn and looked in through it. After that, they had a candle brought out to examine the shutter, a lantern to follow the footprints, and a pitchfork to search the bushes. When this was finished, to the breathless interest of everyone watching, they came back inside. Mr. Giles and Brittles were then made to act out their parts in the previous night\u2019s events. They performed it about six times, contradicting each other in only one important detail the first time, and in at least a dozen by the last. Once this was done, Blathers and Duff cleared the room and held a long private discussion. Compared with its secrecy and seriousness, a meeting of great doctors debating the hardest problem in medicine would have seemed like child\u2019s play.\\n\\nMeanwhile, the doctor paced uneasily in the next room, while Mrs. Maylie and Rose watched with worried faces.\\n\\n\u201cUpon my word,\u201d he said, stopping after many quick turns, \u201cI hardly know what to do.\u201d\"}"
