          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"6140da2ae335232d55df477f\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cHe was brought to you. You see that I know the circumstances?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat is certainly true,\u201d said Defarge. His wife had signaled with an accidental touch of her elbow as she knitted and hummed that he should answer, but always briefly.\\n\\n\u201cIt was to you,\u201d said the spy, \u201cthat his daughter came; and it was from your care that she took him, accompanied by a neat brown gentleman\u2014what was his name?\u2014wearing a little wig\u2014Lorry\u2014of Tellson and Company\u2019s bank\u2014to England.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat is true,\u201d Defarge repeated.\\n\\n\u201cVery interesting memories!\u201d said the spy. \u201cI have known Doctor Manette and his daughter in England.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes?\u201d said Defarge.\\n\\n\u201cYou do not hear much about them now?\u201d asked the spy.\\n\\n\u201cNo,\u201d said Defarge.\\n\\n\u201cIn fact,\u201d Madame Defarge interrupted, looking up from her work and her little song, \u201cwe never hear about them. We received word that they had arrived safely, and perhaps one other letter, or perhaps two. Since then, they have gone their way in life\u2014we have gone ours\u2014and we have had no correspondence.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cExactly so, madame,\u201d replied the spy. \u201cShe is going to be married.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGoing?\u201d Madame Defarge echoed. \u201cShe was pretty enough to have been married long ago. You English seem cold to me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh! You know I am English.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI can hear it in your speech,\u201d Madame Defarge replied; \u201cand I suppose a man is like his tongue.\u201d\\n\\nHe did not take this as a compliment, but he made light of it with a laugh. After finishing his cognac, he added:\\n\\n\u201cYes, Miss Manette is going to be married. But not to an Englishman; to someone who, like her, was born French. And speaking of Gaspard\u2014poor Gaspard! It was cruel, cruel!\u2014it is a