          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"7b1d853f6c6fbbf5bcf9b129\",\"rewritten_text\":\"The oaks around us were home to a tribe of nightingales\u2014there I am now; Idris, in the precious prime of youth, is beside me. Remember, I am only twenty-two, and barely seventeen summers have passed over the beloved of my heart. The river, swollen by autumn rains, flooded the lowlands, and Adrian, in his favorite boat, was engaged in the dangerous sport of plucking the highest branch from a submerged oak. Are you tired of life, Adrian, that you play so carelessly with danger?\u2014\\n\\nHe secured his prize and guided his boat through the flood. We watched him anxiously, but the current carried him away from us. He had to land much farther downstream and take a long route before he could rejoin us. \u201cHe is safe!\u201d said Idris, leaping ashore and waving the branch above his head as a sign of victory. \u201cWe will wait for him here.\u201d\\n\\nWe were alone together. The sun had set, the nightingales began to sing, and the evening star shone clearly in the light that still lingered unfaded in the west. My angelic girl\u2019s blue eyes rested on this sweet image of herself. \u201cHow the light trembles,\u201d she said, \u201cas though that trembling were the star\u2019s life. Its shifting brightness seems to say that its condition, like ours on earth, is uncertain and changeable; it fears, I think, and it loves.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDo not gaze at the star, dear, generous friend,\u201d I cried. \u201cDo not read love in its trembling rays; do not look toward distant worlds or speak of the mere idea of a feeling. I have been silent for a long time\u2014so long that the desire to speak has made me ill\u2014and I have wished to place my soul, my life, my whole being in your hands. Do not look at the star, dear love\u2014or do, and let that eternal spark speak for me. Let it be my witness and advocate, silent as it shines. Love is to me what light is to the star; as long as that light is not extinguished by annihilation, I will love you.\u201d\\n\\nThe joy of that moment must remain forever hidden from the world\u2019s hardened eyes. I can still feel her graceful body pressed against my overflowing heart; even now, sight, pulse, and breath weaken and fail when I remember that first kiss. Slowly and silently, we went to meet Adrian, whom we heard approaching.\\n\\nI begged Adrian to return to me after taking his sister home. That same evening, as we walked along the moonlit forest paths, I poured out my whole heart\u2014its joy and its hope\u2014to my friend. For a moment he looked troubled. \u201cI might have expected this,\u201d he said. \u201cWhat conflict will now follow!\u201d\"}"
