          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"faa594650690df9463663877\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cWell,\u201d I said, \u201cI needed the watermelon.\u201d But he said I didn\u2019t need it to escape from prison; that was the difference. He said if I\u2019d wanted it to hide a knife in and smuggle it to Jim so he could kill the seneschal, it would have been all right. So I let it go, though I couldn\u2019t see any advantage in pretending to be a prisoner if I had to sit down and chew over a lot of fine distinctions like that every time I saw a chance to grab a watermelon.\\n\\nWell, as I was saying, that morning we waited until everyone had settled down to work and no one was in sight around the yard. Then Tom carried the sack into the lean-to while I stood a little way off to keep watch. After a while he came out, and we went and sat on the woodpile to talk. He said:\\n\\n\u201cEverything\u2019s all right now except the tools; and that\u2019s easy to fix.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTools?\u201d I said.\\n\\n\u201cYes.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTools for what?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, to dig with. We aren\u2019t going to _gnaw_ him out, are we?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAren\u2019t those old crippled picks and things in there good enough to dig a Black man out with?\u201d I said.\\n\\nHe turned on me, looking so pitying he could have made anyone cry, and said:\\n\\n\u201cHuck Finn, have you _ever_ heard of a prisoner having picks and shovels, with all the modern conveniences in his wardrobe to dig himself out with? Now I want to ask you\u2014if you have any sense at all\u2014what kind of chance would _that_ give him to be a hero? Why, they might as well lend him the key and be done with it. Picks and shovels\u2014why, they wouldn\u2019t provide them even to a king.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, then,\u201d I said, \u201cif we don\u2019t want the picks and shovels, what do we want?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cA couple of case knives.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTo dig the foundations out from under that cabin?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDamn it, Tom, that\u2019s foolish.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt doesn\u2019t matter how foolish it is; it\u2019s the _right_ way\u2014and it\u2019s the usual way. And there isn\u2019t any _other_ way that I\u2019ve ever heard of, and I\u2019ve read all the books that give information about these things. They always dig out with a case knife\u2014and not through dirt, mind you; usually it\u2019s through solid rock. And it takes them weeks and weeks and weeks, forever and ever. Why, look at one of those prisoners in the bottom dungeon of the Ch\u00e2teau d\u2019If, in the harbor of Marseilles, who dug himself out that way; how long do you suppose _he_ worked at it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t know.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, guess.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t know. A month and a half.\u201d\"}"
