selves to create a suspicion that should guide all further investigation of the mystery. I said \u2018proper conclusions,\u2019 but that does not fully express my meaning. I mean that these are the only correct conclusions, and that the suspicion follows from them inevitably as their one result. I will not yet say what that suspicion is. I only want you to remember that, for me, it was strong enough to give my inquiries in the chamber a definite direction.\\n\\n\u201cLet us now imagine ourselves in that chamber. What should we look for first? The means by which the murderers escaped. It is safe to say that neither of us believes in supernatural events.\"}"
