          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"c7be3d527054655d6d13d502\",\"rewritten_text\":\"This was Mrs. Umney, the housekeeper, whom Mrs. Otis, at Lady Canterville\u2019s earnest request, had agreed to retain in her old position. She gave each of them a low curtsey as they stepped down, and said in a quaint, old-fashioned way, \u2018I welcome you to Canterville Chase.\u2019 They followed her through the handsome Tudor hall into the library, a long, low chamber panelled in black oak, with a large stained-glass window at the far end. Tea had been prepared for them there, and, after removing their wraps, they sat down and began looking about while Mrs. Umney attended to them.\\n\\nAll at once Mrs. Otis noticed a dull red mark on the floor beside the fireplace and, quite unaware of its true meaning, said to Mrs. Umney, \u2018I fear something has been spilled there.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Yes, madam,\u2019 answered the old housekeeper softly, \u2018blood was spilled in that place.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018How dreadful,\u2019 exclaimed Mrs. Otis; \u2018I really dislike bloodstains in a sitting-room. It must be cleaned away immediately.\u2019\\n\\nThe old woman smiled and replied in the same quiet, mysterious tone, \u2018It is the blood of Lady Eleanore de Canterville, murdered on that very spot by her husband, Sir Simon de Canterville, in 1575. Sir Simon lived nine years beyond her, then vanished suddenly in circumstances of the greatest mystery. His body has never been found, but his guilty ghost still haunts the Chase. Tourists and others have greatly admired the stain, and it cannot be removed.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018That is complete nonsense,\u2019 cried Washington Otis; \u2018Pinkerton\u2019s Champion Stain Remover and Paragon Detergent will take it off in no time.\u2019 Before the frightened housekeeper could stop him, he had dropped to his knees and was vigorously scrubbing the floor with a little stick of what appeared to be black cosmetic. Within moments, not a trace of the bloodstain remained.\\n\\n\u2018I knew Pinkerton would manage it,\u2019 he declared proudly, glancing around at his admiring family. But scarcely had he spoken when a dreadful flash of lightning illuminated the gloomy room, a terrifying crash of thunder sent them all springing to their feet, and Mrs. Umney fainted.\\n\\n\u2018What an outrageous climate!\u2019 said the American Minister calmly, lighting a long cheroot. \u2018I suppose the old country is so crowded that there isn\u2019t enough respectable weather to go around. I have always believed emigration is England\u2019s only solution.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018My dear Hiram,\u2019 cried Mrs. Otis, \u2018what are we to do with a woman who faints?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Put it down as breakage,\u2019 replied the Minister; \u2018she won\u2019t faint again after that.\u2019 And within a few moments Mrs. Umney had indeed recovered.\"}"
