yes glittered and his cheeks reddened with pleasure; at that instant, I thought him as beautiful as the stranger. She seemed moved by other emotions; brushing several tears from her lovely eyes, she extended her hand to Felix, who kissed it passionately and called her, as far as I could make out, his sweet Arabian. She did not seem to understand him, but smiled. He helped her dismount and, sending away her guide, led her into the cottage. He exchanged some words with his father, while the young stranger knelt before the old man and tried to kiss his hand; but he lifted her up and embraced her warmly.\\n\\n\u201cI soon discovered that, although the stranger made articulate sounds and seemed to possess a language of her own, neither she nor the cottagers understood the other.\u201d\"}"
