          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"021945a4091dd36f619d3853\",\"rewritten_text\":\"After dinner, the whole gang went out onto the sandbar to hunt turtle eggs. They poked sticks into the sand, and whenever they found a soft spot, they knelt down and dug with their hands. Sometimes they pulled fifty or sixty eggs from a single hole. The eggs were perfectly round and white, a little smaller than an English walnut. That night they had a grand feast of fried eggs, and another on Friday morning.\\n\\nAfter breakfast, they went whooping and prancing onto the bar. They chased one another in circles, taking off their clothes as they ran, until they were naked. Then they continued their game far up the shallow water, fighting against the strong current. Every so often it knocked their legs out from under them, which made the fun even greater. Sometimes they gathered together and splashed water into one another\u2019s faces with their hands. They slowly moved closer, turning their faces away to avoid the choking sprays, until they grabbed and wrestled. The strongest boy ducked his neighbor, and then they all went under in a tangle of pale arms and legs. They came up blowing, sputtering, laughing, and gasping for breath all at once.\\n\\nWhen they were thoroughly tired, they ran out onto the dry, hot sand, sprawled there, and covered themselves with it. Soon they rushed back into the water and repeated the whole performance. At last they realized that their bare skin looked much like flesh-colored \u201ctights.\u201d They drew a circle in the sand and put on a circus, with three clowns, since none of them would give up that proudest role to another.\\n\\nNext they took out their marbles and played \u201cknucks,\u201d \u201cringtaw,\u201d and \u201ckeeps\u201d until they grew tired of that too. Then Joe and Huck went swimming again, but Tom refused. While kicking off his trousers, he had knocked the string of rattlesnake rattles from his ankle, and he wondered how he had avoided cramps so long without the protection of that mysterious charm. He would not swim again until he found it. By then, the other boys were tired and ready to rest. They slowly drifted apart, sank into the \u201cdumps,\u201d and gazed wistfully across the broad river toward the village, which lay sleeping in the sun. Tom caught himself writing \u201cBECKY\u201d in the sand with his big toe. He rubbed it out and felt angry at his own weakness. But he wrote it again anyway; he could not stop himself. He erased it once more, then escaped the temptation by gathering the other boys together and joining them.\"}"
