ou take their watches and other things, but you always remove your hat and speak politely. Nobody is as polite as robbers\u2014you\u2019ll see that in any book. Then the women fall in love with you, and after they\u2019ve been in the cave for a week or two, they stop crying. After that, you couldn\u2019t make them leave. If you forced them out, they\u2019d turn around and come back. That\u2019s how it happens in all the books.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, it\u2019s really great, Tom. I think it\u2019s better than being a pirate.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, it\u2019s better in some ways, because it\u2019s close to home, circuses, and everything else.\u201d\\n\\nBy then everything was ready, and the boys entered the hole, with Tom leading. They worked their way to the far end of the tunnel, tied their joined kite strings securely, and moved on.\"}"
