e had not; the matter had simply never entered her mind. Thus, without realizing it, she was already forecasting the authentic history of future prisoners in the Castle d\u2019If. It seemed clear to me now that, under her training, those inherited prisoners were merely property\u2014nothing more and nothing less. After all, when we inherit property, we do not think of throwing it away, even if we place no value on it.\\n\\nWhen I led my procession of human bats into the open air and the harsh afternoon sunlight\u2014having first blindfolded them, out of mercy for eyes so long unaccustomed to light\u2014they were a sight to behold. Skeletons, scarecrows, goblins, pitiful horrors, every one of them; the most legitimate children imaginable of Monarchy by the Grace of God and the Established Church.\"}"
