one your raptures until I write again? I have no room at present to do them justice.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, it does not matter. I shall see her in January. But do you always write such charmingly long letters to her, Mr. Darcy?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThey are usually long; but whether they are always charming is not for me to decide.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI believe that anyone who can easily write a long letter cannot write badly.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat is not much of a compliment to Darcy, Caroline,\u201d cried her brother, \u201cbecause he does not write easily. He thinks too hard over four-syllable words. Do you not, Darcy?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy writing style is very different from yours.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh,\u201d cried Miss Bingley, \u201cCharles writes in the most careless way imaginable.\u201d\"}"
