from side to side. He would have fallen if his men had not caught him.\\n\\n\u201cTruly,\u201d said King Arthur, \u201cthat knight of the many colors is a good knight.\u201d The king then called Sir Launcelot to him and asked him to fight that knight. \u201cSir,\u201d said Launcelot, \u201cI can easily find it in my heart to spare him for now, because he has worked hard enough today. When a good knight performs so well in a single day, it is not the part of a good knight to take away his honor, especially after seeing how much labor he has endured. Perhaps,\u201d Sir Launcelot continued, \u201chis cause is here today, and perhaps this lady loves him best of all who are here. I can see that he is straining himself to accomplish great deeds. Therefore, as far as I am concerned, he shall have the honor today. Though I had the power to take it from him, I would not.\u201d\"}"
