{"request_id":"07403c1e04b845e077dae6dd","rewritten_text":"As I passed my hand through the valve, carrying a cup of water for the old cat, my shirt sleeves caught in the loop supporting the basket, and in an instant pulled it loose from the bottom. Had the entire thing truly vanished into thin air, it could not have disappeared from my sight more suddenly. Indeed, scarcely a tenth of a second passed between the basket’s release and its complete, utter disappearance, together with everything inside it. My good wishes went with it toward the earth, though naturally I had no expectation that either cat or kittens would survive to recount their misfortune.

“At six o’clock, I saw a large part of the earth’s visible surface to the east covered in heavy shadow. This shadow advanced with extraordinary speed, until, at five minutes before seven, the entire scene before me lay wrapped in the darkness of night. Yet it was long afterward that the setting sun’s rays stopped shining upon the balloon; and this, though entirely expected, still afforded me immense pleasure. Clearly, in the morning I would see the rising sun at least several hours before the inhabitants of Rotterdam, despite their position much farther east. Thus, day after day, as my altitude increased, I would enjoy sunlight for a progressively longer time. I now resolved to keep a journal of my journey, counting each day as twenty-four continuous hours, without regard to the periods of darkness.

“At ten o’clock, growing drowsy, I decided to lie down for the remainder of the night. But then a problem arose which, obvious as it may seem, had escaped me until that very moment. If I slept as intended, how could the air in the chamber be renewed meanwhile? To breathe it for more than an hour at most would be impossible; and even if that period could be prolonged to an hour and a quarter, the consequences might prove disastrous. This dilemma caused me considerable anxiety; and it may scarcely be believed that, after all the dangers I had endured, I regarded the matter so gravely that I abandoned every hope of fulfilling my ultimate purpose and finally resolved that I must descend. But this uncertainty lasted only an instant."}

