          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"b0e54ecf3faaf2256a80274b\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201c\u2018We have been to your residence,\u2019 said the first, \u2018but were unfortunate enough not to find you there. We were told that you were probably walking this way, so we followed, hoping to catch up with you. Will you please enter the carriage?\u2019\\n\\n\u201cThe manner of both men was commanding, and as they spoke they moved to place me between themselves and the carriage door. They were armed. I was not.\\n\\n\u201c\u2018Gentlemen,\u2019 I said, \u2018forgive me, but I usually ask who has the honour of seeking my help, and what kind of case has brought me here.\u2019\\n\\n\u201cThe second speaker answered. \u2018Doctor, your clients are people of rank. As for the nature of the case, our confidence in your skill assures us that you will discover it more accurately than we could explain it. Enough. Will you please enter the carriage?\u2019\\n\\n\u201cI could do nothing but obey, and entered in silence. They followed me\u2014the last one jumping in after raising the steps. The carriage turned around and continued at its former speed.\\n\\n\u201cI repeat this conversation exactly as it happened. I have no doubt that these are the precise words. I describe everything exactly as it occurred, forcing my mind not to stray from the task. Where I make the broken marks below, I stop for the moment and place my paper in its hiding place.\\n\\n*****\\n\\n\u201cThe carriage left the streets, passed through the North Barrier, and came out onto the country road. About two-thirds of a league beyond the Barrier\u2014I did not measure the distance then, but did so later when I traveled the route\u2014it turned off the main road and soon stopped at a lonely house. All three of us got out and walked along a damp, soft path through a garden where an abandoned fountain had overflowed, to the house door. When the door did not open at once after the bell was rung, one of my two escorts struck the man who opened it across the face with his heavy riding glove.\\n\\n\u201cThis did not especially surprise me, since I had seen ordinary people struck more often than dogs. But the other man, also angry, struck him in the same way with his arm. The brothers\u2019 expressions and manner were then so exactly alike that I realized for the first time that they were twins.\\n\\n\u201cFrom the moment we got out at the outer gate\u2014which was locked, and which one brother opened to let us in before locking it again\u2014I had heard cries coming from an upper room.\"}"
