h, she had claims of many kinds that quickly and permanently recommended her.\\n\\nThe recent services she had performed for Anne would have been sufficient on their own, and their marriage, instead of taking one friend from her, gave her two. She was the first visitor to their established household; and Captain Wentworth, by helping her recover her husband\u2019s property in the West Indies\u2014writing on her behalf, acting for her, and guiding her through every minor difficulty with the energy of a fearless man and a determined friend\u2014fully repaid the services she had rendered, or had ever intended to render, to his wife.\"}"
