s a thin skeleton stretched out on the stone floor. It seemed to be reaching with its long, bare fingers toward an old-fashioned wooden dish and water jug placed just beyond its grasp. The jug had clearly once held water, for its inside was coated with green mold. The dish held nothing but a heap of dust. Virginia knelt beside the skeleton, folded her small hands, and began to pray silently. The others watched in wonder at the terrible tragedy whose secret had finally been revealed.\"}"
