          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"f925527be2be79a38603aa77\",\"rewritten_text\":\"When the wedding took place, about three weeks later, St. Peter\u2019s was packed with a perfect crowd of fashionable people. The Dean of Chichester conducted the service with great solemnity, and everyone agreed that they had never seen a more handsome couple than the bride and groom. They were more than handsome, however\u2014they were happy. Lord Arthur never once regretted all he had suffered for Sybil\u2019s sake, while she, for her part, gave him the finest things a woman can give a man\u2014devotion, tenderness, and love. For them, romance was not destroyed by reality. They always felt young.\\n\\nSeveral years later, after two beautiful children had been born to them, Lady Windermere came to stay at Alton Priory, a lovely old house that had been the Duke\u2019s wedding gift to his son. One afternoon, as she sat with Lady Arthur beneath a lime tree in the garden, watching the little boy and girl play up and down the rose walk like flickering sunbeams, she suddenly took her hostess\u2019s hand and asked, \u2018Are you happy, Sybil?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Dear Lady Windermere, of course I\u2019m happy. Aren\u2019t you?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018I have no time to be happy, Sybil. I always like the last person introduced to me; but usually, as soon as I get to know people, I grow tired of them.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Don\u2019t your lions satisfy you, Lady Windermere?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Oh, no! Lions are only good for one season. Once their manes are cut, they are the dullest creatures alive. Besides, they behave very badly if you are genuinely kind to them. Do you remember that dreadful Mr. Podgers? He was a terrible impostor. Of course, I didn\u2019t mind that at all, and I even forgave him when he wanted to borrow money, but I couldn\u2019t tolerate his making love to me. He has truly made me hate cheiromancy. I\u2019m interested in telepathy now. It\u2019s much more entertaining.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018You mustn\u2019t say anything against cheiromancy here, Lady Windermere; it is the only subject Arthur doesn\u2019t like people to joke about. I assure you, he takes it quite seriously.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018You don\u2019t mean to say he believes in it, Sybil?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Ask him, Lady Windermere\u2014here he is.\u2019 Lord Arthur came up the garden carrying a large bunch of yellow roses, with his two children dancing around him.\\n\\n\u2018Lord Arthur?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Yes, Lady Windermere.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018You don\u2019t mean to say that you believe in cheiromancy?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Of course I do,\u2019 said the young man with a smile.\\n\\n\u2018But why?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Because I owe it all the happiness of my life,\u2019 he murmured, lowering himself into a wicker chair.\"}"
