ways staying until after supper\u2014unless some barbarous neighbour, whom he could not possibly detest enough, had invited him to dinner, an invitation he felt obliged to accept.\\n\\nElizabeth now had little time to speak with her sister, because while Bingley was present Jane had no attention to give anyone else. But during the periods of separation that sometimes had to occur, Elizabeth found herself very useful to them both. When Jane was absent, Bingley always attached himself to Elizabeth for the pleasure of talking about her; and when Bingley had gone, Jane constantly sought the same comfort.\\n\\n\u201cHe has made me so happy,\u201d she said one evening, \u201cby telling me that he had been completely unaware that I was in town last spring!\u201d\"}"
