          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"a6f948e6b01e9839c65adb2d\",\"rewritten_text\":\"According to the latest reports from Rotterdam, that city appears to be in a remarkable state of philosophical agitation. Strange events have taken place there\u2014so wholly unforeseen, so entirely new, so utterly opposed to established opinions\u2014that I cannot doubt all Europe is by now in commotion, physics in turmoil, and reason and astronomy at open war.\\n\\nIt seems that on the\u2014\u2014 day of\u2014\u2014 (the exact date I cannot confidently state), an immense crowd had gathered, for reasons not clearly specified, in the great square of the Exchange in the well-kept city of Rotterdam. The weather was warm\u2014uncommonly warm for the season\u2014and scarcely a breath of wind moved; nor were the people displeased when, from time to time, brief friendly showers descended from broad white clouds that passed fitfully across the blue firmament. Yet around noon a slight but extraordinary disturbance arose among them: ten thousand voices began clattering; and immediately afterward ten thousand faces turned upward, ten thousand pipes dropped together from the corners of ten thousand mouths, and a cry, comparable to nothing except the roar of Niagara, rolled long, loudly, and furiously through the whole neighborhood of Rotterdam.\\n\\nThe cause of this uproar soon became plain enough. From behind the enormous mass of one of the sharply outlined clouds already mentioned, there slowly appeared in an open patch of blue a strange, confused, yet seemingly solid object, so oddly formed and so whimsically assembled that the sturdy burghers below could neither understand it nor admire it sufficiently. What could it be? By all the vrows and devils in Rotterdam, what could it possibly signify? Nobody knew, nobody could guess; nobody\u2014not even the burgomaster, Mynheer Superbus Von Underduk\u2014possessed the least clue for solving the mystery. Thus, since nothing more sensible suggested itself, every man carefully put his pipe back into the corner of his mouth, raised his right eye toward the apparition, puffed, paused, waddled about, and grunted meaningfully\u2014then waddled back, grunted, paused, and at last\u2014puffed once more.\\n\\nMeanwhile, the object that had aroused such curiosity and produced so much smoke descended lower and lower toward the pleasant city. Within a few minutes it had come near enough to be clearly examined. It seemed to be\u2014yes! it was certainly a kind of balloon; but surely Rotterdam had never before witnessed such a balloon.\"}"
