          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"d6e8a480e9fd2942625c11e0\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cNever!\u201d the girl replied.\\n\\n\u201cTell me why?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cFor one reason,\u201d the girl answered firmly, \u201cbecause the lady knows about it and will stand by me\u2014I know she will, for I have her promise. And for this other reason too: bad a life as he has led, I have led a bad life as well. Many of us have followed the same path together, and I will not turn against them. Any of them might have turned against me, but they did not, bad as they are.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen,\u201d said the gentleman quickly, as if this were the point he had been trying to reach, \u201cput Monks in my hands and leave me to deal with him.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat if he turns against the others?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI promise you that, if he does, and the truth is forced from him, the matter will end there. There must be parts of Oliver\u2019s short history that would be painful to reveal publicly. If the truth is brought out, the others shall go free.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd if it is not?\u201d the girl asked.\\n\\n\u201cThen,\u201d continued the gentleman, \u201cthis Fagin shall not be brought to justice without your consent. In that case, I think I could show you reasons that would persuade you to give it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDo I have the lady\u2019s promise for that?\u201d asked the girl.\\n\\n\u201cYou do,\u201d Rose replied. \u201cYou have my true and faithful pledge.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMonks would never discover how you learned what you know?\u201d the girl asked after a short pause.\\n\\n\u201cNever,\u201d replied the gentleman. \u201cThe information would be used against him in such a way that he could never even guess its source.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have been a liar, and lived among liars, since I was a little child,\u201d said the girl after another silence, \u201cbut I will trust your word.\u201d\\n\\nAfter both assured her that she could safely do so, she began speaking so quietly that the listener often found it difficult to understand even the meaning of her words. She described, by name and location, the public house from which she had been followed that night. From the way she sometimes paused, it seemed that the gentleman was quickly writing down the information she gave him. When she had fully explained the place, the best position from which to watch it without being noticed, and the night and hour when Monks most often visited it, she paused for a few moments, trying to bring his face and appearance clearly back to mind.\\n\\n\u201cHe is tall,\u201d said the girl, \u201cand strongly built, but not fat. He walks in a secretive way, and as he walks he constantly looks over his shoulder, first to one side and then to the other.\u201d\"}"
