          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"36edc8b769b1877370f96a43\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cBut,\u201d said I, handing the slip back to him, \u201cI am no less confused than before. Even if all the jewels of Golconda were promised to me for solving this riddle, I am certain I could not earn them.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd yet,\u201d said Legrand, \u201cthe solution is not nearly as difficult as a first hurried look at the symbols might lead you to think. As anyone might guess, these symbols form a cipher\u2014that is, they carry a meaning. But, knowing what I did of Kidd, I could not imagine him capable of creating one of the more complicated cryptographs. I immediately decided that it was a simple kind, though one that would seem completely impossible to the sailor\u2019s rough mind without the key.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd you actually solved it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cEasily. I have solved others ten thousand times more difficult. Circumstances, along with a certain tendency in my mind, have made me interested in such puzzles, and it may well be that human ingenuity cannot create a riddle that human ingenuity cannot solve with proper effort. In fact, once I had found a sequence of connected, readable symbols, I hardly thought about the difficulty of discovering their meaning.\\n\\n\u201cIn this case\u2014as in every case of secret writing\u2014the first question concerns the cipher\u2019s language. The methods of solving it, especially in the simpler ciphers, depend on and change with the nature of the particular language. Usually, the solver has no choice but to test every language he knows, guided by probability, until he finds the right one. But with the cipher before us, the signature removed all difficulty. The pun on the word \u2018Kidd\u2019 works in no language except English. Without that clue, I would have begun with Spanish and French, the languages in which a pirate of the Spanish Main would most naturally have written such a secret. As it was, I assumed the cryptograph was English.\\n\\n\u201cYou will notice that there are no spaces between the words. If there had been spaces, the task would have been fairly easy. I would then have begun by comparing and studying the shorter words. If a one-letter word had appeared, as would most likely happen\u2014\u2018a\u2019 or \u2018I,\u2019 for example\u2014I would have considered the solution certain. But since there were no spaces, my first step was to identify the most common letters, as well as the rarest ones.\u201d\"}"
