          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"eb3b038d737c0037f86cfeb4\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cAnd so I\u2019m owner of a few knights,\u201d said I, as we rode away. \u201cWho would ever have thought I should live to enter assets of that kind. I shan\u2019t know what to do with them, unless I raffle them off. How many are there, Sandy?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSeven, if you please, sir, with their squires.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s a handsome haul. Who are they? Where do they hang out?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhere do they hang out?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, where do they live?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAh, I understood thee not. That will I tell thee presently.\u201d Then she said thoughtfully and softly, turning the words delicately upon her tongue: \u201cHang they out\u2014hang they out\u2014where hang\u2014where do they hang out; eh, even so; where do they hang out. Truly the phrase hath a pleasant and winning grace, and is prettily fashioned besides. I will repeat it anon and anon in mine idleness, whereby I may perhaps learn it. Where do they hang out. Even so! already it trips readily from my tongue, and inasmuch as\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t forget the cowboys, Sandy.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCowboys?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes; the knights, you know. You were going to tell me about them. You remember, a while ago. Figuratively speaking, the game\u2019s called.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGame\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, yes, yes! Go to bat. I mean, get to work on your statistics, and don\u2019t use so much kindling getting your fire going. Tell me about the knights.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI will indeed, and shall begin lightly. So they two departed and rode into a great forest. And\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGreat Scott!\u201d\\n\\nYou see, I knew my mistake immediately. I had set her machinery in motion; it was my own fault, and she would take thirty days to reach those facts. She usually began without a preface and ended without a conclusion. If you interrupted her, she would either continue without noticing, or answer in a few words and then return to repeat the sentence. Thus interruptions only made matters worse; yet I had to interrupt, and often, too, to preserve my life. A man would die if he allowed her monotony to drip over him all day long.\\n\\n\u201cGreat Scott!\u201d I said in my distress. She went straight back and began again:\\n\\n\u201cSo they two departed and rode into a great forest. And\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201c_Which_ two?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSir Gawaine and Sir Uwaine. And so they came to an abbey of monks, where they were well lodged. On the morrow they heard their masses in the abbey, and then rode forth until they came to a great forest; there Sir Gawaine became aware, in a valley by a turret, of twelve fair damsels and two knights armed upon great horses, while the damsels went to and fro beside a tree.\u201d\"}"
