          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"7e353f95834ab7c8589cb38f\",\"rewritten_text\":\"At the stairs where we had taken him aboard, and ever since, I had watched carefully for any sign that we were suspected. I had seen none. We certainly had not been followed then, and no boat was following us now. If any boat had been waiting for us, I would have turned toward shore and forced her either to continue on or to show her purpose. But we continued without any sign of interference.\\n\\nHe wore his boat-cloak and looked, as I have said, like a natural part of the scene. It was remarkable\u2014though perhaps the miserable life he had led explained it\u2014that he was the least anxious of us all. He was not indifferent. He told me he hoped to live to see his gentleman become one of the finest gentlemen in a foreign country. Nor, as I understood him, was he willing simply to submit or give up. But he had no intention of going out to meet danger. When danger came to him, he faced it; until then, he would not trouble himself about it.\\n\\n\u201cIf you knowed, dear boy,\u201d he said to me, \u201cwhat it is to sit here alonger my dear boy and have my smoke, arter being day by day betwixt four walls, you\u2019d envy me. But you don\u2019t know what it is.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI think I know the pleasures of freedom,\u201d I answered.\\n\\n\u201cAh,\u201d he said, shaking his head seriously. \u201cBut you don\u2019t know it equal to me. You must have been under lock and key, dear boy, to know it equal to me\u2014but I ain\u2019t a-going to be low.\u201d\\n\\nIt seemed inconsistent to me that, for any ruling idea, he should have risked his freedom and even his life. But I reflected that freedom without danger might be so unlike everything he had known that it could not mean to him what it would mean to another man. I was not far wrong, for after smoking a little he said:\\n\\n\u201cYou see, dear boy, when I was over yonder, t\u2019other side the world, I was always looking toward this side; and it got flat to be there, though I was growing rich. Everybody knowed Magwitch, and Magwitch could come and go, and nobody\u2019s head would be troubled about him. They ain\u2019t so easy concerning me here, dear boy\u2014wouldn\u2019t be, leastwise, if they knowed where I was.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIf all goes well,\u201d I said, \u201cyou will be perfectly free and safe again within a few hours.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell,\u201d he replied, drawing a long breath, \u201cI hope so.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd think so?\u201d\"}"
