          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"3ab162cf99f4364ce3b1b89e\",\"rewritten_text\":\"She studied me closely for a while, then said quietly,\\n\\n\u201cWhat do you want for them?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOnly,\u201d I replied, \u201cthat you would not treat them as you do the others. They may share the same blood, but believe me, they are not the same in nature.\u201d\\n\\nStill watching me closely, Miss Havisham repeated,\\n\\n\u201cWhat do you want for them?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou see, I am not clever enough,\u201d I said, aware that I was beginning to blush, \u201cto hide from you, even if I wished to, that I do want something. Miss Havisham, if you would spend the money to give my friend Herbert lasting help in life\u2014help that, because of the circumstances, must be given without his knowing\u2014I could show you how.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy must it be done without his knowledge?\u201d she asked, resting both hands on her stick so she could study me more closely.\\n\\n\u201cBecause,\u201d I said, \u201cI began helping him myself more than two years ago, without his knowledge, and I do not want to be exposed. I cannot explain why I am unable to finish what I began. That is part of a secret belonging to someone else, not to me.\u201d\\n\\nShe slowly turned her eyes away from me and fixed them on the fire. She watched it for what seemed, in the silence and the light of the slowly burning-down candles, a long time. Then the collapse of some red coals brought her back, and she looked at me again\u2014first blankly, then with steadily growing attention. Throughout this, Estella continued knitting. When Miss Havisham had focused on me, she spoke as though our conversation had not been interrupted:\\n\\n\u201cWhat else?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cEstella,\u201d I said, turning to her and trying to control my trembling voice, \u201cyou know that I love you. You know I have loved you for a long time, and deeply.\u201d\\n\\nHearing herself addressed, she lifted her eyes to my face. Her fingers