          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"b55356efe64665bb33375b4b\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cJoseph!! Joseph!!!\u201d He shook his head and tapped it, showing how little he thought of Joseph.\\n\\n\u201cBut my dear young friend,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook, \u201cyou must be hungry and exhausted. Sit down. Here is a chicken from the Boar, here is a tongue from the Boar, and here are one or two little things from the Boar, which I hope you will not despise. But do I,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook, rising again the moment after sitting down, \u201csee before me the boy I once played with in his happy infancy? And may I\u2014_may_ I\u2014?\u201d\\n\\nBy this, he meant to ask whether he might shake hands. I agreed, and he did so warmly before sitting down again.\\n\\n\u201cHere is wine,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook. \u201cLet us drink: Thanks to Fortune, and may she always choose her favourites with equal judgment! And yet I cannot,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook, rising again, \u201csee before me One\u2014and drink to One\u2014without once more expressing\u2014May I\u2014_may_ I\u2014?\u201d\\n\\nI said he might. He shook hands with me again, emptied his glass, and turned it upside down. I did the same; and if I had turned myself upside down before drinking, the wine could not have gone more quickly to my head.\\n\\nMr. Pumblechook helped me to the liver wing and the best slice of tongue\u2014none of those remote Pork No Thoroughfares now\u2014and took almost no care of himself. \u201cAh! Poultry, poultry! You little knew,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook, addressing the fowl on the dish, \u201cwhen you were a young fledgling, what was waiting for you. You little knew you were to provide refreshment beneath this humble roof for one who\u2014Call it weakness, if you like,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook, rising again, \u201cbut may I? _may_ I\u2014?\u201d\\n\\nIt was no longer necessary to repeat that he might, so he did it at once. How he managed to do it so often without cutting himself on my knife, I do not know.\\n\\n\u201cAnd your sister,\u201d he continued after eating steadily for a while, \u201cwho had the honour of raising you by hand! It is sad to think that she is no longer able to understand that honour fully. May\u2014\u201d\\n\\nI saw he was about to come at me again, and stopped him.\\n\\n\u201cWe\u2019ll drink her health,\u201d I said.\\n\\n\u201cAh!\u201d cried Mr. Pumblechook, leaning back in his chair, limp with admiration, \u201cthat\u2019s how you recognize them, sir!\u201d (I do not know who Sir was, but he certainly was not me, and no third person was present); \u201cthat\u2019s how you recognize the noble-minded, sir!\u201d\"}"
