          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"13c0f7c5d54c3995e5527d04\",\"rewritten_text\":\"The following day he did not go out, but spent nearly all his time in his own room, stricken by a frantic fear of death, while remaining careless of life itself. The sense of being pursued, trapped, and hunted down had begun to master him. If the tapestry merely stirred in the breeze, he trembled. The dead leaves blown against the leaded windows appeared to him as his own squandered resolutions and reckless regrets. Whenever he shut his eyes, he saw once more the sailor\u2019s face looking through the mist-marked glass, and horror seemed again to press its hand upon his heart.\\n\\nYet perhaps it was only his imagination that had summoned vengeance from the darkness and placed those loathsome forms of punishment before him. Real life was chaotic, but imagination possessed a dreadful logic. It was imagination that made remorse follow sin\u2019s footsteps. It was imagination that caused every crime to produce its deformed offspring. In the ordinary world of fact, the wicked went unpunished and the good unrewarded. Success belonged to the strong, while failure was forced upon the weak. That was all. Moreover, if some stranger had been creeping around the house, the servants or keepers would have noticed him. If footprints had appeared in the flower-beds, the gardeners would have mentioned them. Yes, it had been nothing but fancy. Sibyl Vane\u2019s brother had not returned to murder him. He had sailed away aboard his ship, only to founder in some winter sea. From him, at least, he was secure. Why, the man did not know who he was, and could not possibly know. The mask of youth had protected him.\\n\\nAnd still, if it had been only an illusion, how dreadful to think that conscience could summon such terrifying phantoms, give them visible bodies, and make them move before one! What kind of existence would his be if, by day and night, the shadows of his crime peered at him from quiet corners, mocked him from hidden places, whispered in his ear while he sat at the feast, and woke him with icy fingers as he slept! As the thought passed through his mind, terror drained the color from his face, and the air seemed suddenly to grow colder. Oh, in what mad and terrible hour he had killed his friend! How horrible even the memory of that scene! He saw everything again. Every dreadful detail returned with increased horror. From time\u2019s black cavern, terrible and wrapped in scarlet, rose the image of his sin.\"}"
        }
