s of laughter.\\n\\n\u2018Economy is an excellent thing,\u2019 remarked the Duchess complacently; \u2018when I married Paisley he possessed eleven castles, and not one house fit for habitation.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018And now he has twelve houses, and not one castle,\u2019 cried Lady Windermere.\\n\\n\u2018Well, my dear,\u2019 said the Duchess, \u2018I like\u2014\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Comfort,\u2019 said Mr. Podgers, \u2018and modern conveniences, and hot water supplied to every bedroom. Your Grace is quite right. Comfort is the sole thing our civilisation can provide us.\\n\\n\u2018You have described the Duchess\u2019s character admirably, Mr. Podgers, and now you must read Lady Flora\u2019s\u2019; and at a nod from the smiling hostess, a tall girl, with sandy Scotch hair and prominent shoulder-blades, stepped awkwardly from behind the sofa and extended a long, bony hand with spatulate fingers.\\n\\n\u2018Ah, a pianist! I see,\u2019 said Mr. Podgers, \u2018an excellent pianist, though perhaps scarcely a musician.\u2019\"}"
