ese children of sin and misery destined for their fate, just as he was destined for his? Were they, like him, only puppets in some monstrous show?\\n\\nYet it was not the mystery of suffering that struck him, but its comedy: its complete uselessness and absurd lack of meaning. How confused everything seemed! How little harmony there was in the world! He was astonished by the contrast between the shallow optimism of the age and the real facts of life. He was still very young.\\n\\nAfter some time, he found himself standing before Marylebone Church. The silent road looked like a long ribbon of polished silver, marked here and there by the dark, twisting patterns of moving shadows.\"}"
