e poisonous dew, and his fat fingers became cold and clammy.\\n\\nLord Arthur noticed these strange signs of distress, and for the first time in his life, he felt afraid. His first impulse was to run from the room, but he held himself back. It was better to know the worst, whatever it might be, than to remain in this terrible uncertainty.\\n\\n\u2018I am waiting, Mr. Podgers,\u2019 he said.\\n\\n\u2018We are all waiting,\u2019 cried Lady Windermere in her quick, impatient manner, but the palm reader made no answer.\\n\\n\u2018I believe Arthur is going on the stage,\u2019 said Lady Jedburgh, \u2018and that after your scolding, Mr. Podgers is afraid to tell him so.\u2019\"}"
