          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"abdb5070f69823ea6bb4e6d7\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cAnd so I\u2019m the owner of some knights,\u201d I said as we rode away. \u201cWho would ever have thought I\u2019d live to list assets like that? I won\u2019t know what to do with them, unless I raffle them off. How many are there, Sandy?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSeven, if you please, sir, and their squires.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s a good haul. Who are they? Where do they hang out?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhere do they hang out?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, where do they live?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAh, I did not understand you. I shall tell you at once.\u201d Then she said thoughtfully and softly, turning the words carefully over in her mouth: \u201cHang they out\u2014hang they out\u2014where hang\u2014where do they hang out; yes, that is it; where do they hang out. Truly, the phrase has a pleasant and charming grace, and is nicely worded too. I will repeat it again and again in my spare time, so that perhaps I may learn it. Where do they hang out. Just so! Already it comes easily from my tongue, and since\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t forget the cowboys, Sandy.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCowboys?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes; the knights, you know. You were going to tell me about them. You remember, a while ago. Figuratively speaking, the game has begun.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGame\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, yes, yes! Go to bat. I mean, get to work on your statistics, and don\u2019t waste so much kindling getting your fire started. Tell me about the knights.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI will, and I shall begin at once. So the two of them left and rode into a great forest. And\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGreat Scott!\u201d\\n\\nYou see, I realized my mistake immediately. I had started her going; it was my own fault, and she would take thirty days to reach those facts. She usually began without an introduction and ended without a conclusion. If you interrupted her, she either continued without noticing or answered in a few words and then went back to repeat the sentence. So interruptions only made things worse; yet I had to interrupt, and often, to save my life. Anyone would die if he let her monotony drip over him all day.\\n\\n\u201cGreat Scott!\u201d I said in distress. She simply went back and began again:\\n\\n\u201cSo the two of them left and rode into a great forest. And\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhich two?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSir Gawaine and Sir Uwaine. And so they came to an abbey of monks, where they were well lodged. In the morning they heard mass in the abbey, and then rode on until they came to a great forest. There Sir Gawaine saw, in a valley beside a turret, twelve fair damsels and two knights armed and mounted on great horses, while the damsels moved back and forth by a tree.\u201d\"}"
