          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"64d6598a468939b494b793a0\",\"rewritten_text\":\"After I had sent them in, I could not stay away from the places where they were, and I felt that they were more hopeful and less desperate when I was near. In this unreasonable restlessness and distress, I would wander the streets in the evening, passing the offices and houses where I had left the petitions. Even now, the tired western streets of London on a cold, dusty spring night, with their rows of stern, closed mansions and long lines of lamps, seem melancholy to me because of this connection.\\n\\nThe daily visits I was allowed to make him were shorter now, and he was watched more closely. Thinking, or imagining, that I was suspected of planning to bring him poison, I asked to be searched before sitting beside his bed. I told the officer who was always there that I was willing to do anything to prove that my intentions were sincere. No one was harsh with either of us. There was a duty to perform, and it was performed, but not cruelly. The officer always assured me that he was worse, and some of the other sick prisoners in the room, along with prisoners who cared for them as nurses\u2014criminals, but thankfully not without kindness\u2014always gave me the same report.\\n\\nAs the days passed, I noticed more and more that he would lie calmly staring at the white ceiling, with no light in his face until one of my words brightened it for a moment; then the light would fade again. Sometimes he was almost, or completely, unable to speak. Then he would answer me by gently pressing my hand, and I came to understand him very well.\\n\\nThe days had reached ten when I saw a greater change in him than ever before. His eyes were turned toward the door, and they brightened when I entered.\\n\\n\u201cDear boy,\u201d he said as I sat beside his bed, \u201cI thought you was late. But I knowed you couldn\u2019t be.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt is exactly the right time,\u201d I said. \u201cI waited for it at the gate.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou always waits at the gate; don\u2019t you, dear boy?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes. So I won\u2019t lose a moment of the time.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThank\u2019ee, dear boy, thank\u2019ee. God bless you! You\u2019ve never deserted me, dear boy.\u201d\\n\\nI pressed his hand in silence, for I could not forget that I had once intended to desert him.\\n\\n\u201cAnd the best thing of all,\u201d he said, \u201cyou\u2019ve been more comfortable alonger me since I was under a dark cloud than when the sun shone.\u201d\"}"
