          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"72b06a25ea70f49639050653\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Biddy wept; the garden growing dark, the lane, and the emerging stars all swam before my eyes.\\n\\n\u201cWas nothing ever found out, Biddy?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNothing.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDo you know what has become of Orlick?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cJudging by the colour of his clothes, I should say he is working in the quarries.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen you have seen him, of course?\u2014Why are you looking at that dark tree in the lane?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI saw him there on the night she died.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat was not the last time, Biddy?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo; I have seen him there since we began walking here.\u2014There is no use,\u201d said Biddy, putting her hand on my arm as I was about to rush out, \u201cyou know I would not deceive you; he was there less than a minute, and then he was gone.\u201d\\n\\nMy indignation was renewed by discovering that this man still haunted her, and I felt an enduring hatred for him. I told her so, and said I would spend whatever money or endure whatever trouble was necessary to drive him from that country. Gradually she drew me into calmer conversation, and told me how Joe loved me, and how Joe never complained of anything\u2014not, she did not say, of me; there was no need, for I understood her meaning\u2014but always performed his duty in his station, with a firm hand, a quiet tongue, and a tender heart.\\n\\n\u201cIndeed, it would be difficult to say too much in his praise,\u201d I said; \u201cand Biddy, we must often talk of these matters, since naturally I shall be coming down here frequently now. I am not going to leave poor Joe by himself.\u201d\\n\\nBiddy did not say a word.\\n\\n\u201cBiddy, don\u2019t you hear me?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, Mr. Pip.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cLeaving aside your calling me Mr. Pip\u2014which seems to me in poor taste, Biddy\u2014what do you mean?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat do I mean?\u201d Biddy asked timidly.\\n\\n\u201cBiddy,\u201d I said, with a self-righteous air of assertion, \u201cI must ask you to explain what you mean by this.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBy this?\u201d said Biddy.\\n\\n\u201cNow, don\u2019t repeat my words,\u201d I answered. \u201cYou never used to echo, Biddy.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNever used to!\u201d said Biddy. \u201cOh, Mr. Pip! Never used to!\u201d\\n\\nWell, I rather thought I would abandon that point as well. After another quiet circuit of the garden, I returned to my principal argument.\\n\\n\u201cBiddy,\u201d I said, \u201cI remarked that I intended to come down here often to see Joe, and you answered with conspicuous silence. Be so good, Biddy, as to tell me why.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAre you quite certain, then, that you WILL come to see him often?\u201d Biddy asked, stopping on the narrow garden path and looking at me beneath the stars with a frank and truthful eye.\"}"
