other\u2019s spirit passed into your body, and you ought to be Diana to me. With every attempt to cast it away, this love fastens itself more tightly, this guilty love, more unnatural than hatred, which withers your hopes and destroys me forever.\\n\\nBetter have loved despair, & safer kissed her.\\n\\nNo time or distance can tear from my soul what has become part of it. Since arriving here I have not for one instant ceased to feel the hell of passion implanted within me, burning until everything is cold, rigid, and dead.\u201d\"}"
