          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"8cd295bfdf37f60891481bbc\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cI now come quickly to the most moving part of my story. I shall describe events that filled me with feelings which, changing me from what I had been, made me what I am.\\n\\n\u201cSpring came on quickly; the weather grew pleasant, and the skies were clear. I was amazed that the land which had once seemed barren and gloomy could now be covered with beautiful flowers and green plants. My senses were delighted and refreshed by countless pleasant scents and lovely sights.\\n\\n\u201cIt was on one of these days, when my cottagers were taking their regular rest from work\u2014the old man playing his guitar while the children listened\u2014that I noticed Felix looked deeply sad. He sighed often. Once, his father stopped playing, and from his manner I guessed that he asked his son why he was unhappy. Felix answered cheerfully, and the old man was beginning to play again when someone knocked at the door.\\n\\n\u201cIt was a lady on horseback, accompanied by a countryman acting as her guide. She wore a dark riding suit and a thick black veil. Agatha asked her a question, but the stranger answered only by saying, in a sweet voice, the name Felix. Her voice was musical, but unlike either of my friends\u2019 voices. At hearing his name, Felix hurried toward her. When she saw him, she lifted her veil, and I saw a face of angelic beauty and expression. Her hair was shining raven-black and carefully braided; her eyes were dark but gentle and lively; her features were perfectly formed, and her remarkably fair complexion was touched with a lovely pink in each cheek.\\n\\n\u201cFelix seemed overwhelmed with joy when he saw her. All his sadness disappeared, and his face immediately showed such ecstatic happiness that I could hardly believe it possible. His eyes sparkled, and pleasure colored his cheeks. At that moment, I thought him as beautiful as the stranger. She seemed moved by other feelings