n a back he recognized through the powerful sympathy of love. Beside that figure was the only empty place on the girls\u2019 side of the schoolhouse. He immediately said:\\n\\n\u201c_I stopped to talk with Huckleberry Finn!_\u201d\\n\\nThe master\u2019s pulse seemed to stop, and he stared helplessly. The hum of study ended. The pupils wondered whether this reckless boy had lost his mind. The master said:\\n\\n\u201cYou\u2014you did what?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cStopped to talk with Huckleberry Finn.\u201d\\n\\nThere was no misunderstanding the words.\\n\\n\u201cThomas Sawyer, this is the most astonishing confession I have ever heard. A simple whipping will not be enough for this offense. Take off your jacket.\u201d\\n\\nThe master\u2019s arm kept moving until it was tired, and the supply of switches had been greatly reduced. Then came the order:\\n\\n\u201cNow, sir, go and sit with the girls! And let this be a warning to you.\u201d\\n\\nThe laughter that moved around the room seemed to embarrass the boy, but in truth he was affected more by his deep awe of his unknown idol and by the thrilling pleasure of his great good fortune.\"}"
