          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"17a6188b8b0633a7991daef4\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Sydney Carton halted in the street, still uncertain where to go. \u201cAt Tellson\u2019s banking-house at nine,\u201d he said thoughtfully. \u201cWould it be wise, meanwhile, to show myself? I think so. It is best that these people should know there is such a man as I here; it is a prudent precaution, and may be a needful preparation. But care, care, care! Let me reason it out!\u201d\\n\\nChecking the steps that had begun to carry him towards a purpose, he turned once or twice through the street, now growing dark, and followed the thought in his mind to its possible results. His first impression was strengthened. \u201cIt is best,\u201d he said at last, having made up his mind, \u201cthat these people should know there is such a man as I here.\u201d And he turned towards Saint Antoine.\\n\\nDefarge had that day described himself as the keeper of a wine-shop in the suburb of Saint Antoine. Anyone well acquainted with the city could find his house without making inquiries. Having learned where it stood, Carton came out again from the narrower streets, dined at a place of refreshment, and fell into a deep sleep after dinner. For the first time in many years, he took no strong drink. Since the previous night he had consumed nothing but a little light, thin wine, and on that night he had let the brandy trickle slowly onto Mr. Lorry\u2019s hearth, like a man who had finished with it.\\n\\nIt was as late as seven o\u2019clock when he awoke refreshed and went out once more into the streets. As he proceeded towards Saint Antoine, he paused at a shop-window containing a mirror, and slightly rearranged his loose cravat, his coat-collar, and his wild hair. This done, he went straight to Defarge\u2019s and entered.\\n\\nThere was, by chance, no customer in the shop except Jacques Three, with the restless fingers and croaking voice. This man, whom he had seen on the Jury, stood drinking at the little counter and talking with the Defarges, husband and wife. The Vengeance joined in the conversation like a regular member of the establishment.\\n\\nWhen Carton came in, sat down, and asked, in very indifferent French, for a small measure of wine, Madame Defarge gave him a careless glance, then a sharper one, and then another sharper still, before approaching him herself to ask what he had ordered.\\n\\nHe repeated his request.\\n\\n\u201cEnglish?\u201d asked Madame Defarge, raising her dark eyebrows with curiosity.\\n\\nAfter looking at her as though even the sound of a single French word took time to reach him, he replied in the same pronounced foreign accent.\"}"
