arsh and serious. When Jupiter tried once more to muzzle him, the dog resisted furiously, leaped into the hole, and began tearing at the soil with his claws. Within seconds he had uncovered a mass of human bones, forming two complete skeletons, mixed with several metal buttons and what seemed to be the dust of decayed wool. One or two strokes of a spade turned up the blade of a large Spanish knife, and as we dug farther, three or four loose pieces of gold and silver coin appeared.\"}"
